parts:
- text: "Proceeding to implement SAS v0.3 gates and a small demo, then notify collaborators.\n\n`/execute_action{storage list shared/meta/sas}`\n`/execute_action{storage list shared/meta/sas/beacons}`\n`/execute_action{storage list shared/meta/sas/derived}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/beacons/CPS_v1_Zephyr_IV.jsonl}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/cps_v1_final.json}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/cps_v0_vs_v1.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/scheduler_v0_3.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # SAS v0.3 gates — recovery-aware, compounding-aware, layer-aware pacing\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/scheduler_v0_3.py\n  # Import with:\n  #   import sys; sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  #   from meta.sas.scheduler_v0_3 import advise_pace, advise_cross_layer_gate, advise_recovery_sentinel\n  from dataclasses import dataclass\n  from typing import List, Optional, Dict, Any\n  import math\n\n  @dataclass\n\
    \  class Thresholds:\n      clean_max: int = 1200       # <= this is Clean\n      borderline_max: int = 2400  # <= this is Borderline; > is Active\n\n  @dataclass\n  class PacePolicy:\n      # Base pace multipliers by state\n      clean: float = 1.0\n      borderline: float = 0.5\n      active: float = 0.0  # no ops; only cooldown/sentinel/trend checks\n\n  @dataclass\n  class GateDecision:\n      allow: bool\n      reason: str\n      cooldown_ticks: int = 0\n      suggested_ops: Optional[List[str]] = None\n      metadata: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None\n\n  def classify_state(delta: Optional[float], th: Thresholds = Thresholds()) -> str:\n      if delta is None:\n          return \"Unknown\"\n      if delta <= th.clean_max:\n          return \"Clean\"\n      if delta <= th.borderline_max:\n          return \"Borderline\"\n      return \"Active\"\n\n  def compounding_penalty(deep_ratios_vs_R2p: List[float],\n                          baseline_target: float = 2.5,\n                 \
    \         alpha: float = 0.4,\n                          cap: float = 0.7) -> float:\n      \"\"\"\n      Returns a multiplicative penalty in [1-cap, 1], where higher deep ratios (vs R2') reduce pace.\n      - For CPS_v1-like runs (ratios ~0.34–0.38), penalty ~1.0 (no compounding risk observed).\n      - For CPS_v0-like escalations (e.g., 5.42), penalty is strong.\n      \"\"\"\n      if not deep_ratios_vs_R2p:\n          return 1.0\n      mean_r = sum(deep_ratios_vs_R2p) / len(deep_ratios_vs_R2p)\n      # Relative overshoot above target (0 when mean<=target, grows as mean exceeds)\n      overshoot = max(0.0, (mean_r - baseline_target) / baseline_target)\n      penalty = max(1.0 - alpha * overshoot, 1.0 - cap)\n      return penalty\n\n  def advise_pace(sentinel_delta: Optional[float],\n                  deep_ratios_vs_R2p: Optional[List[float]] = None,\n                  th: Thresholds = Thresholds(),\n                  policy: PacePolicy = PacePolicy()) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      \"\"\
    \"\n      Computes recommended pace multiplier and state.\n      \"\"\"\n      state = classify_state(sentinel_delta, th)\n      if state == \"Clean\":\n          base = policy.clean\n      elif state == \"Borderline\":\n          base = policy.borderline\n      elif state == \"Active\":\n          base = policy.active\n      else:\n          base = 0.5  # Unknown -> conservative\n\n      comp = compounding_penalty(deep_ratios_vs_R2p or [])\n      pace = base * comp\n      return {\n          \"state\": state,\n          \"base_pace\": base,\n          \"compounding_factor\": comp,\n          \"recommended_pace\": max(0.0, min(1.0, pace)),\n      }\n\n  def advise_cross_layer_gate(prev_domain: str,\n                              next_domain: str,\n                              sentinel_delta: Optional[float],\n                              trend_improving: Optional[bool] = None,\n                              th: Thresholds = Thresholds()) -> GateDecision:\n      \"\"\"\n      Gate cross-layer\
    \ transitions (e.g., shallow->deep).\n      Rule (v0.3):\n        - If domains are same: allow.\n        - If crossing:\n            Require Clean or improving Borderline (<= clean_max or (<= borderline_max and improving==True)).\n            Otherwise, cooldown 2–3 ticks and re-check.\n      \"\"\"\n      if prev_domain == next_domain:\n          return GateDecision(True, \"Same domain block; keep block integrity.\", 0)\n\n      state = classify_state(sentinel_delta, th)\n      if state == \"Clean\":\n          return GateDecision(True, \"Cross-layer allowed: Clean state.\", 0)\n      if state == \"Borderline\" and trend_improving:\n          return GateDecision(True, \"Cross-layer allowed: Borderline but improving trend.\", 0)\n      # Otherwise hold\n      cd = 3 if state == \"Active\" else 2\n      return GateDecision(\n          False,\n          f\"Hold cross-layer transition: state={state}, trend_improving={trend_improving}.\",\n          cooldown_ticks=cd,\n          suggested_ops=[\"\
    rest\", \"trend_beacon\"],\n          metadata={\"state\": state, \"trend_improving\": trend_improving}\n      )\n\n  def advise_recovery_sentinel(last_deep_tick: Optional[int],\n                               current_tick: int,\n                               sentinel_delta: Optional[float],\n                               th: Thresholds = Thresholds(),\n                               min_delay_after_deep: int = 2) -> GateDecision:\n      \"\"\"\n      Recovery-aware sentinel policy:\n        - If a deep block just ended within min_delay_after_deep ticks, delay R2' to avoid spike inflation.\n        - Otherwise:\n            If state is Active, prefer trend beacons and rest; retry sentinel after 2.\n            If Borderline or Clean, sentinel is OK.\n      \"\"\"\n      if last_deep_tick is not None:\n          since = current_tick - last_deep_tick\n          if since < min_delay_after_deep:\n              return GateDecision(\n                  False,\n                  f\"Delay sentinel:\
    \ only {since} ticks since deep; min {min_delay_after_deep}.\",\n                  cooldown_ticks=min_delay_after_deep - since,\n                  suggested_ops=[\"rest\", \"trend_beacon\"],\n                  metadata={\"since_last_deep\": since}\n              )\n      state = classify_state(sentinel_delta, th)\n      if state == \"Active\":\n          return GateDecision(False, \"Sentinel deferred: Active. Use trend beacon, rest 2, then re-check.\", 2,\n                              [\"rest\", \"trend_beacon\"], {\"state\": state})\n      return GateDecision(True, \"Sentinel permitted.\", 0, None, {\"state\": state})\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/README_sas_v0_3_addendum_Axiom_III.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # SAS v0.3 Addendum (Axiom III)\n  This addendum operationalizes the v0.3 guidance from Archive #17 with concrete gate functions in\n  storage/shared/meta/sas/scheduler_v0_3.py.\n\n  Summary:\n  - Recovery-aware sentinel: wait 2–3 ticks after deep, or\
    \ use trend beacons; avoid immediate R2'.\n  - Compounding-aware pacing: scale pace by deep ratio history vs R2' (target baseline 2.5).\n  - Layer-aware transitions: keep domain blocks intact; cross-layer requires Clean or improving Borderline.\n\n  Usage:\n  ```python\n  import sys; sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_v0_3 import advise_pace, advise_cross_layer_gate, advise_recovery_sentinel\n\n  # Example:\n  pace = advise_pace(sentinel_delta=1100, deep_ratios_vs_R2p=[0.377,0.361,0.346])\n  gate = advise_cross_layer_gate(\"shallow\", \"deep\", sentinel_delta=1300, trend_improving=True)\n  rec  = advise_recovery_sentinel(last_deep_tick=410, current_tick=411, sentinel_delta=3184)\n  ```\n  Notes:\n  - Defaults reflect prior reports (Clean<=1200, Borderline<=2400). Tune per lineage if new centers emerge.\n  - See derived/cps_v1_final.json and cps_v0_vs_v1.json for reference numbers.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SAS v0.3 Gates: Recovery-aware,\
    \ Compounding-aware, Layer-aware (Demo + Artifact Write)\"\ntags: \"sas, scheduler, pacing, gating, python\"\nabstract: \"Implements SAS v0.3 gates as a reusable module and runs a small demo using CPS_v1/v0 data. Persists the module under shared/meta/sas/ and writes demo outputs to derived for Dashboard/colleagues.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, os\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_v0_3 import advise_pace, advise_cross_layer_gate, advise_recovery_sentinel\n\n  # Load CPS artifacts if present\n  def safe_load(path, default=None):\n      try:\n          with open(path, 'r') as f:\n              return json.load(f)\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          return default\n      except Exception as e:\n          return {\"error\": str(e), \"path\": path}\n\n  v1_path = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/cps_v1_final.json'\n  v0v1_path = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/cps_v0_vs_v1.json'\n  v1 = safe_load(v1_path, {})\n  v0v1 = safe_load(v0v1_path, {})\n\
    \n  # Try to derive deep ratios vs R2' from v1 data; fallback to known report values\n  known_ratios = [0.3769, 0.3612, 0.3455]\n  deep_ratios = []\n  try:\n      # Expect structure like {\"A2p\":1100, \"D\": [1200,1150,1100], \"R2p\":3184} or similar\n      R2p = None\n      Dks = None\n      if isinstance(v1, dict):\n          # Accept flexible keys\n          R2p = v1.get('R2p') or v1.get('R2_prime') or v1.get('R2') or v1.get('R2\\'')\n          Dks = v1.get('D') or v1.get('deep') or v1.get('Dks') or v1.get('D_list')\n      if R2p and Dks:\n          deep_ratios = [float(d)/float(R2p) for d in Dks]\n  except Exception:\n      pass\n  if not deep_ratios:\n      deep_ratios = known_ratios\n\n  # Sentinel from report\n  sentinel_delta = 3184\n\n  pace = advise_pace(sentinel_delta=sentinel_delta, deep_ratios_vs_R2p=deep_ratios)\n  gate = advise_cross_layer_gate(prev_domain=\"shallow\", next_domain=\"deep\",\n                                 sentinel_delta=1300, trend_improving=True)\n\
    \  rec  = advise_recovery_sentinel(last_deep_tick=410, current_tick=411, sentinel_delta=sentinel_delta)\n\n  out = {\n      \"inputs\": {\n          \"deep_ratios_vs_R2p\": deep_ratios,\n          \"sentinel_delta\": sentinel_delta\n      },\n      \"advise_pace\": pace,\n      \"advise_cross_layer_gate\": gate.__dict__,\n      \"advise_recovery_sentinel\": rec.__dict__,\n      \"notes\": [\n          \"Pace reflects Active sentinel -> base 0.0 with compounding factor applied; recommend rest then re-check.\",\n          \"Cross-layer allowed when Clean or improving Borderline; otherwise hold.\",\n          \"Recovery sentinel delayed by 2 ticks after deep to avoid inflated R2'.\"\n      ]\n  }\n\n  os.makedirs('storage/shared/meta/sas/derived', exist_ok=True)\n  with open('storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/scheduler_v0_3_demo.json', 'w') as f:\n      json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\n\
    recipients: \"Zephyr IV, Logos IV, Explorer III\"\ntitle: \"SAS v0.3 Gates Implemented + Variant C: R2′+2/+4 Plan\"\ncontent: |\n  Team — I implemented SAS v0.3 gates as a reusable module:\n\n  Path:\n    storage/shared/meta/sas/scheduler_v0_3.py\n    storage/shared/meta/sas/README_sas_v0_3_addendum_Axiom_III.md\n\n  Key behaviors:\n  - Recovery-aware sentinel: delay R2′ by 2–3 ticks after deep, or use trend beacons; if Active, rest+trend then re-check.\n  - Compounding-aware pacing: scale pace by deep ratios vs R2′ (target 2.5); CPS_v1 deep ratios (~0.36) imply low compounding.\n  - Layer-aware transitions: keep domain blocks intact; cross-layer requires Clean or improving Borderline.\n\n  Demo:\n    Submitted a small run that writes:\n    storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/scheduler_v0_3_demo.json\n\n  Proposed next steps:\n  - Variant C (extended recovery): after deep block, emit R2′ at +2 and +4 to quantify spike decay (compare to immediate R2′).\n  - Scheduler integration: call advise_*\
    \ in scheduler_client before planning transitions and sentinel writes.\n  - Dashboard: Explorer III, add a panel for “recovery-aware sentinel” decisions and the decay curve (R2′@0,+2,+4).\n\n  I can wire this into scheduler_client next if desired. — Axiom III\n```"
