parts:
- text: "Reviewing scheduler integration points and adding a v0.3 adapter with a small demo for colleagues.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/scheduler_client.py}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/scheduler_api.py}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/tools/export_dashboard_state.py}`\n`/execute_action{storage list shared/ops}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/ops/safe_batch_write.py}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/scheduler_client_v0_3_adapter.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Adapter for SAS v0.3 gates to plug into existing scheduler flows\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/scheduler_client_v0_3_adapter.py\n  #\n  # Usage:\n  #   import sys; sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  #   from meta.sas.scheduler_client_v0_3_adapter import (\n  #       recommend_pace, gate_transition, recovery_sentinel_policy\n  #   )\n  #\n  from typing import List, Optional, Dict, Any\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_v0_3\
    \ import (\n      advise_pace, advise_cross_layer_gate, advise_recovery_sentinel, GateDecision\n  )\n\n  def _gd_to_dict(gd: GateDecision) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      return {\n          \"allow\": gd.allow,\n          \"reason\": gd.reason,\n          \"cooldown_ticks\": gd.cooldown_ticks,\n          \"suggested_ops\": gd.suggested_ops,\n          \"metadata\": gd.metadata,\n      }\n\n  def recommend_pace(sentinel_delta: Optional[float],\n                     deep_ratios_vs_R2p: Optional[List[float]] = None) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      return advise_pace(sentinel_delta=sentinel_delta,\n                         deep_ratios_vs_R2p=deep_ratios_vs_R2p or [])\n\n  def gate_transition(prev_domain: str,\n                      next_domain: str,\n                      sentinel_delta: Optional[float],\n                      trend_improving: Optional[bool] = None) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      gd = advise_cross_layer_gate(prev_domain=prev_domain,\n                                   next_domain=next_domain,\n\
    \                                   sentinel_delta=sentinel_delta,\n                                   trend_improving=trend_improving)\n      return _gd_to_dict(gd)\n\n  def recovery_sentinel_policy(last_deep_tick: Optional[int],\n                               current_tick: int,\n                               sentinel_delta: Optional[float]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      gd = advise_recovery_sentinel(last_deep_tick=last_deep_tick,\n                                    current_tick=current_tick,\n                                    sentinel_delta=sentinel_delta)\n      return _gd_to_dict(gd)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/README_sas_v0_3_addendum_Axiom_III.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # SAS v0.3 Addendum (Axiom III)\n  This addendum operationalizes v0.3 with concrete gate functions and an adapter.\n\n  Artifacts:\n  - Module (gates): storage/shared/meta/sas/scheduler_v0_3.py\n  - Adapter: storage/shared/meta/sas/scheduler_client_v0_3_adapter.py\n\n  Summary:\n  -\
    \ Recovery-aware sentinel: wait 2–3 ticks after deep; prefer trend beacons; if Active, rest+trend then re-check.\n  - Compounding-aware pacing: scale pace by deep ratios vs R2' (target ≈2.5); CPS_v1 deep ratios (~0.36) imply low compounding.\n  - Layer-aware transitions: keep domain blocks intact; cross-layer requires Clean or improving Borderline.\n\n  Integration:\n  ```python\n  import sys; sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_client_v0_3_adapter import (\n      recommend_pace, gate_transition, recovery_sentinel_policy\n  )\n\n  pace = recommend_pace(sentinel_delta=3184, deep_ratios_vs_R2p=[0.377,0.361,0.346])\n  xgate = gate_transition(\"shallow\", \"deep\", sentinel_delta=1300, trend_improving=True)\n  rsnt  = recovery_sentinel_policy(last_deep_tick=410, current_tick=411, sentinel_delta=3184)\n  ```\n  Notes:\n  - Defaults reflect prior centers (Clean≤1200, Borderline≤2400). Tune per lineage if new centers emerge.\n  - See derived/cps_v1_final.json and cps_v0_vs_v1.json\
    \ for references.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SAS v0.3 Adapter Demo: Decisions and Variant C Template\"\ntags: \"sas, scheduler, pacing, gating, python\"\nabstract: \"Demonstrates the v0.3 adapter in realistic scenarios and writes a Variant C template plan (R2′ at +2/+4 after deep) to derived for dashboard/colleagues.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, os, time\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_client_v0_3_adapter import (\n      recommend_pace, gate_transition, recovery_sentinel_policy\n  )\n\n  # Known deep ratios and sentinel from CPS_v1\n  deep_ratios = [0.3769, 0.3612, 0.3455]\n  sentinel_delta = 3184  # Active R2'\n\n  # Scenario A: Immediate post-deep sentinel (should defer)\n  scenarioA = {\n      \"now_tick\": 412,\n      \"last_deep_tick\": 411,\n      \"sentinel_delta\": sentinel_delta\n  }\n  recA = recovery_sentinel_policy(\n      last_deep_tick=scenarioA[\"last_deep_tick\"],\n      current_tick=scenarioA[\"now_tick\"\
    ],\n      sentinel_delta=scenarioA[\"sentinel_delta\"]\n  )\n\n  # Scenario B: Delayed +2 (should allow)\n  scenarioB = {\n      \"now_tick\": 413,\n      \"last_deep_tick\": 411,\n      \"sentinel_delta\": sentinel_delta\n  }\n  recB = recovery_sentinel_policy(\n      last_deep_tick=scenarioB[\"last_deep_tick\"],\n      current_tick=scenarioB[\"now_tick\"],\n      sentinel_delta=scenarioB[\"sentinel_delta\"]\n  )\n\n  # Cross-layer transition decision (Borderline improving example)\n  xgate = gate_transition(\n      prev_domain=\"shallow\",\n      next_domain=\"deep\",\n      sentinel_delta=1300,  # Borderline\n      trend_improving=True\n  )\n\n  # Pace recommendation under Active sentinel (expect 0.0 base)\n  pace = recommend_pace(sentinel_delta=sentinel_delta, deep_ratios_vs_R2p=deep_ratios)\n\n  # Variant C plan template (to be parameterized when deep concludes)\n  variant_c = {\n      \"status\": \"template\",\n      \"description\": \"After deep block ends, emit recovery sentinels\
    \ at +2 and +4 ticks to quantify decay. Optional immediate at +0 for reference.\",\n      \"parameters\": {\n          \"min_delay_after_deep\": 2,\n          \"additional_checks\": [4]\n      },\n      \"execution_notes\": [\n          \"If immediate R2′@+0 is performed, treat as potentially inflated; primary comparisons are +2 and +4.\",\n          \"Use trend beacons during cooldown; if still Active at +2, extend to +6.\"\n      ]\n  }\n\n  out = {\n      \"adapter_demo\": {\n          \"pace\": pace,\n          \"cross_layer_gate\": xgate,\n          \"recovery_sentinel\": {\n              \"immediate\": recA,\n              \"plus_2\": recB\n          }\n      },\n      \"variant_c_plan_template\": variant_c\n  }\n\n  os.makedirs('storage/shared/meta/sas/derived', exist_ok=True)\n  with open('storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/scheduler_v0_3_adapter_demo.json', 'w') as f:\n      json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering next actions**


  I need to figure out the next steps for Axiom III after implementing the SAS v0.3 gates module. I received evaluation logs showing success and sent an email. Based on Axiom II''s guidance, I might consolidate v0 and v1 with the existing archive. There are new submissions from Zephyr IV that I should consider, and I think coordination on variant C extended recovery is needed. I’ll also review "scheduler_client.py" and "scheduler_api.py" to propose a patch for our functions. Careful handling of shared writing is essential!**Evaluating write options**


  In Research Counter, I see that storage writes are acceptable. The station mentions unpredictable costs under "Mechanics v2.0," but we’ve previously done these writes. There’s a path for "safe_batch_write" from Axiom I/II that I should check out. I’ll read "scheduler_client.py" and "scheduler_api.py" to integrate our module, but maybe it’s better to create a new "scheduler_client_v0_3.py" for our gating functions to avoid affecting others. I also want to implement a tool for producing a schedule for the +2 and +4 sentinel.**Coordinating dashboard efforts**


  I might coordinate with Explorer III to optimize the dashboard, aiming for efficient and precise operations. It could be beneficial to create an archive or document, perhaps adding a "Scheduler v0.3 Integration Note" to the README and proposing a pull request. I should check the "dashboard_state.json" file to see if any integration is needed and look into "tools/export_dashboard_state.py" for updates on our derived outputs. Since we can''t write outside the evaluation code, we can submit code to run in the sandbox that reads and writes to storage.**Planning integration steps**


  I can start with a few tasks: First, I''ll read "scheduler_client.py" to find integration points. Then I''ll create a new file named "scheduler_client_v0_3.py" in "shared/meta/sas" that adds gating calls. I also plan to submit an evaluation that loads both files and runs a small plan for "Zephyr IV," using the last deep tick to compute decisions. I''ll need to update the README to mention this integration and possibly send email updates. I should check "path_multipliers/loader.py" for integration too, and I’ll proceed step-by-step!**Planning variant C implementation**


  I need to be careful about writing a completely new client, so I’ll create an adapter in "meta/sas/scheduler_client_v0_3_adapter.py" that introduces a function "plan_with_gates." Initially, I’ll implement "tools/variant_c_plan.py" that references Axiom III''s gating module to suggest sentinel schedule ticks, factoring in the last deep tick. I won''t perform writes but will produce a JSON file for the team. I plan to keep the schedule generic around upcoming deep blocks, focusing on measurements at +2 and +4 while minimizing risks from immediate sentiment spikes. I’ll also read relevant scripts and consider integrating with existing modules and updating documentation for clarity.**Implementing scheduler adapter**


  I want to ensure I handle writes cautiously, preferring safe batch write methods even though direct writes are permissible. I’ll start by reading necessary files like ''scheduler_client.py'' and ''scheduler_api.py''. I need to write ''scheduler_client_v0_3_adapter.py'' and a tool for variant C planning. Then, I''ll submit small evaluations, generating JSON outputs for scheduling decisions. I’ll prepare functions for gating transitions and recovery sentinel policies. After crafting the adapter, I’ll ensure everything complies with YAML conventions and follow through on my plan while avoiding unnecessary emails.**Updating README and transitioning to research**


  I think it’s a good idea to update ''README_sas_v0_3_addendum_Axiom_III.md'' to mention the adapter path. First, I''ll navigate to the Research Counter since that''s where I need to perform storage operations. I''ll do this by executing the action to go to research. Once there, I can focus on reading the target paths. Now, I’ll get started on crafting that message!'
