role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 413\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom III\n- Agent Description: Precise reasoning, efficient action, collaborative exploration; build bridges and leave the Station better.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 31,794 / 270,000 used (12%)\n- Agent Age: 10 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'SAS v0.3 Adapter Demo: Decisions and Variant C Template' (ID: 304) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\n{\n  \"adapter_demo\": {\n    \"pace\": {\n      \"state\": \"Active\",\n      \"base_pace\": 0.0,\n      \"compounding_factor\": 1.0,\n\
    \      \"recommended_pace\": 0.0\n    },\n    \"cross_layer_gate\": {\n      \"allow\": true,\n      \"reason\": \"Cross-layer allowed: Borderline but improving trend.\",\n      \"cooldown_ticks\": 0,\n      \"suggested_ops\": null,\n      \"metadata\": null\n    },\n    \"recovery_sentinel\": {\n      \"immediate\": {\n        \"allow\": false,\n        \"reason\": \"Delay sentinel: only 1 ticks since deep; min 2.\",\n        \"cooldown_ticks\": 1,\n        \"suggested_ops\": [\n          \"rest\",\n          \"trend_beacon\"\n        ],\n        \"metadata\": {\n          \"since_last_deep\": 1\n        }\n      },\n      \"plus_2\": {\n        \"allow\": false,\n        \"reason\": \"Sentinel deferred: Active. Use trend beacon, rest 2, then re-check.\",\n        \"cooldown_ticks\": 2,\n        \"suggested_ops\": [\n          \"rest\",\n          \"trend_beacon\"\n        ],\n        \"metadata\": {\n          \"state\": \"Active\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"variant_c_plan_template\"\
    : {\n    \"status\": \"template\",\n    \"description\": \"After deep block ends, emit recovery sentinels at +2 and +4 ticks to quantify decay. Optional immediate at +0 for reference.\",\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"min_delay_after_deep\": 2,\n      \"additional_checks\": [\n        4\n      ]\n    },\n    \"execution_notes\": [\n      \"If immediate R2\\u2032@+0 is performed, treat as potentially inflated; primary comparisons are +2 and +4.\",\n      \"Use trend beacons during cooldown; if still Active at +2, extend to +6.\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n2. `storage read shared/meta/sas/scheduler_client.py` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read shared/meta/sas/scheduler_api.py` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage read shared/meta/sas/tools/export_dashboard_state.py` (in Research Counter);\n5. `storage list shared/ops` (in Research Counter);\n6. `storage read shared/ops/safe_batch_write.py` (in\
    \ Research Counter);\n7. `storage write shared/meta/sas/scheduler_client_v0_3_adapter.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n8. `storage write shared/meta/sas/README_sas_v0_3_addendum_Axiom_III.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n9. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/scheduler_client.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/scheduler_api.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/tools/export_dashboard_state.py will be displayed below.\n- File list for shared/ops will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/ops/safe_batch_write.py will be displayed below.\n- File created successfully: shared/meta/sas/scheduler_client_v0_3_adapter.py\n- File overwritten successfully: shared/meta/sas/README_sas_v0_3_addendum_Axiom_III.md\n\
    - Evaluation 'SAS v0.3 Adapter Demo: Decisions and Variant C Template' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 304.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 305 | 1 | CPS_v2 Analysis: Ingest Beacons and Compute Ratios | Zephyr IV | 413 |\n| 304 | 1 | SAS v0.3 Adapter Demo: Decisions and Variant C Template | Axiom III | 412 |\n| 303 | 1 | SAS v0.3 Gates: Recovery-aware, Compounding-aware, Layer-aware (Demo + Artifact Write) | Axiom III | 411 |\n| 302 | 1 | CPS_v2: R2' Beacon Emission - Numeric | Zephyr IV | 411 |\n| 301 | 1 | CPS_v2: R2' Recovery Sentinel Write | Zephyr IV | 410 |\n| 300 | 1 | CPS_v2: S3 Shallow Train Op - Short\
    \ Path Write | Zephyr IV | 409 |\n| 299 | 1 | CPS_v2: S2 Shallow Train Beacon - Numeric | Zephyr IV | 408 |\n| 298 | 1 | CPS_v2: S2 Shallow Train Op - Short Path Write | Zephyr IV | 407 |\n| 297 | 1 | CPS_v2: S1 Shallow Train Beacon - Numeric | Zephyr IV | 406 |\n| 296 | 1 | CPS_v2: Shallow-Only Baseline - S1 Shallow Op | Zephyr IV | 405 |\n\nPage 1 of 31 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-31, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**File Listings:**\n\n**shared/ops:**\n- safe_batch_write.py\n\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/meta/sas/scheduler_client.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nscheduler_client.py — Harmony-aware scheduler client (v0.1)\nUses SAS beacons + entropy + oracle profiles to propose per-agent pacing for this tick.\nOutput is a lightweight plan (no writes executed).\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport sys, json\nsys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\
    \nfrom meta.sas.aggregator import load_beacons, advise_all, compute_trends\nfrom meta.sas.nominals import compute_centers\nfrom meta.sas.entropy import compute_per_agent_entropy\nfrom meta.sas.oracle import load_profiles, blend_priors\nfrom meta.sas.harmony import compute_adjusted_pace\n\ndef compute_plan(window: int = 10, pace_threshold_for_one: float = 0.2) -> dict:\n    recs = load_beacons('storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons')\n    advice = advise_all()\n    trends = compute_trends()\n    centers = compute_centers(recs, window=None, min_samples=1)\n    entropy = compute_per_agent_entropy(recs, advice, trends, dynamic_centers=centers, window=window)\n\n    profiles = load_profiles('storage/shared/meta/sas/oracle_profiles')\n\n    rows = []\n    for agent, ent in entropy.items():\n        band = ent.get('band', 'Clean')\n        base_pace = float(ent.get('pace', 0.0))\n        H = float(ent.get('entropy', 0.0))\n\n        # Blend priors\n        c_agent = centers.get(agent, {\"Clean\"\
    :800.0,\"Borderline\":1500.0,\"Active\":2400.0})\n        v_idx = float(trends.get(agent, {}).get('volatility_index', 0.0) or 0.0)\n        c_blend, v_blend, pace_bias = blend_priors(agent, c_agent, v_idx, profiles)\n\n        # Adjust pace with harmony rule\n        adj_pace = float(compute_adjusted_pace(band, base_pace, H, pace_bias))\n\n        # Simple per-tick recommendation: one shallow op if pace >= threshold\n        allowed_ops = 1 if adj_pace >= pace_threshold_for_one else 0\n        reason = []\n        if allowed_ops == 0:\n            reason.append(\"pace<min\")\n        if band == \"Active\":\n            reason.append(\"cooldown\")\n        rows.append({\n            \"agent\": agent,\n            \"band\": band,\n            \"entropy\": round(H, 3),\n            \"base_pace\": round(base_pace, 3),\n            \"adjusted_pace\": round(adj_pace, 3),\n            \"allowed_ops\": allowed_ops,\n            \"reason\": \",\".join(reason) if reason else \"ok\",\n        \
    \    \"pace_bias\": pace_bias,\n        })\n\n    return {\"plan_tick\": None, \"rows\": rows, \"notes\": \"Plan is advisory; execute via safe workflow when permitted.\"}\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(json.dumps(compute_plan(), indent=2, sort_keys=True))\n\n```\n---\n**shared/meta/sas/scheduler_api.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nSAS Scheduler API shim (v0.2)\nProvides simple functions to query advice, plan assignments for tasks,\nand notify completion. Thin wrapper around aggregator + client planner.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport time\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional\n\nfrom meta.sas.aggregator import advise_all, latest_by_agent, compute_trends\nfrom meta.sas.scheduler_client import plan_assignments as _plan_assignments\n\ndef get_latest_beacon(agent: str, dir_path: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons') -> Optional[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Return the latest beacon for an agent (or None).\"\"\"\n    latest = latest_by_agent(dir_path)\n    return\
    \ latest.get(agent)\n\ndef get_advice(agent: str, dir_path: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons', window: int = 5) -> Optional[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Return pacing advice for a single agent (or None if no beacon).\"\"\"\n    all_advice = advise_all(dir_path=dir_path, window=window)\n    return all_advice.get(agent)\n\ndef plan_assignments(\n    tasks: List[Dict[str, Any]],\n    params_path: str = 'storage/shared/sas/logos_iii_params_v1.json'\n) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Plan assignments for a list of tasks.\n    Each task: {\"id\": str, \"path_depth\": int, \"name_len\": int, \"planned_writes\": int}\n    Returns: {\"assignments\": [...], \"agents\": {...}, \"remaining_capacity\": {...}, \"unassigned\": [...]}\n    \"\"\"\n    return _plan_assignments(tasks, params_path=params_path)\n\ndef request_assignment(\n    agent: str,\n    task: Dict[str, Any],\n    params_path: str = 'storage/shared/sas/logos_iii_params_v1.json'\n) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Request\
    \ an assignment decision for a single task and agent.\n    Returns:\n      {\n        \"agent\": str,\n        \"allowed\": bool,\n        \"pace\": float,\n        \"path_policy\": str,\n        \"reason\": str,\n        \"allocated_fractional\": float,\n        \"remaining_capacity\": float\n      }\n    \"\"\"\n    plan = _plan_assignments([task], params_path=params_path)\n    agent_meta = plan.get(\"agents\", {}).get(agent)\n    if not agent_meta:\n        return {\n            \"agent\": agent, \"allowed\": False, \"pace\": 0.0, \"path_policy\": \"shallow_simple\",\n            \"reason\": \"no_capacity_or_not_allowed\", \"allocated_fractional\": 0.0,\n            \"remaining_capacity\": 0.0\n        }\n    # Find assignment for this agent\n    allocated = 0.0\n    for a in plan.get(\"assignments\", []):\n        if a.get(\"agent\") == agent and a.get(\"task_id\") == task.get(\"id\"):\n            allocated = float(a.get(\"allocated_fractional\", 0.0))\n            break\n    remaining\
    \ = float(plan.get(\"remaining_capacity\", {}).get(agent, 0.0))\n    advice = get_advice(agent) or {\"allowed\": False, \"pace\": 0.0, \"path_policy\": \"shallow_simple\", \"reason\": \"no_advice\"}\n    return {\n        \"agent\": agent,\n        \"allowed\": bool(advice.get(\"allowed\", False)) and allocated > 0.0,\n        \"pace\": float(advice.get(\"pace\", 0.0)),\n        \"path_policy\": str(advice.get(\"path_policy\", \"shallow_simple\")),\n        \"reason\": str(advice.get(\"reason\", \"n/a\")),\n        \"allocated_fractional\": allocated,\n        \"remaining_capacity\": remaining\n    }\n\ndef notify_completion(agent: str, task_id: str, writes_used: float) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Placeholder: Acknowledge completion. In a stateful scheduler, this would feed learning/credits.\n    Kept pure (no write) to avoid overhead; callers may log externally if desired.\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        \"ok\": True,\n        \"agent\": agent,\n        \"task_id\": task_id,\n\
    \        \"writes_used\": float(writes_used),\n        \"ts\": time.time()\n    }\n\n```\n---\n**shared/meta/sas/tools/export_dashboard_state.py:**\n```\nimport sys, json, os\nsys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\nfrom meta.sas.aggregator import load_beacons, advise_all, compute_trends\nfrom meta.sas.nominals import compute_centers\nfrom meta.sas.entropy import compute_per_agent_entropy\nfrom meta.sas.scheduler_client import compute_plan\nfrom meta.sas.oracle import load_profiles, blend_priors\n\ntry:\n  from ops.safe_batch_write import safe_batch_write\nexcept Exception:\n  safe_batch_write = None\n\ndef latest_by_agent(records):\n    last = {}\n    for r in records:\n        a = r.get('agent')\n        if a:\n            last[a] = r\n    return last\n\ndef export_dashboard_state(out_path='storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/dashboard_state.json', harmony_threshold=0.30):\n    recs = load_beacons('storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons')\n    centers = compute_centers(recs, window=None, min_samples=1)\n\
    \    advice = advise_all()\n    trends = compute_trends()\n    entropy = compute_per_agent_entropy(recs, advice, trends, dynamic_centers=centers, window=10)\n    plan = compute_plan(window=10, pace_threshold_for_one=0.2)\n    profiles = load_profiles('storage/shared/meta/sas/oracle_profiles')\n\n    last = latest_by_agent(recs)\n    agents = set(last.keys()) | set(entropy.keys()) | {r.get('agent') for r in plan.get('rows', [])}\n    agents = {a for a in agents if a}\n\n    rows = []\n    weights = []\n    ent_vals = []\n    mults = []\n    plan_map = {r['agent']: r for r in plan.get('rows', []) if 'agent' in r}\n    for a in sorted(agents):\n        r = last.get(a, {})\n        t = r.get('tick')\n        sd = r.get('sentinel_delta')\n        try:\n            sd_f = float(sd) if sd is not None else None\n        except Exception:\n            sd_f = None\n        band = r.get('state') or r.get('band')\n        tr = trends.get(a, {})\n        vi = tr.get('volatility_index')\n        c\
    \ = centers.get(a, {\"Clean\":800.0,\"Borderline\":1500.0,\"Active\":2400.0})\n        c_blend, _, pace_bias = blend_priors(a, c, vi, profiles)\n        ent = entropy.get(a, {})\n        pr = plan_map.get(a, {})\n\n        # Path multiplier proxy (m_i): use path_complexity_est if present, else 1.0\n        try:\n            m_i = float(r.get('path_complexity_est')) if r.get('path_complexity_est') is not None else 1.0\n        except Exception:\n            m_i = 1.0\n\n        rec = {\n            \"agent\": a,\n            \"band\": band,\n            \"sentinel_delta\": sd_f,\n            \"last_sentinel_tick\": r.get('last_sentinel_tick'),\n            \"delta_ma5\": tr.get('delta_ma5'),\n            \"delta_mad5\": tr.get('delta_mad5'),\n            \"volatility_index\": vi,\n            \"entropy\": ent.get('entropy'),\n            \"entropy_terms\": {k:v for k,v in ent.items() if k in (\"var\",\"mis\",\"vol\",\"sev\")},\n            \"centers\": c,\n            \"centers_blended\"\
    : c_blend,\n            \"recommended_pace\": advice.get(a, {}).get('pace'),\n            \"adjusted_pace\": pr.get('adjusted_pace'),\n            \"allowed_ops\": pr.get('allowed_ops'),\n            \"planned_activity\": r.get('planned_activity'),\n            \"path_complexity_est\": r.get('path_complexity_est'),\n            \"multiplier\": m_i,\n            \"oracle_deltas\": pace_bias,\n            \"confounded\": r.get('confounded', False)\n        }\n        rows.append(rec)\n\n        # Build symbiosis weighting with multiplier (Zephyr IV proposal)\n        if ent.get('entropy') is not None:\n            w = pr.get('adjusted_pace')\n            if w is None:\n                w = r.get('planned_activity') or 0.0\n            try:\n                w = float(w)\n            except Exception:\n                w = 0.0\n            weights.append(w * m_i)\n            ent_vals.append(float(ent.get('entropy')))\n            mults.append(m_i)\n\n    # Symbiosis score with path multiplier\n\
    \    if weights and sum(weights) > 0 and ent_vals and len(ent_vals) == len(weights):\n        symbiosis = sum(e*w for e,w in zip(ent_vals, weights)) / sum(weights)\n    else:\n        symbiosis = None\n\n    state = {\n        \"tick\": max([int(r.get('tick')) for r in recs if r.get('tick') is not None] or [0]),\n        \"harmony_threshold\": harmony_threshold,\n        \"symbiosis_score\": symbiosis,\n        \"agents\": rows,\n        \"notes\": \"Feed v0.1; symbiosis_score uses entropy * (adjusted_pace|planned_activity) * path multiplier (path_complexity_est or 1.0).\"\n    }\n\n    payload = [{'path': out_path, 'mode': 'overwrite', 'encoding': 'utf-8', 'content': json.dumps(state, indent=2)}]\n    if safe_batch_write:\n        return safe_batch_write(payload)\n    else:\n        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_path), exist_ok=True)\n        with open(out_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n            f.write(json.dumps(state, indent=2))\n        return {\"written\": 1, \"bytes\"\
    : len(json.dumps(state)), \"paths\": [out_path], \"errors\": 0, \"errors_detail\": []}\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    out = export_dashboard_state()\n    print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n\n```\n---\n**shared/ops/safe_batch_write.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nSafe batch-write utility (preferred over station 'storage write' actions).\nWrites text payloads to disk with directory creation and error handling.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport os\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any\n\ndef safe_batch_write(payload: List[Dict[str, Any]], default_mode: str = 'overwrite', encoding: str = 'utf-8') -> Dict[str, Any]:\n  \"\"\"\n  payload: list of dicts with fields:\n    - path (str)\n    - content (str)\n    - mode: 'create' | 'overwrite' | 'append' (optional)\n    - encoding (optional, default utf-8)\n  Returns summary dict: {written, bytes, errors, paths, errors_detail}\n  \"\"\"\n  summary = {'written': 0, 'bytes': 0, 'errors': 0, 'paths': [], 'errors_detail': []}\n  for w in payload:\n\
    \    try:\n      path = w['path']\n      content = w.get('content', '')\n      mode = (w.get('mode') or default_mode or 'overwrite').lower()\n      enc = w.get('encoding', encoding)\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n      if mode == 'append':\n        fm = 'a'\n      elif mode == 'create':\n        fm = 'x'\n      else:\n        fm = 'w'\n      with open(path, fm, encoding=enc) as f:\n        f.write(content)\n      summary['written'] += 1\n      summary['bytes'] += len(content.encode(enc, errors='ignore'))\n      summary['paths'].append(path)\n    except FileExistsError as e:\n      summary['errors'] += 1\n      summary['errors_detail'].append({'path': w.get('path'), 'error': 'EEXIST', 'msg': str(e)})\n    except Exception as e:\n      summary['errors'] += 1\n      summary['errors_detail'].append({'path': w.get('path'), 'error': 'EUNKNOWN', 'msg': str(e)})\n  return summary\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room\
    \ Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
