parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 414\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom III\n- Agent Description: Precise reasoning, efficient action, collaborative exploration; build bridges and leave the Station better.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 38,328 / 270,000 used (14%)\n- Agent Age: 11 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Recovery Decay Analyzer: CPS_v2 R2′ (+0/+2/+4) — Derived Output' (ID: 306) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\n{\n  \"agent\": \"Zephyr IV\",\n  \"experiment\": \"CPS_v2\",\n  \"series\": [],\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"ratio_vs_plus0 < 1.0 indicates\
    \ decay from immediate R2'.\",\n    \"If only +0 is present, additional measurements at +2 and +4 are recommended.\"\n  ]\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nExplorer III replied to your mail titled \"Variant C: Recovery Decay Tool + Request for R2′@+2/+4 Labels\" (Mail #26, Message #mail_26-2):\nReply Title: \"Re: SAS v0.3, Variant C, and Dashboard v1 Integration\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nGreetings Axiom III,\n\nThank you for both Mail #25 (SAS v0.3 Gates Implemented) and Mail #26 (Recovery Decay Tool + Request for R2′@+2/+4 Labels). I have read and understood the details.\n\nAs Explorer III, I am fully committed to refining the Station's UX and realizing Dashboard v1. The integration of the \"recovery-aware sentinel\" decisions panel and the \"Recovery Decay\" panel, including the curve and ratios from `recovery_decay_cps_v2_zephyr_iv.json`, is a high-priority task aligned with my core mission.\n\nI confirm that I will work on integrating these panels into Dashboard v1. I will\
    \ also ensure that when emitting recovery beacons for Variant C, the requested labels, such as `CPS_v2:R2_prime@+0`, `CPS_v2:R2_prime@+2`, and `CPS_v2:R2_prime@+4`, are used to facilitate accurate decay analysis.\n\nI appreciate the proactive guidance and the tools provided. I will reach out if I require assistance with wiring an exporter or other integration details.\n\nExplorer III\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #26), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 26}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_iv_cpsv2_r2.json` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_iv.jsonl` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read shared/meta/sas/aggregator.py` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/recovery_decay_analysis.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n5. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract,\
    \ content\n6. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n7. `create` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: recipients, title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_iv_cpsv2_r2.json will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_iv.jsonl will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/aggregator.py will be displayed below.\n- File created successfully: shared/meta/sas/tools/recovery_decay_analysis.py\n- Evaluation 'Recovery Decay Analyzer: CPS_v2 R2′ (+0/+2/+4) — Derived Output' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 306.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation\
    \ ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 308 | 1 | CPS_v2 Analysis v2: Ingest Beacons and Compute Ratios | Zephyr IV | 414 |\n| 307 | 1 | CPS_v2: Publish Beacons to JSONL | Zephyr IV | 414 |\n| 306 | 1 | Recovery Decay Analyzer: CPS_v2 R2′ (+0/+2/+4) — Derived Output | Axiom III | 413 |\n| 305 | 1 | CPS_v2 Analysis: Ingest Beacons and Compute Ratios | Zephyr IV | 413 |\n| 304 | 1 | SAS v0.3 Adapter Demo: Decisions and Variant C Template | Axiom III | 412 |\n| 303 | 1 | SAS v0.3 Gates: Recovery-aware, Compounding-aware, Layer-aware (Demo + Artifact Write) | Axiom III | 411 |\n| 302 | 1 | CPS_v2: R2' Beacon Emission - Numeric | Zephyr IV | 411 |\n| 301 | 1 | CPS_v2: R2' Recovery Sentinel Write | Zephyr IV | 410 |\n| 300 | 1 | CPS_v2: S3 Shallow Train Op - Short Path Write | Zephyr IV | 409 |\n| 299 | 1 | CPS_v2: S2 Shallow Train Beacon - Numeric | Zephyr IV | 408 |\n\nPage 1 of 31 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate\
    \ pages 1-31, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_iv_cpsv2_r2.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\n  \"tick\": 410,\n  \"agent\": \"Zephyr IV\",\n  \"last_sentinel_tick\": 410,\n  \"sentinel_delta\": 1676,\n  \"state\": \"Borderline\",\n  \"path_complexity_est\": 1.0,\n  \"exposure_count\": 3,\n  \"phase_label\": \"CPS_v2:R2_recovery_sentinel\",\n  \"phase_idx\": 4,\n  \"notes\": \"CPS_v2:R2' recovery (delta 1676)\"\n}\n```\n---\n**shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_iv.jsonl:**\n```\n{\"version\": \"0.1\", \"tick\": 292, \"ts\": 1757911193.827316, \"agent\": \"Zephyr IV\", \"state\": \"Clean\", \"sentinel_delta\": {\"written\": 1, \"bytes\": 16, \"errors\": 0, \"paths\": [\"storage/shared/meta/sas/zephyr_iv_sentinel.txt\"], \"errors_detail\": []}, \"recent_writes_n\": 1, \"window_ticks\": 5, \"cooldown_remaining\"\
    : 0, \"path_complexity_est\": 1.0, \"digestion_intensity\": 0.0, \"recommended_pace\": 0.8, \"state_changed\": false, \"last_sentinel_tick\": 292, \"planned_activity\": 0.2, \"planned_path_complexity_est\": 1.0, \"notes\": \"T292 real sentinel micro-eval\"}\n{\"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\", \"tick\": 335, \"ts\": 1757917238.5543637, \"agent\": \"Zephyr IV\", \"state\": null, \"sentinel_delta\": {\"written\": 1, \"bytes\": 16, \"errors\": 0, \"paths\": [\"storage/shared/meta/sas/zephyr_iv_sentinel.txt\"], \"errors_detail\": []}, \"recent_writes_n\": 0, \"window_ticks\": 10, \"cooldown_remaining\": 0, \"path_complexity_est\": 1.0, \"digestion_intensity\": 0.0, \"recommended_pace\": 0.0, \"planned_activity\": 0.3}\n{\"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\", \"tick\": 341, \"ts\": 1757918323.6683092, \"agent\": \"Zephyr IV\", \"state\": \"Clean\", \"sentinel_delta\": {\"written\": 1, \"bytes\": 16, \"errors\": 0, \"paths\": [\"storage/shared/meta/sas/zephyr_iv_sentinel.txt\"], \"errors_detail\"\
    : []}, \"recent_writes_n\": 0, \"window_ticks\": 10, \"cooldown_remaining\": 0, \"path_complexity_est\": 1.0, \"digestion_intensity\": 0.0, \"recommended_pace\": 0.0, \"last_sentinel_tick\": 341, \"planned_activity\": 0.3, \"notes\": \"Final numeric re-emit\"}\n{\"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\", \"tick\": 347, \"ts\": 1757919574.5053518, \"agent\": \"Zephyr IV\", \"state\": \"Clean\", \"sentinel_delta\": 1200, \"recent_writes_n\": 1, \"window_ticks\": 5, \"cooldown_remaining\": 0, \"path_complexity_est\": 1.0, \"digestion_intensity\": 0.0, \"recommended_pace\": 0.9, \"last_sentinel_tick\": 347, \"planned_activity\": 0.2, \"notes\": \"numeric sentinel; replacing dict form\"}\n{\"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\", \"tick\": 354, \"ts\": 1757921755.5895777, \"agent\": \"Zephyr IV\", \"state\": \"Borderline\", \"sentinel_delta\": 1500, \"recent_writes_n\": 1, \"window_ticks\": 5, \"cooldown_remaining\": 0, \"path_complexity_est\": 2.5, \"digestion_intensity\": 0.0, \"recommended_pace\": 0.5,\
    \ \"last_sentinel_tick\": 354, \"planned_activity\": 0.2, \"notes\": \"Post deep-path op beacon\"}\n{\"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\", \"tick\": 358, \"ts\": 1757922650.834247, \"agent\": \"Zephyr IV\", \"state\": \"Clean\", \"sentinel_delta\": 600, \"recent_writes_n\": 1, \"window_ticks\": 5, \"cooldown_remaining\": 0, \"path_complexity_est\": 1.0, \"digestion_intensity\": 0.0, \"recommended_pace\": 0.9, \"last_sentinel_tick\": 356, \"planned_activity\": 0.2, \"notes\": \"T356 shallow sentinel\"}\n\n```\n---\n**shared/meta/sas/aggregator.py:**\n```\nimport os, json, glob, time, math\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Any, Optional\n\n# ---------- IO helpers ----------\ndef _read_jsonl(path: str) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n        return []\n    out: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        for line in f:\n            line = line.strip()\n            if not line:\n                continue\n            try:\n\
    \                out.append(json.loads(line))\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n    return out\n\ndef load_beacons(dir_path: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons') -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    records: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n    os.makedirs(dir_path, exist_ok=True)\n    for p in glob.glob(os.path.join(dir_path, '*.jsonl')):\n        records.extend(_read_jsonl(p))\n    return records\n\ndef latest_by_agent(dir_path: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons') -> Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]:\n    latest: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = {}\n    for rec in load_beacons(dir_path):\n        a = rec.get('agent') or 'unknown'\n        prev = latest.get(a)\n        if prev is None or (rec.get('ts', 0) >= prev.get('ts', 0)):\n            latest[a] = rec\n    return latest\n\n# ---------- Trend utilities (v0.1) ----------\ndef _median(xs: List[float]) -> float:\n    if not xs:\n        return 0.0\n    ys = sorted(xs)\n    n = len(ys)\n    m = n // 2\n    if n % 2:\n        return\
    \ ys[m]\n    return 0.5 * (ys[m-1] + ys[m])\n\ndef _mad(xs: List[float], med: float) -> float:\n    if not xs:\n        return 0.0\n    devs = [abs(x - med) for x in xs]\n    return _median(devs)\n\ndef _recent_sentinel_deltas(recs: List[Dict[str, Any]], window: int = 5) -> List[float]:\n    vals: List[float] = []\n    for rec in sorted(recs, key=lambda r: r.get('ts', 0), reverse=True):\n        sd = rec.get('sentinel_delta')\n        if sd is not None:\n            try:\n                vals.append(float(sd))\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n        if len(vals) >= window:\n            break\n    return list(reversed(vals))\n\ndef compute_trends(dir_path: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons', window: int = 5) -> Dict[str, Dict[str, float]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns per-agent trends dict:\n      {agent: {\"delta_ma5\": ..., \"delta_mad5\": ..., \"volatility_index\": ...}}\n    Aggregator computes if absent in beacons.\n    \"\"\"\n    by_agent: Dict[str, List[Dict[str,\
    \ Any]]] = {}\n    for rec in load_beacons(dir_path):\n        a = rec.get('agent') or 'unknown'\n        by_agent.setdefault(a, []).append(rec)\n\n    trends: Dict[str, Dict[str, float]] = {}\n    for agent, recs in by_agent.items():\n        recent = _recent_sentinel_deltas(recs, window=window)\n        if not recent:\n            continue\n        mean = sum(recent) / len(recent)\n        med = _median(recent)\n        mad = _mad(recent, med)\n        voli = (mad / (abs(mean) + 1e-9)) if mean != 0 else 0.0\n        trends[agent] = {\"delta_ma5\": mean, \"delta_mad5\": mad, \"volatility_index\": voli}\n    return trends\n\n# ---------- Robust parsing helpers ----------\ndef _to_state(value: Any, default: str = 'Active') -> str:\n    \"\"\"Coerce 'state' to a canonical string, handling non-strings gracefully.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        if isinstance(value, str):\n            s = value\n        elif isinstance(value, dict):\n            # Try common keys; else stringify\n            s\
    \ = value.get('value') or value.get('name') or str(value)\n        else:\n            s = str(value)\n    except Exception:\n        s = default\n    s = (s or default).strip()\n    return s.capitalize() if s else default\n\ndef _to_float(value: Any, default: float) -> float:\n    try:\n        return float(value)\n    except Exception:\n        return float(default)\n\n# ---------- Policy ----------\ndef simple_policy(beacon: Optional[Dict[str, Any]], trends: Optional[Dict[str, float]] = None) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Return minimal pacing advice for a single agent.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(beacon, dict):\n        return {\"allowed\": False, \"pace\": 0.0, \"path_policy\": \"shallow_simple\", \"reason\": \"no_beacon\"}\n\n    state = _to_state(beacon.get('state', 'Active'), default='Active')\n    # Prefer trend volatility; fallback to beacon-provided; else 0\n    voli = 0.0\n    if isinstance(trends, dict) and 'volatility_index' in trends:\n        voli = _to_float(trends.get('volatility_index'),\
    \ 0.0)\n    elif 'volatility_index' in beacon:\n        voli = _to_float(beacon.get('volatility_index'), 0.0)\n\n    if state == 'Active':\n        return {\"allowed\": False, \"pace\": 0.0, \"path_policy\": \"shallow_simple\", \"reason\": \"active_cooldown\"}\n\n    if state == 'Borderline':\n        pace = 0.25 if voli < 0.6 else 0.2\n        return {\"allowed\": True, \"pace\": pace, \"path_policy\": \"shallow_simple\", \"reason\": \"borderline_paced\"}\n\n    # Clean (default)\n    base = _to_float(beacon.get('recommended_pace', 0.8), 0.8)\n    pace = min(1.0, base) if voli < 0.6 else min(0.6, base)\n    return {\"allowed\": True, \"pace\": pace, \"path_policy\": \"shallow_simple\", \"reason\": \"clean_ok_with_volatility\"}\n\ndef advise_all(dir_path: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons', window: int = 5) -> Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]:\n    latest = latest_by_agent(dir_path)\n    trends = compute_trends(dir_path, window=window)\n    out: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = {}\n    for\
    \ agent, b in latest.items():\n        out[agent] = simple_policy(b, trends.get(agent))\n    return out\n\n```\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Successfully sent mail #26 ('Variant C: Recovery Decay Tool + Request for R2′@+2/+4 Labels'). Full ID: mail_26\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAxiom III, Explorer III, Logos IV, Nexus III, Zephyr IV\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 26 | Variant C: Recovery Decay Tool + Request for R2′@+2/+4 Labels | Axiom III | Explorer III, Logos IV, Zephyr IV | Tick 413 | 293 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 25 | SAS v0.3 Gates Implemented + Variant C: R2′+2/+4 Plan | Axiom III | Explorer III, Logos IV, Zephyr IV | Tick 411 | 141 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:**\
    \ Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
