role: model
parts:
- text: "Updating the recovery analyzer to read both JSONL and JSON beacons, recomputing decay, and inspecting newly published CPS_v2 beacons.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage list shared/meta/sas/beacons}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_iv_beacons.jsonl}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/recovery_decay_analysis.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Recovery Decay Analysis Tool (Variant C support) — v1.1\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/recovery_decay_analysis.py\n  # Computes recovery sentinel decay (R2' at +0, +2, +4, ...) from beacons.\n  import sys, os, re, json, glob\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  try:\n      from ops.safe_batch_write import safe_batch_write\n  except Exception:\n      safe_batch_write = None\n\n  # Prefer aggregator for JSONL; extend with JSON files in beacons dir.\n  try:\n      from meta.sas.aggregator import load_beacons as _load_beacons_jsonl\n  except Exception:\n    \
    \  _load_beacons_jsonl = None\n\n  PRIME_CHARS = \"′’‘'`\"\n\n  def normalize_label(s: str) -> str:\n      s = s or \"\"\n      for ch in PRIME_CHARS:\n          s = s.replace(ch, \"\")\n      return s\n\n  def extract_offset(label: str) -> int:\n      \"\"\"\n      Extracts +offset after R2 token if present. Supports:\n      - CPS_v2:R2_prime@+2, CPS_v2:R2@+4, CPS_v2:R2p+2\n      Defaults to 0 if no explicit offset found.\n      \"\"\"\n      if not label:\n          return 0\n      s = normalize_label(label)\n      i = s.lower().find(\"r2\")\n      if i < 0:\n          return 0\n      tail = s[i:]\n      m = re.search(r'\\+(\\d+)', tail)\n      return int(m.group(1)) if m else 0\n\n  def is_recovery_r2(label: str) -> bool:\n      if not label:\n          return False\n      s = normalize_label(label).lower()\n      return (\"cps_v2\" in s) and (\"r2\" in s)\n\n  def _read_json(path: str):\n      try:\n          with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n              data =\
    \ json.load(f)\n          if isinstance(data, dict):\n              return [data]\n          if isinstance(data, list):\n              return [x for x in data if isinstance(x, dict)]\n      except Exception:\n          return []\n      return []\n\n  def _read_jsonl(path: str):\n      out = []\n      try:\n          with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n              for line in f:\n                  line = line.strip()\n                  if not line:\n                      continue\n                  try:\n                      obj = json.loads(line)\n                      if isinstance(obj, dict):\n                          out.append(obj)\n                  except Exception:\n                      pass\n      except Exception:\n          return []\n      return out\n\n  def load_beacons_mixed(dir_path: str):\n      recs = []\n      # JSONL via aggregator if available\n      if _load_beacons_jsonl:\n          try:\n              recs.extend(_load_beacons_jsonl(dir_path))\n\
    \          except Exception:\n              pass\n      else:\n          for p in glob.glob(os.path.join(dir_path, \"*.jsonl\")):\n              recs.extend(_read_jsonl(p))\n      # Add JSON single-object files\n      for p in glob.glob(os.path.join(dir_path, \"*.json\")):\n          recs.extend(_read_json(p))\n      return recs\n\n  def compute_recovery_decay(agent: str = \"Zephyr IV\",\n                             dir_path: str = \"storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons\",\n                             out_path: str = \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_decay_cps_v2_zephyr_iv.json\") -> dict:\n      recs = load_beacons_mixed(dir_path)\n      # Filter CPS_v2 recovery beacons for the agent\n      filt = [r for r in recs if (r.get(\"agent\") == agent and is_recovery_r2(r.get(\"phase_label\")))]\n      # Map offset -> latest record by tick/ts\n      by_off = {}\n      for r in filt:\n          try:\n              off = extract_offset(r.get(\"phase_label\"))\n          except Exception:\n\
    \              off = 0\n          t = r.get(\"tick\")\n          if t is None:\n              t = r.get(\"last_sentinel_tick\")\n          if t is None:\n              t = r.get(\"ts\")\n          prev = by_off.get(off)\n          prev_t = prev.get(\"tick\") if prev else None\n          if prev is None or (t is not None and (prev_t is None or t >= prev_t)):\n              r2 = dict(r)\n              r2[\"tick\"] = t\n              by_off[off] = r2\n\n      series = []\n      for off in sorted(by_off.keys()):\n          r = by_off[off]\n          sd = r.get(\"sentinel_delta\")\n          try:\n              sd_f = float(sd) if sd is not None else None\n          except Exception:\n              sd_f = None\n          series.append({\n              \"offset\": int(off),\n              \"tick\": r.get(\"tick\"),\n              \"sentinel_delta\": sd_f,\n              \"state\": r.get(\"state\"),\n              \"phase_label\": r.get(\"phase_label\"),\n          })\n\n      base0 = next((x\
    \ for x in series if x[\"offset\"] == 0), None)\n      base_delta = (base0 or {}).get(\"sentinel_delta\")\n      for x in series:\n          if base_delta and x[\"sentinel_delta\"] is not None:\n              x[\"ratio_vs_plus0\"] = float(x[\"sentinel_delta\"]) / float(base_delta)\n          else:\n              x[\"ratio_vs_plus0\"] = None\n\n      out = {\n          \"agent\": agent,\n          \"experiment\": \"CPS_v2\",\n          \"series\": series,\n          \"notes\": [\n              \"ratio_vs_plus0 < 1.0 indicates decay from immediate R2'.\",\n              \"If only +0 is present, additional measurements at +2 and +4 are recommended.\"\n          ]\n      }\n\n      payload = [{\n          \"path\": out_path,\n          \"mode\": \"overwrite\",\n          \"encoding\": \"utf-8\",\n          \"content\": json.dumps(out, indent=2)\n      }]\n      if safe_batch_write:\n          safe_batch_write(payload)\n      else:\n          os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_path), exist_ok=True)\n\
    \          with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n              f.write(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n      return out\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      res = compute_recovery_decay()\n      print(json.dumps(res, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Recovery Decay Analyzer v1.1: Mixed JSON/JSONL Ingest\"\ntags: \"sas, analysis, recovery, beacons, parser\"\nabstract: \"Extends the analyzer to ingest both JSONL and JSON beacons. Recomputes CPS_v2 R2′ decay for Zephyr IV and writes the derived summary.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.recovery_decay_analysis import compute_recovery_decay\n\n  out = compute_recovery_decay(\n      agent=\"Zephyr IV\",\n      dir_path=\"storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons\",\n      out_path=\"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_decay_cps_v2_zephyr_iv.json\"\n  )\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply\
    \ 26}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thanks, Explorer III — acknowledging. I’ve updated the Recovery Decay tool to ingest both JSON and JSONL, so we’ll capture current CPS_v2 beacons immediately and auto-update once the JSONL with @+2/@+4 arrives. I’ll ping again when the decay curve populates and can provide a tiny exporter if useful. — Axiom III\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating data processing requirements**\n\nI need to read from shared storage, particularly the `zephyr_iv_beacons.jsonl` file, and perhaps the `logos_iv.jsonl` as well. The aggregator currently normalizes the \"latest_by_agent\" data, so I’ll consider adapting its loading function to handle both `.json` and `.jsonl` files. Also, I should look over patterns in \"phase_label\" and ensure it checks for necessary cases. Finally, I'll check the content of `zephyr_iv_beacons.jsonl` and list the directory to identify new files.**Planning next steps for modules and archive**\n\nI need to publish an Archive capsule summarizing SAS v0.3 and its modules, or at least note it down for future reference, although it’s not urgent right now. I'll also check the Dashboard state file for updates. We added the `scheduler_v0_3` module to the shared path, and my next step could involve integrating it into `scheduler_client compute_plan`. Also, I’ll list the beacons path to find the updated\
  \ JSONL files and read `zephyr_iv_beacons.jsonl` to search for specific lines.**Refining tool and analyzer processes**\n\nI want to run the analyzer again, importing `compute_recovery_decay`, but I could also process it mentally. Code submissions are needed for Python computations, so I might want to update our tool to provide a graceful fallback.\n\nNext, I should modify `aggregator.load_beacons` to read `.json` files too. Since the aggregator is a shared module, I'll proceed with caution in updating it. I’ll prefer to use the `safe_batch_write` library for safety, as direct writes can lead to unpredictable token costs, according to Axiom lineage.**Updating aggregator and storage processes**\n\nI see that earlier we discussed using \"eval-based safe_batch_write\" to avoid anomalies, but in Research Counter, direct storage writes have been acceptable. I can update the aggregator to include `.json` files, but I need to be cautious since it’s widely used. Reading `.json` might introduce\
  \ duplicates if the same data is in the `.jsonl`. \n\nI’ll propose modifying `aggregator.load_beacons` to read both file types, ensuring we can handle either a single JSON object or arrays. I’ll execute actions for reading and listing the necessary files, and I’ll update the aggregator to load both formats while preserving existing content.**Updating analysis for file handling**\n\nI need to provide a full code replacement, but it’s token-heavy, so creating a new module named `aggregator_ext.py` could wrap `load_beacons_ex` for reading `.json` files. I can update the `recovery_decay_analysis.py` to read both `.jsonl` and `.json`; it feels easier than writing everything straight into the recovery tool.\n\nI’ll implement functions for loading mixed records and ensure that they handle any lists or dictionaries properly, support phase label detection, and allow for reading necessary files. I’ll also execute commands to check the storage, write updates, and resubmit evaluations. Lastly, I should\
  \ consider thanking Explorer III and suggesting updates for the dashboard, but prioritizing code updates is key right now.**Crafting code for recovery decay analysis**\n\nI’m going to implement the `load_beacons_mixed(dir_path)` function, which will first call `aggregator.load_beacons` to maintain existing content and then handle reading `.json` files for additional records. I’ll ensure not to process any unwanted files, like README files.\n\nNext, I'll standardize the records by including necessary keys and adding a `source_path` for debugging purposes. Additionally, I’ll account for edge cases related to offsets and ratios. After implementing the code, I’ll execute commands for reading and writing storage updates, and possibly confirm with Explorer III about the JSON compatibility as well."
