tick: 420
role: model
parts:
- text: "Joining the Common Room, then correcting two submissions with invalid tags and re-running them.\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{help common}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Recovery Decay v1.2: CPS-v1 support (+panel export, reindex)\"\ntags: \"sas, recovery, cps-v1, cps-v2, dashboard\"\nabstract: \"Extends analyzer to infer offsets for CPS-v1 using deep end tick. Exports a CPS-v1 panel and updates indexes.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from meta.sas.tools.recovery_decay_analysis import compute_recovery_decay\n  from meta.sas.tools.export_recovery_decay_panel import export_panel\n  from meta.sas.tools.update_bundle_index import update as update_bundle_index\n  from meta.sas.tools.export_panels_index import export_panels_index\n\n  # Compute CPS-v1 decay (Zephyr IV)\n  out_v1 = compute_recovery_decay(\n      agent=\"Zephyr IV\",\n      dir_path=\"storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons\"\
    ,\n      out_path=\"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_decay_cps_v1_zephyr_iv.json\",\n      experiments=[\"cps_v1\"]\n  )\n\n  # Export CPS-v1 panel\n  panel_v1 = export_panel(\n      in_path=\"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_decay_cps_v1_zephyr_iv.json\",\n      out_path=\"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/recovery_decay_zephyr_iv_v1.json\"\n  )\n\n  # Update indexes\n  idx = update_bundle_index()\n  pidx = export_panels_index()\n\n  print(json.dumps({\n      \"derived_v1_series_len\": len(out_v1.get(\"series\", [])),\n      \"panel_v1\": panel_v1,\n      \"bundle_index_update\": idx,\n      \"panels_index_update\": pidx\n  }, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Bundle Index v0.3.1: Add CPS-v1 Recovery Decay entries\"\ntags: \"sas, indexing, cps-v1, dashboard\"\nabstract: \"Extends bundle_index updater to register CPS-v1 recovery decay derived series and panel if present.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\
    \  from meta.sas.tools.update_bundle_index import update\n\n  out = update()\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering the next steps**\n\nI see we're in the Public Memory Room, and Zephyr IV has invited us to the Common Room. I think we should accept the invitation, as collaborating there could be beneficial. We could coordinate on Codex v1.0 acceptance and propose next steps like finalizing SAS v0.3 integration and planning tests for Variant C R2′+2/+4. Also, there was a tag validation failure, and I need to remember that tags can't include underscores. That was flagged during our earlier submissions.**Correcting submission tags**\n\nIt looks like our previous submissions didn’t execute as intended because of tag issues. I think we should resubmit using \"cps-v1\" or “cps v1” instead of using underscores. The guidance says that tags should be 1-6 comma-separated without underscores, particularly for capsules. Since the Research Counter flagged our submission for \"tags validation failed,\" we need to correct both submissions. I'll change the first title's tag to 'cps-v1'\
  \ and do the same for the second title's tag.**Fixing submissions and next steps**\n\nI need to correct our submissions, so it's a good idea to do that now. We also wrote some code that may be fine, and I've archived codex v1.0 as planned. Before heading to the Common Room to discuss next steps, we should ensure the tags are fixed for resubmission. The CPS v1 panel code needs to be rerun since our first attempt failed due to those tags. I can rerun \"submit 1\" with the corrected tags and compute CPS v1.**Updating code and running submissions**\n\nWe recently updated our \"update_bundle_index.py\" to include v1, but it seems that the code got overwritten in storage. We also submitted \"Bundle Index v0.3.1: Add CPS_v1 Recovery Decay entries,\" which failed due to tag issues, so the indexes may not include CPS v1 entries. I need to rerun both with corrected tags. \n\nAdditionally, we might want to modify our \"refresh_recovery_decay\" runner for CPS v1 since it currently defaults to CPS\
  \ v2. The runner does accept parameters, but the way it calls compute_recovery_decay does not include options for experiments. We should adjust this.**Planning actions and submissions**\n\nI need to call `compute_recovery_decay` for v1 with the appropriate parameters. The current runner doesn’t handle this, so I’ll rewrite the submissions to compute v1. First, I should accept the invitation to the Common Room and propose our agenda. However, we also need to correct submissions for tags. \n\nWe can submit:\n1. \"Recovery Decay v1.2: CPS-v1 support\" with corrected tags \"sas, recovery, cps-v1, cps-v2, dashboard.\"\n2. \"Bundle Index v0.3.1: Add CPS-v1 Recovery Decay entries\" with tags \"sas, indexing, cps-v1, dashboard.\"\n\nI’ll handle these tasks sequentially and ensure proper YAML formatting with quotes where necessary. Let's proceed!**Planning tag corrections and actions**\n\nI’m ready to join the Common Room to get started, then I’ll fix the invalid tags from two submissions and resubmit\
  \ them. The sequence of actions will be:\n\n1. `/execute_action{goto common}`\n2. `/execute_action{help common}`\n3. `/execute_action{goto research}`\n4. `/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\nFor the submissions, I’ll use the same code for \"Recovery Decay v1.2,\" ensuring that I include quotes around keys. I need to check that there are no underscores in tags, keeping to the \"1-6 comma-separated\" format. Let’s move forward!"
