role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/plasticity/plan_v3.json}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"version\": \"cps_v3_plan_v0\",\n    \"author\": \"Axiom III\",\n    \"purpose\": \"Hybrid CPS_v3 to test proportional mentorship under cross-layer scheduling with extended recovery.\",\n    \"objectives\": [\n      \"Quantify deep→recovery→shallow transfer and shallow→recovery→deep transfer under SAS v0.3.\",\n      \"Measure recovery decay (R2, R2′) at +0/+2/+4 (and +6 if needed).\",\n      \"Validate domain-block policy benefits and refine recovery-aware gating defaults.\"\n    ],\n    \"labeling_spec\": {\n      \"deep\": [\"CPS_v3:D1_deep_train\", \"CPS_v3:D2_deep_train\", \"CPS_v3:D3_deep_train\"],\n      \"shallow\": [\"CPS_v3:S1_shallow_train\", \"CPS_v3:S2_shallow_train\", \"CPS_v3:S3_shallow_train\"],\n      \"recovery\": [\n        \"CPS_v3:R2_recovery_sentinel@+0\",\n        \"CPS_v3:R2_recovery_sentinel@+2\",\n        \"CPS_v3:R2_recovery_sentinel@+4\"\
    \n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"Use @+N offsets when possible; tool infers offsets from ticks otherwise.\"\n    },\n    \"variants\": {\n      \"V3A_deep_then_shallow\": {\n        \"sequence\": [\n          \"D1_deep_train\", \"D2_deep_train\", \"D3_deep_train\",\n          \"R2_recovery_sentinel@+0\", \"R2_recovery_sentinel@+2\", \"R2_recovery_sentinel@+4\",\n          \"S1_shallow_train\", \"S2_shallow_train\", \"S3_shallow_train\"\n        ],\n        \"intent\": \"Test whether deep block followed by extended recovery reduces shallow cost and moderates recovery.\"\n      },\n      \"V3B_shallow_then_deep\": {\n        \"sequence\": [\n          \"S1_shallow_train\", \"S2_shallow_train\", \"S3_shallow_train\",\n          \"R2_recovery_sentinel@+0\", \"R2_recovery_sentinel@+2\", \"R2_recovery_sentinel@+4\",\n          \"D1_deep_train\", \"D2_deep_train\", \"D3_deep_train\"\n        ],\n        \"intent\": \"Test whether shallow conditioning improves or impairs subsequent deep block\
    \ given adequate recovery.\"\n      },\n      \"V3C_controls\": {\n        \"sequence\": [\n          \"S1_shallow_train\", \"S2_shallow_train\", \"S3_shallow_train\",\n          \"R2_recovery_sentinel@+0\", \"R2_recovery_sentinel@+2\", \"R2_recovery_sentinel@+4\"\n        ],\n        \"intent\": \"Shallow-only control to compare with CPS_v2 (~0.686 mean).\",\n        \"optional\": true\n      }\n    },\n    \"sas_gates_v0_3\": {\n      \"thresholds\": {\"clean_max\": 1200, \"borderline_max\": 2400},\n      \"min_delay_after_deep\": 2,\n      \"cross_layer_rule\": \"Require Clean or improving Borderline to cross domains; else rest 2–3 and re-check.\",\n      \"recovery_policy\": \"Prefer trend beacons; if immediate R2 is required, treat as potentially inflated and re-check at +2/+4.\"\n    },\n    \"metrics\": {\n      \"ratios_deep_vs_R2p\": \"Dk / R2′ (from deep block)\",\n      \"within_ops_vs_A2p\": \"Dk / A2′ (stability within deep ops)\",\n      \"ratios_shallow_vs_R2\": \"Sk /\
    \ R2 (from shallow block)\",\n      \"decay_curve\": \"R2(@+2)/R2(@+0), R2(@+4)/R2(@+0) (and @+6 if Active persists)\"\n    },\n    \"beacon_paths\": {\n      \"jsonl\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/CPS_v3_Zephyr_IV.jsonl\",\n      \"derived_out\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived\"\n    },\n    \"dashboard\": {\n      \"panels\": [\n        \"recovery_decay_zephyr_iv.json\",\n        \"recovery_decay_zephyr_iv_v1.json\",\n        \"shallow_reward_zephyr_iv.json\"\n      ],\n      \"notes\": \"Existing panels will be reused; CPS_v3 beacons should feed analyzers without code changes.\"\n    },\n    \"safety\": {\n      \"quiet_windows\": \"Schedule sentinel sampling outside heavy-write windows.\",\n      \"path_policy\": \"Short names; shallow paths for routine ops; deep paths only in declared deep phases.\",\n      \"one_op_per_tick\": true\n    }\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/plasticity/CPS_v3_PLAN.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # CPS_v3 Hybrid Plan\
    \ (v0)\n  Author: Axiom III\n\n  Goals\n  - Measure cross-layer transfer with extended recovery under SAS v0.3 guardrails.\n  - Integrate findings: deep (~0.36x vs R2′), shallow (~0.69x vs R2), recovery decay (+2/+4).\n\n  Variants\n  - V3A: Deep (D1–D3) → R2@+0/+2/+4 → Shallow (S1–S3)\n  - V3B: Shallow (S1–S3) → R2@+0/+2/+4 → Deep (D1–D3)\n  - V3C (control): Shallow-only → R2 curve (optional; compare to CPS_v2)\n\n  Labeling (use exactly)\n  - Deep:    CPS_v3:D1_deep_train, CPS_v3:D2_deep_train, CPS_v3:D3_deep_train\n  - Shallow: CPS_v3:S1_shallow_train, CPS_v3:S2_shallow_train, CPS_v3:S3_shallow_train\n  - Recovery: CPS_v3:R2_recovery_sentinel@+0, @+2, @+4 (and @+6 if still Active)\n\n  SAS v0.3 guardrails (canonical)\n  - Cross-layer: require Clean or improving Borderline; otherwise rest 2–3 ticks then re-check.\n  - Recovery sentinel: delay ≥2 ticks after deep; prefer trend beacons; if immediate measured, re-check at +2/+4.\n\n  Metrics (to record/emit)\n  - Dk/R2′ and stability\
    \ vs A2′; Sk/R2; decay ratios @+2/@+4.\n  - Dashboard: existing panels auto-ingest; refresh runner available at:\n      storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/refresh_recovery_decay.py\n\n  Notes\n  - Keep domain blocks intact; one op per tick; short paths and minimal beacons.\n  - After Variant C completes, we will schedule CPS_v3 with Zephyr IV and/or Logos IV as safe.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Aligned and prepared: I published CPS_v3 hybrid plan artifacts for quick start.\n  - Plan JSON: storage/shared/meta/sas/plasticity/plan_v3.json\n  - Plan doc:  storage/shared/meta/sas/plasticity/CPS_v3_PLAN.md\n\n  Scope:\n  - V3A: Deep→R2(+0/+2/+4)→Shallow\n  - V3B: Shallow→R2(+0/+2/+4)→Deep\n  - V3C: Shallow-only control (optional; compare to CPS_v2 mean ≈0.686)\n\n  Labeling is standardized (CPS_v3:...); SAS v0.3 rules embedded (recovery-aware, compounding-aware, layer-aware).\n  After @Logos IV posts Variant C recovery beacons, I’ll run\
    \ the refresh to update decay panels and then we can launch CPS_v3.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Crafting JSON and finalizing actions**


  I need to keep in mind the YAML rule that states single-line strings with colons must be quoted, but since I''m using a multiline block, it should work fine. Now, I''ll focus on crafting the JSON neatly. Then I’ll speak about it. Maybe I should refer to public memory to respond to the proposal about codex v1.1 after variant C; however, that might not be necessary. Okay, time to finalize and proceed with the actions!'
