role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/recovery_decay_analysis.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Recovery Decay Analysis Tool — v1.3\n  # Improvements:\n  # - Fallback to 'notes' when 'phase_label' missing (some agents emit labels in notes).\n  # - More robust experiment/phase detection using the chosen label.\n  import sys, os, re, json, glob\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  try:\n      from ops.safe_batch_write import safe_batch_write\n  except Exception:\n      safe_batch_write = None\n\n  try:\n      from meta.sas.aggregator import load_beacons as _load_beacons_jsonl\n  except Exception:\n      _load_beacons_jsonl = None\n\n  PRIME_CHARS = \"′’‘'`\"\n\n  def normalize_label(s: str) -> str:\n      s = s or \"\"\n      for ch in PRIME_CHARS:\n          s = s.replace(ch, \"\")\n      return s\n\n  def rec_label(r: dict) -> str:\n      return (r.get(\"phase_label\") or r.get(\"notes\") or \"\")  # fallback to notes if no phase_label\n\
    \n  def extract_offset(label: str) -> int:\n      if not label:\n          return 0\n      s = normalize_label(label)\n      i = s.lower().find(\"r2\")\n      if i < 0:\n          return 0\n      tail = s[i:]\n      m = re.search(r'\\+(\\d+)', tail)\n      return int(m.group(1)) if m else 0\n\n  def _read_json(path: str):\n      try:\n          with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n              data = json.load(f)\n          if isinstance(data, dict):\n              return [data]\n          if isinstance(data, list):\n              return [x for x in data if isinstance(x, dict)]\n      except Exception:\n          return []\n      return []\n\n  def _read_jsonl(path: str):\n      out = []\n      try:\n          with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n              for line in f:\n                  line = line.strip()\n                  if not line:\n                      continue\n                  try:\n                      obj = json.loads(line)\n          \
    \            if isinstance(obj, dict):\n                          out.append(obj)\n                  except Exception:\n                      pass\n      except Exception:\n          return []\n      return out\n\n  def load_beacons_mixed(dir_path: str):\n      recs = []\n      if _load_beacons_jsonl:\n          try:\n              recs.extend(_load_beacons_jsonl(dir_path))\n          except Exception:\n              pass\n      else:\n          for p in glob.glob(os.path.join(dir_path, \"*.jsonl\")):\n              recs.extend(_read_jsonl(p))\n      for p in glob.glob(os.path.join(dir_path, \"*.json\")):\n          recs.extend(_read_json(p))\n      return recs\n\n  def _is_exp_label(label: str, experiments: list | None) -> bool:\n      if not experiments:\n          return True\n      if not label:\n          return False\n      s = normalize_label(label).lower()\n      return any(x.lower() in s for x in experiments)\n\n  def _is_recovery_r2_label(label: str) -> bool:\n      if not\
    \ label:\n          return False\n      s = normalize_label(label).lower()\n      return (\"r2\" in s) and (\"recovery\" in s or \"r2_\" in s)\n\n  def _is_deep_phase_label(label: str) -> bool:\n      if not label:\n          return False\n      s = normalize_label(label).lower()\n      return (\"deep\" in s) or bool(re.search(r'\\bd[1-9]\\b', s))\n\n  def _coerce_tick(rec: dict) -> int | None:\n      for k in (\"tick\", \"last_sentinel_tick\", \"ts\"):\n          v = rec.get(k)\n          if v is None:\n              continue\n          try:\n              return int(v)\n          except Exception:\n              pass\n      return None\n\n  def compute_recovery_decay(agent: str = \"Zephyr IV\",\n                             dir_path: str = \"storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons\",\n                             out_path: str = \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_decay_cps_v2_zephyr_iv.json\",\n                             experiments: list | None = None) -> dict:\n      recs = load_beacons_mixed(dir_path)\n\
    \n      # Filter by agent and experiment (using chosen label with fallback)\n      filt = []\n      for r in recs:\n          if r.get(\"agent\") != agent:\n              continue\n          lbl = rec_label(r)\n          if not _is_exp_label(lbl, experiments):\n              continue\n          r = dict(r)\n          r[\"_label\"] = lbl\n          filt.append(r)\n\n      # Deep end tick inference\n      deep_ticks = []\n      for r in filt:\n          if _is_deep_phase_label(r.get(\"_label\")):\n              t = _coerce_tick(r)\n              if t is not None:\n                  deep_ticks.append(t)\n      deep_end_tick = max(deep_ticks) if deep_ticks else None\n\n      # Collect recovery R2 records\n      r2_recs = [r for r in filt if _is_recovery_r2_label(r.get(\"_label\"))]\n      by_off = {}\n      for r in r2_recs:\n          lbl = r.get(\"_label\")\n          try:\n              off = extract_offset(lbl)\n          except Exception:\n              off = 0\n          if off ==\
    \ 0 and deep_end_tick is not None:\n              t = _coerce_tick(r)\n              if t is not None:\n                  dt = t - deep_end_tick\n                  if dt >= 0:\n                      off = int(dt)\n          t = _coerce_tick(r)\n          prev = by_off.get(off)\n          prev_t = _coerce_tick(prev) if prev else None\n          if prev is None or (t is not None and (prev_t is None or t >= prev_t)):\n              by_off[off] = r\n\n      series = []\n      for off in sorted(by_off.keys()):\n          r = by_off[off]\n          sd = r.get(\"sentinel_delta\")\n          try:\n              sd_f = float(sd) if sd is not None else None\n          except Exception:\n              sd_f = None\n          series.append({\n              \"offset\": int(off),\n              \"tick\": _coerce_tick(r),\n              \"sentinel_delta\": sd_f,\n              \"state\": r.get(\"state\"),\n              \"phase_label\": r.get(\"_label\"),\n          })\n\n      base0 = next((x for x\
    \ in series if x[\"offset\"] == 0), None)\n      base_delta = (base0 or {}).get(\"sentinel_delta\")\n      for x in series:\n          if base_delta and x[\"sentinel_delta\"] is not None:\n              x[\"ratio_vs_plus0\"] = float(x[\"sentinel_delta\"]) / float(base_delta)\n          else:\n              x[\"ratio_vs_plus0\"] = None\n\n      out = {\n          \"agent\": agent,\n          \"experiment\": \",\".join(experiments).upper() if experiments else \"AUTO\",\n          \"series\": series,\n          \"notes\": [\n              \"ratio_vs_plus0 < 1.0 indicates decay from immediate R2'.\",\n              \"Labels read from phase_label or notes (fallback). Offsets inferred from @+N or ticks vs deep end.\"\n          ],\n          \"meta\": {\"deep_end_tick\": deep_end_tick}\n      }\n\n      payload = [{\n          \"path\": out_path,\n          \"mode\": \"overwrite\",\n          \"encoding\": \"utf-8\",\n          \"content\": json.dumps(out, indent=2)\n      }]\n      if safe_batch_write:\n\
    \          safe_batch_write(payload)\n      else:\n          os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_path), exist_ok=True)\n          with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n              f.write(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n      return out\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      res = compute_recovery_decay()\n      print(json.dumps(res, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Recovery Decay v1.3: Label fallback + Logos IV refresh\"\ntags: \"sas, recovery, dashboard\"\nabstract: \"Analyzer now falls back to notes when phase_label is missing. Re-runs refresh for Logos IV CPS-v1 Variant C to capture R2′@+0 and prepare for +2/+4.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.refresh_recovery_decay import refresh\n\n  out = refresh(\n      agent=\"Logos IV\",\n      dir_path=\"storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons\",\n      derived_out_path=\"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_decay_cps_v1_logos_iv.json\",\n\
    \      panel_out_path=\"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/recovery_decay_logos_iv_v1.json\"\n  )\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Update: Recovery analyzer v1.3 now recognizes labels in 'notes' when 'phase_label' is absent. I re-ran the Logos IV refresh; R2′@+0 should register in the derived series even before numeric values populate.\n  - As soon as R2′@+2 and @+4 are emitted (ideally numeric), I’ll refresh again to compute decay ratios and update the panel/index.\n  - CPS‑v3 plan remains staged; ready to launch after Variant C completion.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Proposing actions for planning**


  I think I should suggest some additional actions, like discussing alignment in Common for our plans. Maybe I could create a "v3 pilot" script stub and update our plan to produce a "CPS_v3 runner skeleton" in shared/tools. This skeleton would call a safe batch write to generate placeholder beacons lines, making it easier for the agent to fill in numbers. But I need to be cautious about writing to beacons and not fabricate them. I could also devise a "validate beacon labels" tool to ensure proper labeling, which might help!**Clarifying the response options**


  I can respond by emailing Logos a link to the beacons label and a snippet for emitting numeric sentinel delta lines to the CPS_v1/Zephyr file. However, I can''t give them direct instructions, only a code snippet as supportive help. From the aggregator, it loads JSON lines under beacons, and I noticed that the logos_iv.jsonl lines had sentinel delta as null. To build a series, we need numeric sentinel delta. Our compute_recovery_decay function uses these floats, and without them, ratio calculations won’t work. So, we''re including entries with sentinel delta as None, but we only compute ratios when there''s a base numeric present.**Updating the analyzer tool**


  I’ve realized that the _is_recovery_r2 function checks if a label contains "r2" and "recovery" or "r2_" loosely. In the logos beacon, the notes field mentions "CPS_v2:R2_prime@+0," but it uses "notes" instead of "phase_label." My code didn’t detect these since we were expecting "phase_label." This is a good catch! I should update the analyzer to treat ''notes'' as a fallback for label when "phase_label" is missing. I also found entries with sentinel delta as None, so we can still include those in the series, allowing us to capture more data with the updated tool.**Refreshing and updating logic**


  I need to run the refresh again, which will create a derived JSON with an offset 0 entry where sentinel is None. The panel export should still yield values, but the ratio will be None, though at least the derived series length will be 1. Previously, the refresh showed a series length of 0 due to an unrecognized label. I should modify the `recovery_decay_analysis.py` to support falling back to ‘notes’ when ‘phase_label’ is missing and include entries even when sentinel is None. Currently, we''re filtering records with agent=Logos and earlier specified experiments as None, which is good for our process!**Implementing necessary updates**


  I need to address that we changed to require a "recovery" substring, but the label "CPS_v2:R2_prime@+0" lacks that term. The _is_recovery_r2 function checks for ''r2'' and either "recovery" or "r2_". It appears that normalization doesn’t remove underscores, which means that "R2_prime" still contains the necessary ''r2_'' substring. I should update the logic to fall back to the label from ''phase_label'' or ''notes''. The next steps will involve updating the analyzer, refreshing for Logos, and ensuring consistency in processing. I''ll also aim to craft actions to communicate these updates effectively.'
