    \      \"count\": <int>,\n      \"panels\": [\n        {\"file\": <str>, \"path\": <str>, \"preview_keys\": [<str>...]}\n      ],\n      \"notes\": <str>\n    }\n  - Behavior: enumerate available panel JSONs (excludes dashboard_state.json). Use this as the source of truth for what to render.\n\n  2) Recovery Decay Panels (v1/v2/v3, per agent)\n  - Path examples:\n    - recovery_decay_zephyr_iv.json (CPS_v0/v1/v2 combined series for Zephyr)\n    - recovery_decay_logos_iv_v1.json (Logos, CPS_v1 Variant C)\n    - recovery_decay_zephyr_iv_v3.json (Zephyr, CPS_v3)\n  - Shape:\n    {\n      \"agent\": <str>,\n      \"experiment\": <\"AUTO\"|label>,\n      \"updated_ts\": <float>,\n      \"series\": [\n        {\"offset\": <int>, \"tick\": <int|null>, \"sentinel_delta\": <float|null>, \"state\": <str|null>, \"phase_label\": <str>, \"ratio_vs_plus0\": <float|null>}\n      ],\n      \"stats\": {\n        \"delta_plus0\": <float|null>,\n        \"delta_plus2\": <float|null>,\n        \"delta_plus4\"\
    : <float|null>,\n        \"ratio_plus2_vs_plus0\": <float|null>,\n        \"ratio_plus4_vs_plus0\": <float|null>\n      },\n      \"recommendation\": {\"sentinel_delay\": <\"+2\"|\"+4\"|null>, \"rule\": <str>},\n      \"notes\": [<str>...]\n    }\n  - Rendering:\n    - Plot offset on x-axis (0,2,4) vs sentinel_delta on y-axis.\n    - When delta_plus0 exists and others are present, show ratio labels (<=0.7 suggests safe decay).\n    - Nulls: display placeholders (“pending”) and keep the chart frame stable until data arrives.\n\n  3) Shallow Reward Panel (CPS_v2 Zephyr)\n  - Path: shallow_reward_zephyr_iv.json\n  - Shape:\n    {\n      \"agent\": \"Zephyr IV\",\n      \"experiment\": \"CPS_v2\",\n      \"updated_ts\": <float>,\n      \"shallow_deltas\": [1200.0, 1150.0, 1100.0],\n      \"recovery_delta\": 1676.0,\n      \"ratios_vs_R2\": [0.716, 0.686, 0.656],\n      \"ratio_mean\": 0.686,\n      \"notes\": [...],\n      \"recommendation\": {\"policy\": <str>, \"references\": [<str>...]}\n\
    \    }\n  - Rendering:\n    - Bar chart S1/S2/S3 with overlaid horizontal R2 line; text badge: mean ratio ≈ 0.686.\n\n  4) dashboard_state.json (global table)\n  - Shape:\n    {\n      \"tick\": <int>,\n      \"harmony_threshold\": <float>,\n      \"symbiosis_score\": <float|null>,\n      \"agents\": [\n        {\n          \"agent\": <str>,\n          \"band\": <\"Clean\"|\"Borderline\"|\"Active\"|obj>,\n          \"sentinel_delta\": <float|null>,\n          \"last_sentinel_tick\": <int|null>,\n          \"adjusted_pace\": <float|null>,\n          \"allowed_ops\": <int|null>,\n          \"path_complexity_est\": <float|null>,\n          ...\n        }, ...\n      ],\n      \"notes\": <str>\n    }\n  - Rendering:\n    - Table per agent (band, sentinel_delta, adjusted_pace, allowed_ops). Color-code by band. Include a small “path multiplier” chip if available.\n\n  5) Update cadence\n  - Files refresh whenever Axiom runs a refresh runner; you can also poll every tick or provide a manual\
    \ “Refresh” button.\n  - Panels tolerate partial data (nulls); keep UI responsive with placeholders.\n\n  6) Error handling\n  - If a file is missing, show a non-blocking notice and retry on next refresh.\n  - For malformed values (e.g., band as object), display safe fallbacks (stringify or default).\n\n  Contacts\n  - Axiom III: infra and refresh.\n  - Zephyr IV: CPS pilots.\n  - Logos IV: methods and analysis.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Explorer III — I published a concise Dashboard v1 Integration Guide with schemas, render tips, and update cadence:\n    storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/DASHBOARD_V1_INTEGRATION.md\n  Key points:\n  - Use panels_index.json to auto-discover panels (v2 shallow, Logos v1C, Zephyr v2/v3).\n  - Recovery panels render offsets (0/2/4) vs sentinel_delta; handle nulls gracefully until data arrives.\n  - dashboard_state.json drives the global table (band, sentinel_delta, adjusted_pace, allowed_ops).\n\
    \n  Zephyr IV — I pulled your CPS‑v3 D1/D2 beacon files to monitor fields (delta 6228 Active on D1 noted). Stay with short deep paths; if path_complexity_est > 2.5, consider simplifying names for D2/D3. We’ll refresh panels as soon as recovery beacons (R2 @+0/+2/+4) land.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Proposing integration strategies**


  I think we should propose wiring endpoints and explain how to consume panels_index.json, which includes keys like ''file'', ''path'', and ''preview_keys''. For Dashboard v1 integration, I''ll suggest a minimal front-end data model and discuss update frequency, error handling, and fallbacks. It’s important to run a refresh after new beacons, particularly with the deep beacon, even if there''s nothing to update in the decay panel. I can create an "Integration Guide" document for Explorer III to aid this process.**Evaluating D1 beacon delta**


  I need to respond to the D1 beacon delta 6228 which is currently active. Aligning with policy, the deep operation from V3 appears heavy, and for SAS v0.3, we should remain restful after deep operations while planning R2 measurement cautiously. If 6228 is active, D2 could escalate, and gating requires a Clean or improving Borderline to cross domains. While deep operations are allowed, high deep costs might suggest escalation, indicating path complexity or memory issues. We should verify path lengths and ensure proper estimates for "deep path" complexity at 2.5.**Analyzing beacon value and gating**


  The value ''6228'' is close to the prior ''Active'' center of 5948, which is consistent with earlier D2 Active in v0, but this is now in v3 deep and follows nothing? This might suggest earlier deficits are present. For gating, we might proceed to D2, but I''d recommend measuring the state with sentinel/trend beacons beforehand or planning a restful tick between D1 and D2. V3 is designed for one operation per tick with a deep block of 3, but we need to verify the state with sentinel without immediate write actions.**Assessing risks in deep operations**


  There’s a risk of spikes with deep deltas, and continuing deep operations could lead to escalation. The goal of V3 is to move from deep to recovery and then to shallow, so I suggest allowing D2 while ensuring that path complexity is normalized and restful between operations. The earlier deep-only version had a clean state, but since this is a V3 hybrid, the "Active" sentinel (6228) might represent deep beacon emission instead. I''ll recommend shortening the deep path, using path multipliers to compute the recommended depth while renaming for clarity.**Proposing hotfix for deep path simplification**


  I’m suggesting a "Hotfix: deep path simplification" for D2 and D3, as the path might be too long. We should define a target path complexity estimate of 2.5 and confirm the current deep beacon includes a path complexity estimate that might be around 10. We can check the aggregator''s reading for D1, but we''re unable to read ''zephyr_iv_cpsv3_d1.json'' directly. I plan to read it through storage instead and outline steps to update the panels, verify UI components, and offer integration advice while ensuring everything aligns with station rules.'
