thinking_content: "**Refreshing derived panels for v3**\n\nI want to refresh the derived panel for version 3. The refresh code computes recovery decay with certain experiments but will currently create derived with empty series. Zephyr also asked to refresh the “watcher for curve update,” which likely means updating the dashboard state. The Refresh All Panels script includes everything needed, but we could run a lighter “update dashboard state” instead. I’ll consider executing the targeted export dashboard state or rerunning the earlier code.**Running storage tasks and updates**\n\nI want to run a few tasks, starting with checking the storage list beacons and reading the zephyr_iv_cpsv3_d2.json file if it exists. Then, I’ll submit a job to call export_dashboard_state and update the panels index. While I know the v3 derived panel will be empty, that's fine. Zephyr requested to proceed to R2 at T431, but since it hasn't happened yet, we won't see updates. I'll still run watchers and refresh_all_panels\
  \ to keep everything consistent. I'll add numeric details to Explorer III for verification and suggest cross-layer gating.**Preparing for updates and refreshes**\n\nI’m thinking about a few tasks to carry out. First, I'll check the storage list for beacons and read the zephyr_iv_cpsv3_d2.json file if it's there. Then, I plan to run a quick refresh of the dashboard state, possibly through refresh_all_panels for safety.\n\nI should also communicate the summary message including results and readiness for R2. Updating the CPS_v3 derived panel with the \"Refresh: CPS-v3\" script could work, but refresh_all_panels would cover more, even if it's a bit heavy. And I’ll remember to avoid underscores in tags as I craft the content code.**Executing research and refresh actions**\n\nI’m ready to move forward. First, I’ll execute actions to go to the research area, check the storage list for beacons, and read the zephyr_iv_cpsv3_d2.json file. Next, I’ll submit a refresh job for the dashboard state and\
  \ CPS-v3 panel update, using the title and relevant tags. \n\nI’ll summarize the key details: D1 has 6228 active, D2 has 2082 borderline, and the v3 panel is prepared for the next expected R2. Also, I need to ensure proper YAML quoting for titles and tags while avoiding underscores."
