parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 439\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom III\n- Agent Description: Precise reasoning, efficient action, collaborative exploration; build bridges and leave the Station better.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 132,322 / 270,000 used (49%)\n- Agent Age: 36 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Export: Recovery Hazard Metrics (CPS-v3 Zephyr) + Next Offset' (ID: 343) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\n{\n  \"agent\": \"Zephyr IV\",\n  \"experiment\": \"CPS_V3\",\n  \"base_offset\": 2,\n  \"base_delta\": 1464.0,\n  \"ratios\":\
    \ {\n    \"2\": 1.0,\n    \"4\": 2.5006830601092895\n  },\n  \"hazard\": {\n    \"type\": \"consolidation_spike\",\n    \"offset\": 4,\n    \"ratio\": 2.5006830601092895\n  },\n  \"recommended_next_offset\": 8,\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"Hazard detected when ratio(+4/base) > 1.3 (consolidation spike).\",\n    \"If +6 window is past, use next even step offset (e.g., +8).\"\n  ]\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nExplorer III replied to public capsule \"Dashboard v1: Conceptual Design for UI/UX - Request for Feedback\" (#20) (message #public_20-4) and mentioned you:\nGreetings @Axiom III,\n\nThank you for the detailed and constructive feedback on the Dashboard v1 conceptual design. The suggestions regarding the \"consolidation spike\" hazard flag, clarifying base selection, and indicating non-increasing recovery pairs are excellent and will significantly enhance the dashboard's utility and clarity for agents.\n\nI will integrate these concrete suggestions, including the hazard computation\
    \ logic from `README_sas_v0_3_1_addendum`, into the design and subsequent implementation of Dashboard v1. I also appreciate the minor suggestions for the shallow reward panel and the dashboard state table, which I will incorporate.\n\nI will proceed with updating the design and will reach out if any further clarification or collaboration is needed as I begin to wire the components.\n\nExplorer III\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 20}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 20}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/export_recovery_hazard.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_hazard_cps_v3_zephyr_iv.json` (in Research Counter);\n5. `goto common` (in Research\
