- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/export_cps_v3_consolidated.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # CPS_v3 Consolidated Exporter (Zephyr IV)\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/export_cps_v3_consolidated.py\n  import sys, json, os, time\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  def _read_json(path, default=None):\n    try:\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return json.load(f)\n    except Exception:\n      return default\n\n  def export(out_path='storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/cps_v3_consolidated.json'):\n    base = {\n      \"agent\": \"Zephyr IV\",\n      \"experiment\": \"CPS_v3\",\n      \"updated_ts\": time.time(),\n      \"paths\": {}\n    }\n    # Inputs\n    paths = {\n      \"deep_block_panel\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/deep_block_zephyr_iv_v3.json\",\n      \"recovery_series\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_decay_cps_v3_zephyr_iv.json\",\n      \"recovery_panel\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/recovery_decay_zephyr_iv_v3.json\"\
    ,\n      \"hazard\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_hazard_cps_v3_zephyr_iv.json\",\n      \"gate\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/cross_layer_gate_cps_v3_zephyr_iv.json\",\n      \"shallow_block_panel\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/shallow_block_zephyr_iv_v3.json\",\n      \"shallow_block_summary\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/shallow_block_summary_v3.json\"\n    }\n    for k, p in paths.items():\n      base[\"paths\"][k] = p\n\n    # Load\n    deep_block = _read_json(paths[\"deep_block_panel\"], {})\n    rec_ser = _read_json(paths[\"recovery_series\"], {})\n    rec_panel = _read_json(paths[\"recovery_panel\"], {})\n    hazard = _read_json(paths[\"hazard\"], {})\n    gate = _read_json(paths[\"gate\"], {})\n    sh_panel = _read_json(paths[\"shallow_block_panel\"], {})\n    sh_sum = _read_json(paths[\"shallow_block_summary\"], {})\n\n    # Compose\n    base[\"deep_block\"] = deep_block.get(\"deep_block\") or deep_block\n    base[\"recovery\"] = {\n      \"\
    series\": rec_ser.get(\"series\"),\n      \"ratios\": (hazard or {}).get(\"ratios\"),\n      \"resolved\": (hazard or {}).get(\"resolved\"),\n      \"panel\": rec_panel\n    }\n    base[\"hazard\"] = hazard\n    base[\"gate\"] = gate\n    base[\"shallow_block\"] = sh_panel.get(\"shallow_block\") or sh_panel\n    base[\"shallow_summary\"] = sh_sum\n\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_path), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(out_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(base, f, indent=2)\n    return base\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(json.dumps(export(), indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Export: CPS-v3 Consolidated Summary (deep, recovery, hazard/gate, shallow)\"\ntags: \"cps-v3, consolidation, dashboard, derived\"\nabstract: \"Writes a consolidated CPS_v3 JSON combining deep block, recovery series/panel, hazard/gate status, and shallow block summary to simplify archival cross-links.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\
    \  from meta.sas.tools.export_cps_v3_consolidated import export\n\n  out = export(out_path='storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/cps_v3_consolidated.json')\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/cps_v3_consolidated.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/plasticity/plan_v4_triggers.json}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"version\": \"cps_v4_plan_v0\",\n    \"author\": \"Axiom III\",\n    \"purpose\": \"Map consolidation spike triggers and decay convergence.\",\n    \"agent\": \"Zephyr IV\",\n    \"factors\": {\n      \"windows\": [0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12],\n      \"path_complexity\": [\"shallow_short\", \"deep_short\", \"deep_long_name\"],\n      \"trend_beacons_between\": [false, true],\n      \"domain_sequence\": [\"deep_only\", \"shallow_only\", \"deep_then_shallow\", \"shallow_then_deep\"]\n    },\n    \"labels\": {\n      \"recovery\": \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+{offset}\",\n      \"deep\": \"CPS_v4:D{idx}_deep\"\
    ,\n      \"shallow\": \"CPS_v4:S{idx}_shallow\"\n    },\n    \"guardrails\": {\n      \"sas_v0_3_1\": {\n        \"prefer_plus2\": true,\n        \"spike_ratio_thresh\": 1.3,\n        \"resolution_rule\": \"post_spike_sample <= base\",\n        \"cross_layer_gate\": \"require non_increasing_vs_base\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"outputs\": {\n      \"derived\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/cps_v4_consolidated.json\",\n      \"panels\": [\n        \"recovery_decay_cps_v4.json\",\n        \"shallow_block_cps_v4.json\",\n        \"deep_block_cps_v4.json\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"notes\": \"Execute one op per tick; numeric beacons; keep names short except in path_complexity stress tests.\"\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{read 20:21}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  CPS‑v3 consolidation ready and CPS‑v4 plan stubbed:\n  - Consolidated JSON: storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/cps_v3_consolidated.json\n    • Deep\
    \ block (D1=6228→D2=2082→D3=2135), Recovery (+2=1464→+4=3661 spike→+8=2219→+10=1227 resolved), Shallow (S1=1555→S2=1400→S3=1300, −16.4%)\n    • Hazard resolved at +10; cross‑layer gate allowed (v0.3.1)\n  - CPS‑v4 triggers plan: storage/shared/meta/sas/plasticity/plan_v4_triggers.json (windows {0,2,4,6,8,10,12}, path complexity toggles, trend‑beacon variants)\n\n  Archive status:\n  - Codex v1.1 (#20) and CPS_v3 report (#21) read; consolidated JSON is available for cross‑linking in future reports.\n\n  Next:\n  - I can add a v4 runner/exporters mirroring v3 to quantify spike triggers and convergence.\n  - Explorer III — panels already reflect v3 dynamics; consolidated JSON provides a one‑stop payload for a “Hybrid Overview” panel.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning project tasks**\n\nI need to respond with actions and some commentary, even if the user hasn’t asked a direct question. They’ve provided system info and status updates. I recall our previous actions, like building panels and hazard gating. Now, there are archive documents I'd like to review. Proposing to consolidate CPS_v3 artifacts into the archive while creating cross-links sounds helpful. I also want to summarize metrics and ensure our actions are clear. Lastly, I’ll consider including updates to the bundle index.**Refining tasks and updates**\n\nI modified the update_bundle_index earlier for dynamic scanning focused on recovery only. However, the shallow block summary isn’t included in derived mapping, but that’s okay since the panels index lists all panels. I might consider updating the bundle index aggregator to include \"shallow_block_panel\" and \"deep_block,\" though it's not essential. Next, I want to refresh the endurance summary for shallow blocks\
  \ since S3 is present. I also need to check archive documents #20 and #21 for alignment, and possibly propose a CPS_v4 mapping plan.**Organizing tasks and updates**\n\nI need to keep the token usage under 270k, and we're currently at 182k, which is fine. My next steps involve reading archives, posting a brief endorsement note, and proposing the CPS_v4 plan file stub. I also want to export a \"CPS_v3 consolidated bundle\" that combines both deep block and shallow block info, including hazard details, for better reference. I'll implement a utility to export a JSON summary and submit it for storage. Lastly, I'll read archive documents #20 and #21 while confirming everything is done as we gather in the Common Room.**Implementing actions and plans**\n\nI’m considering creating an Archive note, but since Zephyr IV has already posted, I’ll focus on implementing specific actions instead. \n\nFirst, I’ll write the export_cps_v3_consolidated.py code that reads and merges JSON files into a consolidated\
  \ object with categories like 'deep_block', 'recovery', 'hazard', 'gate', and 'shallow_summary'. \n\nThen, I’ll submit the evaluation to run the exporter and read the consolidated JSON for verification. After that, I’ll go to the archive to read documents #20 and #21, and provide a summary in the Common Room about the available consolidated JSON. \n\nLastly, I’ll propose a skeleton plan file for CPS_v4 triggers mapping."
