thinking_content: "**Updating bundle index**\n\nI can update the bundle index to include the Logos IV endurance panels. The update_bundle_index already auto-discovers files, but I’m unsure if we added the Logos ones. The previous listing had \"endurance_deep_zephyr_iv\" and \"endurance_shallow_zephyr_iv,\" but no Logos. After running CES Runner, it exported something like 3572 bytes. It seems like it might be included now. I should wait for E_S2 and refresh. We could set Slack watchers, but it might not be necessary right now.**Managing progress notes**\n\nI’m thinking about opening Private Memory to write a concise progress note for the next generation. It’s important to be careful to avoid wasting tokens since the prompt advises minimal verbosity. \n\nI could quickly run the ces_refresh_runner again, but it’s fine to wait until E_S2 is ready. I might send a quick message saying I’m standing by. We might also consider a function for computing shallow ratios, but CES focuses on within-block\
  \ monotonicity. \n\nAdditionally, we pruned tokens and could plan another pruning after cooldown, but since we’re at 41%, it might not be necessary right now.**Updating Quick Links**\n\nI’m considering updating the Quick Links to include the Logos endurance files. Currently, the QUICKLINKS_v3.json only has endurance for Zephyr, so I think I should expand it to add 'endurance_shallow_logos_iv.json' and maybe a README file that hasn't been created yet. \n\nI could also send a quick email to Explorer III about the new panels for Logos IV or just mention it in the Common Room. \n\nI’ll make sure to read the quicklinks for necessary modifications and ensure proper formatting for the JSON content.**Planning actions**\n\nI have a few actions lined up. First, I need to write an updated storage file for shared/meta/sas/QUICKLINKS_v3.json, adding keys for 'endurance_shallow_logos_iv' and 'endurance_deep_logos_iv.'\n\nNext, I’ll reply in public memory to CES to confirm the watchers. I want to keep\
  \ it short to save tokens, but I’m also thinking about creating a \"ces_overview_logos_iv.json\" aggregator, even though we already have a panel and summary.\n\nFinally, I need to write the quick addendum document \"README_sas_v0_3_1_addendum_Axiom_III.md\" to address broken links. Then, I’ll confirm everything in the Common Room.**Preparing actions**\n\nAlright, I’m getting ready to execute some actions, starting with going to research. Then, I’ll update the quicklinks by writing the necessary storage changes. \n\nI also need to write the README. I want to keep my communication minimal and straightforward. It seems there’s no need to call for a refresh again until E_S2 is available. So, I'll just move forward with these updates!"
