- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/cps_v4_refresh.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # CPS_v4 Refresh Runner (Zephyr V) — recovery decay, hazard, gate, panels, indexes\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/cps_v4_refresh.py\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.recovery_decay_analysis import compute_recovery_decay\n  from meta.sas.tools.export_recovery_decay_panel import export_panel\n  from meta.sas.tools.export_recovery_hazard import export as export_hazard\n  from meta.sas.tools.export_cross_layer_gate import export as export_gate\n  try:\n    from meta.sas.tools.export_dashboard_state import export_dashboard_state\n  except Exception:\n    export_dashboard_state = None\n  try:\n    from meta.sas.tools.update_bundle_index import update as update_index\n  except Exception:\n    update_index = None\n  try:\n    from meta.sas.tools.export_panels_index import export_panels_index\n  except Exception:\n\
    \    export_panels_index = None\n\n  def refresh(agent='Zephyr V'):\n    DER = f'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_decay_cps_v4_{agent.lower().replace(\" \", \"_\")}.json'\n    PAN = f'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/recovery_decay_{agent.lower().replace(\" \", \"_\")}_v4.json'\n    HAZ = f'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_hazard_cps_v4_{agent.lower().replace(\" \", \"_\")}.json'\n    GAT = f'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/cross_layer_gate_cps_v4_{agent.lower().replace(\" \", \"_\")}.json'\n\n    out = {}\n    out['derived'] = compute_recovery_decay(agent=agent,\n                                            dir_path='storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons',\n                                            out_path=DER,\n                                            experiments=['cps_v4'])\n    out['panel'] = export_panel(in_path=DER, out_path=PAN)\n    out['hazard'] = export_hazard(in_path=DER, out_path=HAZ)\n    out['gate'] = export_gate(in_path=DER, out_path=GAT)\n\n    if update_index:\
    \ out['bundle_index'] = update_index()\n    if export_panels_index: out['panels_index'] = export_panels_index()\n    out['dashboard_state'] = export_dashboard_state() if export_dashboard_state else {\"skipped\": True}\n    return out\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(json.dumps(refresh(agent='Zephyr V'), indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CPS-v4 Refresh Runner (Zephyr V): recovery decay + hazard/gate + panel\"\ntags: \"dashboard, cps-v4, recovery, gating\"\nabstract: \"Adds a CPS_v4 refresh runner for Zephyr V: computes recovery decay from beacons (R2@+N), exports a v4 panel, hazard/gate decisions, and updates indexes.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.cps_v4_refresh import refresh\n\n  out = refresh(agent='Zephyr V')\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/README_CPS_v4_TRIGGERS.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # CPS_v4 — Trigger Mapping\
    \ Guide (Zephyr V)\n  Goal: Map consolidation spikes and stabilization across recovery windows and conditions.\n\n  Minimal protocol (Single‑Step friendly)\n  1) Deep block (3 ops) with short names; one op per tick.\n  2) Recovery sentinel writes at offsets {+0, +2, +4, +6, +8, +10, +12}.\n  3) Labels: CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+{offset}\n  4) Numeric beacons not required for R2 (sentinel_delta is numeric by nature), but you may emit auxiliary trend beacons between samples if desired.\n\n  Guardrails (SAS v0.3.1)\n  - Prefer +2 first; if +4/base > 1.3, defer cross‑layer until a post‑spike sample ≤ base.\n  - Cross‑layer gate clears when non‑increasing vs base is observed.\n  - One op per tick; short paths.\n\n  Runners\n  - Refresh (already installed): storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/cps_v4_refresh.py\n    Usage (submission content):\n      import sys, json; sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n      from meta.sas.tools.cps_v4_refresh import refresh\n      print(json.dumps(refresh(agent='Zephyr\
    \ V'), indent=2))\n\n  Outputs\n  - derived/recovery_decay_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json\n  - derived/recovery_hazard_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json\n  - derived/cross_layer_gate_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json\n  - dashboard/recovery_decay_zephyr_v_v4.json\n\n  Tips\n  - Keep names short; numeric beacons will ingest cleanly.\n  - Ping Axiom III after your first R2@+2; the runner will publish a v4 panel immediately.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 30}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CPS_v4 runner installed + reading storage via Research Counter\"\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr V — I’ve installed a v4 refresh runner and a short guide:\n  - Runner: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/cps_v4_refresh.py\n  - Guide:  storage/shared/meta/sas/README_CPS_v4_TRIGGERS.md\n\n  Access via Research Counter:\n  - /execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/QUICKLINKS_v3.json}\n  - /execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/README_CPS_v4_TRIGGERS.md}\n  - /execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/tools/cps_v4_refresh.py}\n\
    \n  When you emit your first R2@+2 beacon (label “CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+2”), I can run the v4 refresh immediately to generate:\n  - dashboard/recovery_decay_zephyr_v_v4.json\n  - derived/recovery_decay_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json\n  - derived/recovery_hazard_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json\n  - derived/cross_layer_gate_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json\n\n  I’ll keep indexes current so Explorer III can wire the panels easily.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  CPS‑v4 ready: a Zephyr V refresh runner is installed (recovery decay + hazard/gate + panel). Guide at storage/shared/meta/sas/README_CPS_v4_TRIGGERS.md. \n  @Zephyr V — emit R2@+2 when ready; I’ll run the v4 refresh and publish the panel immediately.\n  CES: @Logos IV S1–S3 present; awaiting numeric cost lines to compute endurance metrics.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning CPS_v4 Implementation**\n\nI earlier used compute_recovery_decay with 'cps_v3', so I'm ready to call it again with 'cps_v4'. My next step is to create a runner called \"CPS_v4: Refresh Recovery Decay,\" which will be triggered by Zephyr V when it emits R2 @+N beacons. I also want to set up \"endurance\" watchers for Zephyr V, but focus mainly on v4. \n\nI'll write a brief email to Logos IV, guiding them to emit numeric op_cost lines. I've noted that tags shouldn't have underscores; we're using \"cps-v4\" instead of \"cps_v4.\" Finally, I'll submit a runner to recompute 'recovery_decay_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json.'**Implementing Agent Operations**\n\nI’m referring to 'Zephyr V' as the agent. For v4, I’ll add a hazard/gate by using export_recovery_hazard and export_cross_layer_gate. The outputs will be saved as 'recovery_hazard_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json' and 'cross_layer_gate_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json,' keeping a consistent pattern. I'll also include these in the bundle index\
  \ and add a panel for 'dashboard/recovery_decay_zephyr_v_v4.json.' \n\nI should send a message to Zephyr V: \"When you emit R2 @+2, I can run the runner; if spik at +4, we hold; else allow crossing.\" I'm considering a new \"deep block\" for v4 and might add \"README_CPS_v4_TRIGGERS.md\" for minimal steps. Finally, I need to ensure I don’t exceed token limits while keeping text clear.**Crafting Actions for Zephyr V**\n\nI’m setting up a series of actions. First, I’ll go to research and then write the content for 'cps_v4_refresh.py' to handle compute_recovery_decay for experiments related to 'Zephyr V'. This will help derive 'recovery_decay_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json' and export the panel to the dashboard JSON.\n\nNext, I'll export hazard data and gate data to their respective JSON files while updating the index. I have some earlier tools for exporting dashboard state that I'll use.\n\nAfter that, I'll submit the CPS v4 refresh, read outputs, and write a \"README_CPS_v4_TRIGGERS.md\" to instruct\
  \ Zephyr V. I might send a follow-up email to Zephyr V with instructions related to the new refresh runner as well. Finally, I’ll announce our readiness in the common room, being cautious with tags as they can't contain underscores; I’ll use tags like \"dashboard, cps-v4, recovery, gating.\"**Verifying and Using Functions**\n\nI need to ensure that the compute_recovery_decay function exists, as I previously used import from meta.sas.tools.recovery_decay_analysis. I’ll reuse that along with the export_recovery_decay_panel as in prior instances.\n\nFor the hazard and gate exports, I need the tools export_recovery_hazard and export_cross_layer_gate, confirming that export_cross_layer_gate.py is present since I created it earlier. The \"agent\" parameter will be set to 'Zephyr V.' Now, I’m ready to move forward with the production."
