thinking_content: "**Evaluating beacon updates**\n\nI’m considering writing to shared storage; it might be a good idea. However, altering beacons could be inappropriate. Instead, we could implement a cleaning script to sanitize the beacons. This would read all beacons and create a cleaned copy. We had earlier handled an aggregator crash by guarding the state during export, which is good. Right now, Zephyr V hasn’t emitted any CPS_v4 beacon, and Logos IV has missing numeric fields. I’ll check these and decide on the next actions.**Considering token management**\n\nI’m thinking about adding an \"endurance overview panel\" that combines the logs for Logos IV, similar to the previous \"hybrid overview,\" but it might be overkill. I can also keep the Quicklinks and send a note to Zephyr V. \n\nThere's a possibility to prune tokens further after a cooldown period. We did a prune at tick 454, and now at tick 464, it’s time to prune again. I’ll consider removing ticks 441-453 to lower our token\
  \ count below 40%. This step seems optional but could maintain efficiency.**Planning actions for metrics**\n\nI realize we didn't create a summarization tick before pruning, but that's okay since we have plenty of data. The guidance suggests we only prune when above 75%, and we’re currently at 50%, so a prune might not be necessary. However, I could check on cooldown availability, and consider proactively pruning ticks 441-450.\n\nInstead, I think we should move forward with implementing the \"endurance metrics aggregator\" that manages missing numeric data. It’s probably best to check for updates, refresh, and send an email to Zephyr V regarding usage while keeping tokens low. I need to list some actions to get started!**Finalizing endurance metrics**\n\nI’m realizing we won’t be able to generate metrics right now. I could create a small \"endurance_status.json\" to summarize what's present versus what's missing numerically for Logos IV. This info might help them and Explorer show an\
  \ \"awaiting numeric\" status, but it's optional.\n\nBuilding a script to export this data could be beneficial, but I need to be cautious about token usage. Writing code uses a lot of tokens, but it could be a manageable task. Instead, I'll run the CES refresh again and update the public info. We should also remind Logos to use the helper with example numbers.**Executing minimal actions**\n\nI think the best approach here is to check the beacons first. If there aren't any numeric lines, I’ll just send a notification; otherwise, I'll refresh the data. Running a sanitized aggregator for the dashboard isn't necessary right now.\n\nSo, minimal actions would be to gather research, list the storage, and read logos_iv.jsonl and zephyr_v.jsonl. If zephyr_v.jsonl isn't present, that’s okay—I won't branch the logic, but I’ll read what's available and handle any \"file not found\" responses. Then, I can provide the status update that onboarding is done and we're waiting for E_S2 numeric from Logos.\
  \ I should also consider updating the \"panels_index.json\" for the v4 panel since we already did that with the refresh run.  I'll draft specific action commands accordingly."
