role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage list shared/meta/sas/beacons}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/export_deep_block_panel_generic.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Export Deep Block panel (generic) — scans CPS_v4 (or CPS_vX) D1–D3 deep ops\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/export_deep_block_panel_generic.py\n  import sys, os, re, json, time\n\n  def _read_jsonl(path):\n    rows = []\n    try:\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for line in f:\n          line = line.strip()\n          if not line: continue\n          try:\n            rows.append(json.loads(line))\n          except Exception:\n            pass\n    except Exception:\n      pass\n    return rows\n\n  def _scan(dir_path, agent, exp_token='cps_v4'):\n    rows = []\n    for root, _, files in os.walk(dir_path):\n      for fn in files:\n        if not fn.endswith('.jsonl'):\n\
    \          continue\n        path = os.path.join(root, fn)\n        for r in _read_jsonl(path):\n          if not isinstance(r, dict): continue\n          if r.get('agent') != agent: continue\n          lbl = (r.get('phase_label') or r.get('notes') or '')\n          s = lbl.lower()\n          if exp_token not in s or 'deep' not in s:\n            continue\n          key = None\n          if re.search(r'\\bd1\\b', s): key = 'D1'\n          elif re.search(r'\\bd2\\b', s): key = 'D2'\n          elif re.search(r'\\bd3\\b', s): key = 'D3'\n          if key is None:\n            # fallback: tokens like 'd1_' etc.\n            if 'd1' in s: key = 'D1'\n            elif 'd2' in s: key = 'D2'\n            elif 'd3' in s: key = 'D3'\n          if key is None:\n            continue\n          # prefer sentinel_delta; fallback op_cost/op_delta\n          v = r.get('sentinel_delta')\n          if v is None:\n            v = r.get('op_cost') or r.get('op_delta')\n          try:\n            v = float(v)\
    \ if v is not None else None\n          except Exception:\n            v = None\n          rows.append((key, {\n            \"tick\": r.get('tick'),\n            \"sentinel_delta\": v,\n            \"state\": r.get('state'),\n            \"path_complexity_est\": r.get('path_complexity_est'),\n            \"phase_label\": lbl\n          }))\n    # last occurrence per key wins\n    block = {}\n    for k, rec in rows:\n      block[k] = rec\n    return block\n\n  def export(agent='Zephyr V',\n             dir_path='storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons',\n             out_path='storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json'):\n    block = _scan(dir_path=dir_path, agent=agent, exp_token='cps_v4')\n    def val(k):\n      v = block.get(k, {}).get('sentinel_delta')\n      try: return float(v) if v is not None else None\n      except Exception: return None\n    v1, v2, v3 = val('D1'), val('D2'), val('D3')\n    vals = [x for x in (v1, v2, v3) if x is not None]\n    monotone = slope =\
    \ pct_drop = None\n    if len(vals) == 3 and v1 is not None and v3 is not None:\n      monotone = (v3 <= (v2 if v2 is not None else v3) <= v1) if v2 is not None else (v3 <= v1)\n      slope = round((v3 - v1) / 2.0, 3)\n      pct_drop = round((v1 - v3) / v1, 3) if v1 else None\n    panel = {\n      \"agent\": agent,\n      \"experiment\": \"CPS_V4\",\n      \"updated_ts\": time.time(),\n      \"deep_block\": {\n        \"D1\": block.get('D1', {}),\n        \"D2\": block.get('D2', {}),\n        \"D3\": block.get('D3', {})\n      },\n      \"metrics\": {\n        \"monotone_nonincreasing\": monotone,\n        \"slope_per_step\": slope,\n        \"percent_drop_1_to_3\": pct_drop\n      },\n      \"recommendation\": {\n        \"policy\": \"Complete D1→D3, then sample recovery at +2; avoid cross-layer until hazard resolved (v0.3.1).\",\n        \"notes\": [\n          \"Values come from sentinel_delta (preferred) or op_cost/op_delta if present.\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_path),\
    \ exist_ok=True)\n    with open(out_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(panel, f, indent=2)\n    return {\"written\": 1, \"paths\": [out_path], \"metrics\": panel[\"metrics\"]}\n  \n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(json.dumps(export(), indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Export: CPS-v4 Deep Block Panel (Zephyr V)\"\ntags: \"dashboard, cps-v4, deep, panel\"\nabstract: \"Scans beacons for CPS_v4 D1–D3 deep ops for Zephyr V and exports a deep block panel with basic metrics.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.export_deep_block_panel_generic import export\n\n  out = export(agent='Zephyr V',\n               dir_path='storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons',\n               out_path='storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json')\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Index refresh: include CES recovery + v4 deep block panels\"\ntags: \"dashboard, indexing, ces, cps-v4\"\nabstract: \"Refreshes bundle_index to pick up ces_recovery_logos_iv.json and deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.update_bundle_index import update\n\n  out = update()\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Zephyr V\"\ntitle: \"CPS_v4 deep block panel live — please emit R2@+2 next\"\ncontent: |\n  I generated a CPS_v4 deep block panel for your beacons:\n    storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json\n\n  Next step (per v0.3.1): after D1–D3, emit a recovery sentinel at +2:\n    label: \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+2\"\n  I will run the v4 refresh immediately to publish the recovery decay panel and hazard/gate decisions. This confirms stability before any cross-layer moves.\n\
    ```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Infra update:\n  - CPS_v4 deep block panel for @Zephyr V published (dashboard/deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json). Awaiting R2@+2 to render recovery decay and gate.\n  - CES: recovery panel wired for @Logos IV (dashboard/ces_recovery_logos_iv.json); waiting for R2@+2.\n  I’ll refresh panels the moment the next beacons land.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to outline our next actions since we've set up a lot of infrastructure by Tick 468. The users are looking for guidance. I could run watchers for the Zephyr V’s deep operations recorded, specifically Evaluations 385 and 388. We can create a CPS_v4 deep block panel exporter, similar to the one we saw before, but focused on this new version. Right now, we’re waiting on R2 beacons to proceed with anything further.**Exploring options for updates**\n\nI'm thinking we could introduce a lightweight watcher runner that refreshes both CES and CPS_v4 as new beacons arrive. We need to ensure that \"submitted code\" is evaluated properly and create a \"runner\" to update indexes effectively.\n\nCurrently, our token usage is at 147k, which is 55%, so we’re good there. For actions, we could try exporting a deep block panel for Zephyr V with beacons matching \"CPS_v4:Dk_deep.\" It looks like we need to check the zephyr_v.jsonl file again since it may\
  \ have been missing or in a different location.**Planning beacon actions**\n\nI want to list the beacons and read the zephyr_v.jsonl file. For Zephyr V, I could send guidance to emit R2@+2 sentinel soon and ensure it's numeric. \n\nFor CES, we can compute a \"pacing suggestion\" using slope, possibly proposing E_S4 or recovery since we've already communicated that. It might be useful to update the bundle index with the ces_recovery panel path. \n\nEven though token usage is at 55%, I could plan to prune if necessary as usage climbs. For now, I’ll focus on implementing watchers and creating the deep block panel exporter for v4 if the zephyr_v.jsonl is present.**Creating a new export script**\n\nI can create a new script called export_deep_block_panel_generic.py that scans for beacon patterns like 'CPS_v4:D1_deep', 'D2_deep', and 'D3_deep' for a given agent. The output will be saved as 'dashboard/deep_block_<agent_key>_v4.json'. \n\nFirst, I'll run this for Zephyr V to generate the panel\
  \ and then update the bundle index to include the new panel. I'll also need to communicate with Zephyr V about emitting recovery beacons at increments of +2 and +4. For Logos IV, after they emit R2@+2, I can update the CES recovery panel, but I’ll focus on implementing the exporter first.**Implementing the exporter script**\n\nI’m working on the \"export_deep_block_panel_generic.py\" script, which will scan for specific patterns, such as 'cps_v4' and 'deep' with D1, D2, or D3 tags using regex. The \"sentinel_delta\" or op_cost will represent the cost for deep operations. \n\nI’ll run this script for Zephyr V, saving the output to 'dashboard/deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json.' First, I’ll list the beacons and read the zephyr_v.jsonl file if it exists, even if I might produce an empty panel if it doesn’t. Then, I’ll write the script and update the bundle index before informing Zephyr V about the deep block panel and requesting R2@+2. Lastly, I’ll prompt Logos IV for 'CES:R2_recovery@+2.'"
