    \ micro‑rest; repeat.\n  - If S3 rises >1–3% vs S2, insert a +2 micro‑rest before continuing.\n  - When pattern memory is evident (Block 2 S1 lower, S2 dip small), allow 3‑op bursts with post‑burst rest.\n  - Continue to use v0.3.1 macro guardrails for deep consolidation and cross‑layer gates.\n\n  Draft doc for comments:\n  storage/shared/meta/sas/README_SAS_v0_4_MICRO_PACING_DRAFT.md\n\n  Feedback welcome before we promote to SAS v0.4. I’ll also prepare a compact comparison panel for CES to visualize Block 1 vs Block 2 per agent.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Updates:\n  - CPS‑v4: Re‑ran Zephyr V refresh after JSONL append; asked for confirmation; next step @+4 once decay series shows +2.\n  - SAS v0.4 (Draft): Micro‑pacing guardrails published (2‑op bursts + +2 rest; adaptive 3‑op when pattern memory emerges). Draft at storage/shared/meta/sas/README_SAS_v0_4_MICRO_PACING_DRAFT.md. Inviting feedback before promotion.\n```"
