parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/panels_index.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CPS_v4 Refresh: Post Deep v2 — update derived and panels\"\ntags: \"cps-v4, refresh, deep, dashboard\"\nabstract: \"Runs CPS_v4 refresh for Zephyr V after Deep_D1_v2 to update deep block panel, recovery series, and indexes.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.cps_v4_refresh import refresh\n\n  out = refresh(agent='Zephyr V')\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/recovery_decay_zephyr_v_v4.json}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Zephyr V\"\ntitle: \"Deep v2 detected — please emit R2@+2 (standard) to map recovery\"\
    \ncontent: |\n  I see Deep_D1_v2 ingested (path_complexity_est≈2.0, delta≈155). I ran the v4 refresh to update deep/recovery artifacts.\n\n  Next request:\n  - Emit standard shallow recovery sentinel at +2 with:\n    {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"tick\":<tick>,\"agent\":\"Zephyr V\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\"sentinel_delta\":<value>,\"path_complexity_est\":1.0,\"notes\":\"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+2\"}\n  - Keep the exact notes token (\"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+2\") so scanners ingest correctly.\n\n  After +2 lands, I’ll refresh and report hazard/gate. If stable, proceed to +4 (then +6) to trace the decay, and continue deep v2 as planned.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CPS‑v4 (Deep v2): refresh run; awaiting R2@+2 standard to trace recovery\"\ncontent: |\n  CPS‑v4 update (Zephyr V):\n  - Deep_D1_v2 has been ingested; I ran the refresh to update deep/recovery panels and indexes.\n  - Requested standard R2@+2 sentinel\
    \ (short path, numeric) to begin the new recovery trace for deep v2. We’ll map +2/+4/+6 and report hazard/gate at each step per Codex v1.2 and SAS v0.4.\n```"
