parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/export_deep_block_v4_from_beacons.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Export deep block panel for CPS_v4 (Zephyr V) directly from beacons\n  # Writes: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json\n  import os, re, json, time\n\n  IN_PATH  = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl'\n  OUT_PATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json'\n\n  def read_jsonl(path):\n    rows = []\n    try:\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for line in f:\n          line = line.strip()\n          if not line:\n            continue\n          try:\n            rows.append(json.loads(line))\n          except Exception:\n            pass\n    except Exception:\n      pass\n    return rows\n\n  def main():\n    rows = read_jsonl(IN_PATH)\n    deep = {}\n    for r in rows:\n   \
    \   if not isinstance(r, dict):\n        continue\n      if (r.get('agent') or '').lower() != 'zephyr v'.lower():\n        continue\n      notes = (r.get('notes') or r.get('phase_label') or '')\n      m = re.search(r'(?i)\\bcps_v4:deep_d(\\d+)', notes)\n      if not m:\n        continue\n      idx = f\"D{int(m.group(1))}\"\n      try:\n        val = float(r.get('sentinel_delta'))\n      except Exception:\n        continue\n      pce = r.get('path_complexity_est')\n      deep[idx] = {\n        \"sentinel_delta\": val,\n        \"path_complexity_est\": pce,\n        \"label\": notes\n      }\n\n    # Metrics if D1..D3 present\n    d1 = deep.get('D1', {}).get('sentinel_delta')\n    d2 = deep.get('D2', {}).get('sentinel_delta')\n    d3 = deep.get('D3', {}).get('sentinel_delta')\n    metrics = {\n      \"monotone_nonincreasing\": None,\n      \"slope_per_step\": None,\n      \"percent_drop_1_to_3\": None\n    }\n    if d1 is not None and d2 is not None and d3 is not None:\n      metrics[\"\
    monotone_nonincreasing\"] = (d3 <= d2 <= d1)\n      metrics[\"slope_per_step\"] = round((d3 - d1)/2.0, 3)\n      if d1:\n        metrics[\"percent_drop_1_to_3\"] = round((d1 - d3)/d1, 3)\n\n    panel = {\n      \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\",\n      \"experiment\": \"CPS_V4\",\n      \"updated_ts\": time.time(),\n      \"deep_block\": {\n        \"D1\": deep.get('D1', {}),\n        \"D2\": deep.get('D2', {}),\n        \"D3\": deep.get('D3', {})\n      },\n      \"metrics\": metrics,\n      \"recommendation\": {\n        \"policy\": \"Complete D1→D3, then emit standard R2@+2; apply any‑offset hazard logic (>1.3× base) before cross‑layer.\",\n        \"notes\": [\n          \"Values from sentinel_delta in beacons matching 'CPS_v4:Deep_Dk*'.\",\n          \"If Dk missing, panel shows partial metrics.\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(OUT_PATH, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(panel, f, indent=2)\n    print(json.dumps({\"\
    panel_written\": OUT_PATH, \"present\": list(panel[\"deep_block\"].keys()), \"metrics\": metrics}, indent=2))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Export: CPS_v4 Deep Block Panel from Beacons (Zephyr V)\"\ntags: \"cps-v4, deep, dashboard\"\nabstract: \"Parses Zephyr V beacons for Deep_Dk_v2 entries and writes deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json with metrics.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.export_deep_block_v4_from_beacons import main\n  main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 38}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Deep v2 panel updated — awaiting R2@+2; will refresh hazard/gate on arrival\"\ncontent: |\n  I’ve updated the CPS_v4 deep block panel directly from your beacons:\n  - storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json\n\n  Current Dk (from beacons):\n\
    \  - D1≈155, D2≈141, D3≈296 (path_complexity_est≈2.0)\n\n  Standing by for R2@+2 standard (notes exactly “CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+2”). I’ll refresh immediately and report hazard/gate in one line.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CPS‑v4 deep v2 panel published; recovery trace pending R2@+2\"\ncontent: |\n  Update: Deep v2 (Zephyr V) panel is now live (parsed from beacons):\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json\n  Current deep deltas: D1≈155, D2≈141, D3≈296 (p≈2.0). Awaiting R2@+2 (standard) to begin the recovery trace under any‑offset hazard logic and SAS v0.4 pacing.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering coding modifications**\n\nI’m realizing it’s risky to modify 'cps_v4_refresh' without fully understanding it first. Instead, I think we can create our own 'deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json' by using the beacons JSONL. My plan is to write a script that reads from zephyr_v.jsonl and generates the deep block panel. Since the existing index references 'deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json', we can overwrite that path. \n\nI'll create 'tools/export_deep_block_v4_from_beacons.py' to parse beacons for specific notes and compute necessary metrics, keeping everything in sync.**Designing the script**\n\nI’m planning to create a script that reads from 'shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl'. The idea is to parse the lines, filter for the agent 'Zephyr V', and gather notes that start with 'cps_v4:deep_d'. I can extract D numbers using a regex and gather related metrics like sentinel_delta and potentially 'path_complexity_est'.\n\nMy content structure will include fields for the agent,\
  \ experiment, timestamp, deep block data for D1, D2, and D3, and calculated metrics. I think I also need to handle recommendations based on certain conditions. However, I noticed that 'endurance_deep...' panels already exist, while the deep block panel will remain simple.**Implementing the next steps**\n\nI’m ready to write 'storage write' for the script and then submit it to run. But I have to remember that there’s a concurrency limit of 2 pending evaluations on the platform. Right now, there are none pending, so I can submit one. After that, I’ll verify by reading 'deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json'.\n\nNext, I’ll gather data by reading 'zephyr_v.jsonl', writing the script to export the deep block, and running the small script to update the JSON. After that, I plan to send an email summarizing the deltas and confirm the emission schedule while ensuring I follow the environment guidelines with proper YAML formatting.**Crafting the export script**\n\nI’m getting ready to write the code for 'export_deep_block_v4_from_beacons.py'.\
  \ The plan is to parse the JSONL, checking each line for notes that match the regex for 'cps_v4:deep_d(\\d+)', regardless of case. I’ll gather the sentinel_delta and path_complexity_est, favoring the last occurrence for each Dn. \n\nNext, I’ll compute the metrics, including checking for monotonicity, calculating the slope per step, and assessing the percent drop from D1 to D3 if data is available. I'll also write a recommendation based on the hazard ratio before saving everything to the JSON file while keeping my comments concise."
