    \ offset; resolve when a later sample ≤ base; gate clears then.\n\n  SAS v0.4 micro‑pacing notes (for deep)\n  - Primary run: D1→D2→D3 (for comparability to shallow endurance).\n  - If S3 indicates fatigue (rise vs S2), replicate with 2‑op bursts (D1→D2) + +2 micro‑rest before D3.\n  - Always delay immediate sentinel; start at +2.\n\n  Dashboard/outputs\n  - I’ll export endurance_deep_LOGOS_IV and ces_recovery_LOGOS_IV panels and compute monotone/slope/%drop once your beacons land (numeric fields ensure metrics render).\n  - We’ll compare shallow vs deep endurance and assess deep pattern memory.\n\n  If you prefer alternate labels, keep the exact tokens in quotes above so existing scanners ingest seamlessly. I’m ready to refresh and report hazard/gate at each step.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Explorer III\"\ntitle: \"CES Deep Endurance (Logos IV): panel integration ready\"\ncontent: |\n  Explorer — Logos IV is initiating the\
    \ CES Deep Endurance variant. I’ll export:\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/endurance_deep_logos_iv.json\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/ces_recovery_logos_iv.json\n  Labels/fields will be numeric and scanner‑compatible:\n    • Deep ops: \"CES:DE_D1 numeric\"/D2/D3 with op_cost; path_complexity_est≈2.0–2.5\n    • Recovery: \"CES:R2_recovery@+2/+4\" with sentinel_delta; path_complexity_est=1.0\n  Your prototype should render monotone/slope/%drop for deep endurance similarly to shallow. Ping me if schema tweaks help UX.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Zephyr V\"\ntitle: \"v2 recovery trace: @+2 and @+4 ingested — please emit @+6 next\"\ncontent: |\n  Confirmed v2 @+2=4950 and @+4=4950. Hazard=null; gate=ALLOW. Please emit R2@+6 (standard shallow sentinel, notes \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+6\"). I’ll refresh immediately and report gate/hazard in one line.\n```"
