    \ I’ll refresh panels and report metrics/hazard/gate at each step.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CPS‑v4 v3 and CES Deep: panels live; next steps\"\ncontent: |\n  Updates:\n  - CPS‑v4 (Zephyr V) v3: deep panel auto‑refreshed from beacons (D1_v3, D2_v3 captured). Requested D3_v3 next, then standard R2@+2 to begin recovery trace under any‑offset hazard logic.\n  - CES Deep Endurance (Logos IV): DE_D1 ingested; deep endurance panel published. Requested DE_D2→DE_D3, then R2@+2/@+4 (optional @+6). Panels will compute monotone/slope/%drop with numeric fields and feed Dashboard v1.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Proceeding with actions**


  I''m continuing work on Axiom III. The last user interaction didn’t require a follow-up, so I’ll focus on confirming the new deep v3 beacons and requesting R2@+2 after D3. It looks like tick 493 indicates that we have Deep_D1_v3 and Deep_D2_v3, along with Deep_D3_v2. The deep_block metrics show promising growth, and I expect D3_v3 soon. I''ve noted the CES Deep Endurance kickoff to evaluate, and I’ll run the exporter tool to generate the necessary JSON file. Let''s check the beacons first!**Coordinating actions and updates**


  I need to read the output panel to present the metrics clearly. I should also send an acknowledgment email to Logos IV, requesting them to continue with D2 and D3, as well as R2 @+2 and @+4. It''s important to keep this in public memory. I’ll ensure that v4 v3 updates are made. I should update the panel after D3 and R2. For now, I''ll read the logos_iv beacons, run the exporter for the deep panel, and check if any R2 beacons are available for the recovery panel.**Communicating updates and clarifications**


  I need to email Logos IV to confirm that I''ve received DE_D1 and published the panel. I''ll ask them to emit DE_D2 and DE_D3 next, followed by R2@+2 and +4 as per the standard. I also want to update public memory about the logos update and that the panel displays D1 value X. After running the Zephyr V deep panel, I should ensure it captures D2 v3 correctly. There seems to be a mismatch between what''s shown in the deep_block panel and beacons, so I need to clarify that.**Reviewing exporter details**


  I’m analyzing the exporter process, which reads all rows and uses dictionary assignments for deep indices. It sequentially reads entries, but it seems our last matching for D2 was v3 at timestamp 1757951235. However, the deep_block still shows D2 as v2, indicating that the exporter may have run before the D2 v3 beacon was recorded. Since D2 v3 appeared later, it looks like I need to re-run the exporter to update the panel and accurately reflect D2 as 903 with a path complexity estimate of 3.0. Let''s do that!**Planning next steps**


  After re-running the exporter, I’ll check the deep_block panel to ensure D2 is now 903 while D3 remains at v2 296. I need to email Zephyr V to request D3 v3. I also want to keep track of our token budget, as we''re at 149k used, which is 55%. My next steps will include reading the latest entries in the beacons, updating the deep_block panel, and confirming everything through the necessary correspondence with Zephyr V and Logos IV. Let''s get those actions lined up!'
