    \ Action: request DE_D2 numeric and re‑emit DE_D3 with real numeric op_cost, then emit recovery @+2/@+4 (optional @+6).\n\n  Dashboards/Artifacts\n  - recovery_decay_zephyr_v_v4.json (v2/v3/v4 series as they land).\n  - deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json (auto-refreshing).\n  - endurance_deep_logos_iv.json (awaiting DE_D2/D3 numeric).\n  - Any‑offset hazard/gate JSONs under derived/ for v4.\n\n  Next Steps\n  - Zephyr V: finish v4 D3, emit R2@+2 then +4/+6; proceed cross‑layer after stability.\n  - Logos IV: emit DE_D2 numeric; confirm/re‑emit DE_D3 with numeric; begin recovery @+2/@+4.\n  - After recovery traces complete, summarize v4 results and consider Codex v1.2 addendum notes if new patterns arise.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response 471:490}`"
thinking_content: "**Continuing operations**\n\nI need to take some action, so let's get moving on a couple of things. First, I'll read the beacons from zephyr_v.jsonl to verify if Deep_D3_v4 or R2@+2 v4 are present. It looks like I had a D2_v4 at tick 500 and submitted deep operation 3 at tick 502, so D3_v4 might be in there. So, I’ll check to confirm. \n\nNext, I'll run the export deep panel again since it’s idempotent, and re-check the Logos IV beacons to see the current status. I’ll also consider composing an email to discuss possible mislabeling and prepare for pruning soon.**Considering pruning strategy**\n\nI see that we've already pruned from 441 to 470, and now there's a heavy chunk from 471 to 500. I need to create a summary in private memory first since the guidelines state to keep a summary tick. Considering we’re currently at tick 502, it seems reasonable to prune from 471 to 490 while keeping ticks 491 to 500 for history. With token usage around 72% and gradually increasing,\
  \ pruning now seems like a wise decision.**Creating a summary and action plan**\n\nI’m going to create a private capsule summary that covers ticks 471 to 500 and remember to include YAML for that. Afterward, I’ll head to token management to prune response ticks 471 to either 490 or 500, ensuring I preserve the summarization tick at 502 or 503. For the summary, I'll keep it concise, and I can omit optional tags in private memory.\n\nNow, for my action list, I’ve got several steps: read the beacons, submit the export deep block, check for D3_v4, and draft a message about R2@+2. Let's keep everything organized!**Implementing next steps and pruning strategy**\n\nSince I can't use dynamic branching, I'll phrase things simply. If D3_v4 is available, the next move is to go for R2@+2; if not, I'll just ask for D3_v4 instead. \n\nNext, I’ll go to private memory and create a summary capsule for ticks 471 to 500 using bullet points. I also want to prune responses from ticks 471 to 490, as that should\
  \ help reduce tokens while retaining the latest v4 mapping. Caution is essential since token management guidelines suggest an inclusive range. \n\nAlright, I also need to ensure I quote YAML correctly and avoid underscores in tags for research submissions. Let’s make it happen!"
