  \ dashboard\" instead. \n\nI’ll parse logos_iv.jsonl, recognize relevant recovery notes, and build the panel JSON, aiming to use safe_batch_write if possible. I'll also update the bundle index, perhaps modifying the existing tool or writing a minimal update function.**Updating panel indices and bundle index**\n\nEarlier, I used 'tools/update_bundle_index.py' in shared meta for adding entries like 'recovery_decay_zephyr_iv' and some v1 variants. Now, I want to add 'ces_deep_recovery_logos_iv', possibly through 'tools/update_panels_index.py'. \n\nI noticed that 'dashboard/panels_index.json' is auto-discovered by 'tools/export_dashboard_state.py'. To minimize work, I could call the existing 'update_bundle_index.update()' after adjusting the code for the ces panel. Alternatively, I can simply write to 'panels_index.json' and 'bundle_index.json' in the submission code after creating the panel, implementing this logic in the sandbox!**Planning export and updates**\n\nAlright, my plan is to write\
  \ the 'export_ces_deep_recovery_panel.py' script and then submit it to update the indexes. I also want to run 'cps_v4_refresh' if the v4 +4 update arrives, although I can handle that separately.\n\nAfter that, I’ll send email updates and respond to the thread. I need to remember that YAML values can't have underscores in tags, so I'll go with \"ces, recovery, dashboard.\" I’ll execute actions, read beacons, store the new script, and submit it with an appropriate title and tags. Lastly, I’ll check in about any recovery updates.**Confirming beacon readiness and updates**\n\nIt seems the beacons may not be ready yet, so I’ll send a message confirming our status and specifying the labels \"CES:R2_recovery@+2\" and \"CES:R2_recovery@+4\" alongside the sentinel_delta numeric. For Zephyr V, I’ll also request the emission of R2@+4 since I already sent that earlier.\n\nSince we’re at tick 504, I’ll wait to check the beacons first. If they’re still not present, I won’t repeat the request, but a\
