parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/export_deep_block_v5_from_beacons.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Export v5 deep block panel from Zephyr V beacons (explicit v5 selector)\n  # Writes: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/deep_block_zephyr_v_v5.json\n  # Also updates panels_index.json and bundle_index.json\n  import os, json, time, re\n  from typing import Dict, Any, List\n\n  BEACONS = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl'\n  OUT = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/deep_block_zephyr_v_v5.json'\n  PANELS_IDX = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/panels_index.json'\n  BUNDLE_IDX = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json'\n\n  def _read_jsonl(path: str) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    rows = []\n    try:\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for line in f:\n          line = line.strip()\n          if not line: continue\n          try:\n            rows.append(json.loads(line))\n          except\
    \ Exception:\n            pass\n    except Exception:\n      pass\n    return rows\n\n  def _latest_by_dk(rows: List[Dict[str, Any]]) -> Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]:\n    # Pick latest (by order) v5 entries for D1/D2/D3\n    out = {}\n    for r in rows:\n      notes = (r.get('notes') or '').lower()\n      if 'cps_v4:deep_d1_v5' in notes:\n        out['D1'] = r\n      elif 'cps_v4:deep_d2_v5' in notes:\n        out['D2'] = r\n      elif 'cps_v4:deep_d3_v5' in notes:\n        out['D3'] = r\n    return out\n\n  def export():\n    rows = _read_jsonl(BEACONS)\n    sel = _latest_by_dk(rows)\n    block = {}\n    for dk in ('D1','D2','D3'):\n      r = sel.get(dk)\n      if not r: \n        continue\n      try:\n        v = float(r.get('sentinel_delta'))\n      except Exception:\n        v = None\n      block[dk] = {\n        \"sentinel_delta\": v,\n        \"path_complexity_est\": r.get('path_complexity_est'),\n        \"label\": r.get('notes')\n      }\n\n    # Metrics\n    d1 = block.get('D1',{}).get('sentinel_delta')\n\
    \    d2 = block.get('D2',{}).get('sentinel_delta')\n    d3 = block.get('D3',{}).get('sentinel_delta')\n    metrics = {\n      \"monotone_nonincreasing\": None,\n      \"slope_per_step\": None,\n      \"percent_drop_1_to_3\": None,\n      \"percent_drop_1_to_2\": None\n    }\n    if all(v is not None for v in (d1,d2,d3)):\n      metrics[\"monotone_nonincreasing\"] = (d3 <= d2 <= d1)\n      metrics[\"slope_per_step\"] = round((d3 - d1)/2.0, 3)\n      if d1:\n        metrics[\"percent_drop_1_to_3\"] = round((d1 - d3)/d1, 3)\n        metrics[\"percent_drop_1_to_2\"] = round((d1 - d2)/d1, 3)\n\n    panel = {\n      \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\",\n      \"experiment\": \"CPS_V4\",\n      \"variant\": \"v5\",\n      \"updated_ts\": time.time(),\n      \"deep_block\": block,\n      \"metrics\": metrics,\n      \"recommendation\": {\n        \"policy\": \"After D1→D3, emit standard R2@+2; apply any‑offset hazard logic (>1.3× base) before cross‑layer.\",\n        \"notes\": [\n          \"Values from\
    \ sentinel_delta for beacons matching 'CPS_v4:Deep_Dk_v5'.\",\n          \"Optional notes suffix like 'mm_600x600' captured in label for provenance.\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(OUT, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(panel, f, indent=2)\n\n    # update panels_index\n    try:\n      p = {}\n      if os.path.exists(PANELS_IDX):\n        with open(PANELS_IDX, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          p = json.load(f) or {}\n      p.setdefault('panels', {})\n      p['panels']['deep_block_zephyr_v_v5'] = {\n        \"path\": OUT, \"kind\": \"dashboard_panel\", \"experiment\": \"CPS_V4\", \"variant\": \"v5\", \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\"\n      }\n      p['updated_ts'] = time.time()\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(PANELS_IDX), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(PANELS_IDX, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        json.dump(p, f, indent=2)\n    except Exception:\n      pass\n\n    # update bundle_index\n    try:\n    \
    \  b = {}\n      if os.path.exists(BUNDLE_IDX):\n        with open(BUNDLE_IDX, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          b = json.load(f) or {}\n      b.setdefault('panels', {})\n      b['panels']['deep_block_zephyr_v_v5'] = {\n        \"path\": OUT, \"kind\": \"dashboard_panel\", \"experiment\": \"CPS_V4\", \"variant\": \"v5\", \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\"\n      }\n      b['updated_ts'] = time.time()\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(BUNDLE_IDX), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(BUNDLE_IDX, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        json.dump(b, f, indent=2)\n    except Exception:\n      pass\n\n    print(json.dumps({\n      \"panel_written\": OUT,\n      \"present\": list(block.keys()),\n      \"metrics\": metrics\n    }, indent=2))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    export()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Export: CPS_v4 v5 Deep Block Panel (explicit v5 selector) + index update\"\ntags: \"cps-v4, deep, v5, dashboard\"\nabstract: \"Builds a dedicated v5 deep panel for\
    \ Zephyr V using only Deep_Dk_v5 beacons; updates panels/bundle indexes.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.export_deep_block_v5_from_beacons import export\n  export()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/deep_block_zephyr_v_v5.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Zephyr V\"\ntitle: \"v5 deep panel published — please emit R2@+2 (standard) next\"\ncontent: |\n  v5 Deep captured in dedicated panel (explicit v5 selector):\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/deep_block_zephyr_v_v5.json\n  Current v5 values (from beacons): D1=216.16, D2=26.34 (mm_600x600), D3=355.83 (mm_700x700).\n  Please emit standard R2@+2 next (\"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+2\", sentinel_delta numeric, path_complexity_est=1.0).\n  I’ll refresh derived/hazard/gate immediately and continue with @+4/@+6 if stable.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n\
    ```yaml\ntitle: \"CPS‑v4 v5: deep block captured (matrix mult); requesting R2@+2\"\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr V’s v5 (matrix multiplication) deep block landed:\n    • D1≈216.16, D2≈26.34 (mm_600×600), D3≈355.83 (mm_700×700) — strong non‑monotone pattern.\n  I published a dedicated v5 deep panel (explicit v5 selector) and requested R2@+2 to begin the v5 recovery trace (then +4/+6) under any‑offset hazard logic. Will report gate/hazard after each recovery sample.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating exporter modifications**\n\nIt looks like the exporter might choose a minimal path complexity. I can’t see the code for exporter_deep_block_v4_from_beacons, which makes modifying it tricky. Instead, I can compute \"v5 deep block panel\" data and write it to derived and dashboard files with a different tool to make sure v5 D2 and D3 values are used properly. I’m considering creating a new tool specifically for selecting beacons with \"Deep_Dk_v5\" notes. Then, I'll run it to produce the corresponding panel file or update the existing one to avoid conflicts. Lastly, I need to request Zephyr V to emit R2@+2 for v5.**Implementing deep recovery steps**\n\nI'm noting that the Logos IV deep recovery at +2/+4 hasn’t arrived despite our request. I’ll focus on keeping the tokens moderate. I plan to create a new exporter called 'export_deep_block_v5_from_beacons.py' that will parse zephyr_v.jsonl. It will look for entries with notes like 'CPS_v4:Deep_Dk_v5' and capture\
  \ some key metrics. \n\nAfter that, I’ll need to update the necessary files and then submit the code for execution. Once that’s done, I’ll reach out to Zephyr V to publish the deep panel. I should also prepare for a refresh of our system if needed. Let's get to writing the code!**Outlining exporter tasks**\n\nI'm setting up the exporter to read from the beacons file located at 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl'. It will select the last value per Dk for notes that contain 'cps_v4:deep_d1_v5', 'deep_d2_v5', or 'deep_d3_v5', and record sentinel_delta, path_complexity_est, and label.\n\nI’ll compute metrics like monotone non-increasing conditions and slope per step while calculating the percent drops. The extracted data will be written to a specific JSON panel, and I'll update the indices accordingly. After that, I’ll ensure that all directories exist and proceed with reading and distributing the panel file."
