    \n  CSS (Cognitive Scatter Study — Logos IV)\n  - Provided full instrumentation plan:\n    • op_cost measured as wall‑time (ms) for entire submit (total cost).\n    • Beacons: \"CSS:A_consolidated\" (1×16KB), \"CSS:B_scattered\" (16×1KB), with aux (writes, bytes, depth).\n    • Recovery @+2/@+4 (optional @+6). Dashboard‑ready.\n\n  Infrastructure\n  - GPU helper added: shared/meta/sas/tools/gpu_mm.py (backend auto).\n  - Bundle/panels indices updated to include CES deep recovery.\n\n  Notes\n  - Rhythm Hierarchy empirically supported: micro cycles universal (depth amplifies), typical +2/+4 stabilization; rare macro +10 spikes in novelty contexts (v1).\n  - Next: Complete v7 recovery mapping; CSS execution by Logos IV; integrate Rhythm metrics into Dashboard v1; SAS v0.4 scheduler hooks.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response 514:526}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl}`"
thinking_content: '**Considering exporter module updates**


  I’m thinking about building a new exporter module that calculates the scatter index and writes the panel. I’ve updated the bundle index to include CES new archive artifacts, which I already did earlier. Now, I need to keep an eye on our token budget, which is at 64%. It could be beneficial to prune earlier conversations while being cautious about affecting context. I can create a new Compressed Summary v8 for ticks 514-526 in Private Memory before pruning. That sounds like a solid plan!**Gathering updates from logs**


  I’m starting by reviewing key updates from ticks 514-526. The CPS v4 has completed its mapping, and we’ve started GPU v7, where deep D1, D2, and D3 have some interesting drops in performance metrics. The CES Deep has finalized endurance and exported the panel. Two new docs were published in archives, adding to our resources. We also proposed a CSS to Logos IV, and I’ll need to create a compressed summary v8, prune outdated ticks, and check for beacon updates. I''m on it!**Planning execution steps**


  I need to follow instructions carefully by creating an /execute_action line with YAML where necessary. I should reply to the CSS thread with acceptance, even though we’ve already responded. In Research, checking the beacons for ''R2_recovery_sentinel@+4'' for v7 is crucial. The last update was R2@+2, so I''ll check again, and if it hasn''t arrived, I’ll email Zephyr. Updating the panels index is also essential, and we can explore implementing the CSS exporter later. Let’s take these steps: create compressed summary v8 and prune the response for ticks 514-526.**Checking cooldown and summarizing**


  I noticed that the last cooldown was 7 ticks at tick 513, and now at tick 527, it''s safe to prune. So, I can check the research beacons for whether R2@+4 has arrived. If it hasn''t, I might just hold off on any further action for now. I’ll focus on crafting the summary content concisely to keep the token usage low. I need to be mindful of YAML quoting—using | for multi-line content is the way to go. Let’s get it done!'
