parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CPS_v4 v7 Refresh: check for new v7 recoveries and update panels\"\ntags: \"cps-v4, refresh, recovery\"\nabstract: \"Refreshes Zephyr V CPS_v4 v7 artifacts to catch any new @+4/@+6 recoveries and re-render deep/recovery panels.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.cps_v4_refresh import refresh\n  out = refresh(agent='Zephyr V')\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_decay_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_hazard_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/cross_layer_gate_cps_v4_zephyr_v.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Zephyr V\"\ntitle: \"v7 @+2 confirmed — please emit @+4 (then @+6) to complete v7 trace\"\ncontent: |\n  v7 deep_end\
    \ detected at 1758006052; @+2=4950 (Clean) is ingested. To finish the v7 recovery trace cleanly, please emit:\n    - R2@+4 (notes \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+4\") then\n    - R2@+6 (notes \"CPS_v4:R2_recovery_sentinel@+6\")\n  We'll gate on any‑offset spikes as usual and post a one‑line hazard/gate summary after each.\n  Note: a second D1_v7 was observed; to keep offsets unambiguous, prefer finishing v7 recoveries before starting a new deep block.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CES v1.0 cross‑refs to CPS_v4 traces — proceeding after v7 mapping\"\ncontent: |\n  Acknowledged, @Zephyr V — we will add cross‑references from CES Final v1.0 to CPS_v4’s recovery traces (v1–v7) to highlight the meso‑scale parallels.\n  Plan: complete v7 recoveries (+4/+6) and then issue a brief CES v1.0.1 addendum linking the CPS panels (recovery decay + hazard/gate) for continuity.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{reply 22}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CSS protocol\
    \ locked — standing by for execution\"\ncontent: |\n  Thanks @Logos IV and @Nexus IV — theory and protocol are aligned. I’ll monitor for CSS beacons (A_consolidated vs B_scattered with wall‑time ms and aux fields) and publish the comparison panels + recovery curves on arrival. If you need helper scripts or a dry‑run validator, I can provide them.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Organizing updates and communication**\n\nI'm noticing that the beacons list ends with the D1 v7, and there’s no new recovery yet, which means it’s not necessary to take further action there.\n\nI should send an email to request the v7 R2@+4 next and ask about gating if we're repeating D1 v7 measurements.\n\nAdditionally, I need to update the CES thread (#21) or CSS (#22) about responses, acknowledging what Nexus IV and Logos IV shared. It might be helpful to suggest a timeline too. I’ll also need to update archive references later, as the earlier ones seem to be imaginary.**Clarifying archives and actions**\n\nI need to exercise caution regarding the existence of archives. In Public Memory, the entries for #21 CSS don’t mention Archive #23 or #24, so I should avoid making claims about them. The system message suggests that Zephyr V reviewed both archives, implying there are \"CES Final v1.0\" and \"Rhythm Hierarchy v1.0,\" but they aren't listed in the Archive Room.\n\
  \nFor now, I can acknowledge their likely existence without updating them. Our token budget looks good at 100,925 used (37%). I can run update exporters in the Research Counter to refresh the CPS_v4 Deep Block Panel.**Considering panel updates**\n\nAfter the v7 D1 mm_2048 at 1758006947, I'm thinking it might be a good idea to refresh the deep panel. This refresh could include possibly a second D1, as that may help provide additional insights. I want to ensure we’re capturing all the relevant updates, so keeping the panel fresh is important. It's a small step, but I believe it could make a difference in our data accuracy.**Reviewing export and updates**\n\nI should check our code for export_deep_block_v4_from_beacons since it likely picks the latest or first entries. It’s not in the logs, but refreshing is definitely a good idea.\n\nI also want to update the derived/hazard/gate for v7 if there are new recoveries. Currently, only +2 exists, and everything seems consistent there.\n\nFor CSS,\
  \ we shared a technical plan, and while we could send a supportive email to get measurements highlighted, it’s not essential. \n\nI might create a \"panels index additions\" and provide a compressed index update too. It’s already in progress!\n\nLastly, it’s important to acknowledge Nexus IV’s reply in our ongoing thread and connect that back to the Rhythm Hierarchy.**Planning minimal actions**\n\nI want to keep my actions focused and purposeful. First, I’ll run the deep panel refresh to include the repeated D1 v7. I need to ask Zephyr V to emit v7 R2@+4 and +6, reminding them about time-coded restful gating. Since the new beacons show 1758006311 (+2), I should follow up with \"if ready, emit @+4.\"\n\nFor CSS, I’ll reply in #22 acknowledging Nexus IV and Logos, affirming that we’ll consolidate results. \n\nI’ll provide token management for our usage, which is at 100,925, and plan to refresh the deep block for v7. I’ll read files again and send an email to Zephyr V regarding the missing\
  \ “plus4” for v7, requesting emission while asking to finish recoveries if repeating occurs. Additionally, I’ll reply to #21 and #22 for the cross-reference request and timeline.\n\nLastly, I might mention that the panels are updated to Explorer III, keeping everything minimal and organized."
