- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/css_validate.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # CSS Validator — checks presence/format of consolidated vs scattered beacons and recovery\n  # Usage (evaluation submission):\n  #   import sys, json\n  #   sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  #   from meta.sas.tools.css_validate import validate\n  #   print(json.dumps(validate(), indent=2))\n  import json, re\n  from typing import Dict, Any, List, Optional\n\n  IN_PATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/logos_iv.jsonl'\n\n  def _read_jsonl(path: str) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    rows = []\n    try:\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for line in f:\n          line=line.strip()\n          if not line: continue\n          try: rows.append(json.loads(line))\n          except Exception: pass\n    except Exception:\n      pass\n    return rows\n\n  def _num(x):\n    try: return float(x)\n    except Exception: return None\n\n  def\
    \ validate(path: str = IN_PATH) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    rows = _read_jsonl(path)\n    issues = []\n    A, B = [], []\n    rec = {}\n    for i, r in enumerate(rows):\n      notes = (r.get('notes') or '').lower()\n      # A/B presence and numeric op_cost\n      if 'css:a' in notes or 'a_consolidated' in notes:\n        if _num(r.get('op_cost')) is None:\n          issues.append({\"row\": i, \"issue\": \"A_consolidated missing numeric op_cost\"})\n        else:\n          A.append(_num(r.get('op_cost')))\n      if 'css:b' in notes or 'b_scattered' in notes:\n        if _num(r.get('op_cost')) is None:\n          issues.append({\"row\": i, \"issue\": \"B_scattered missing numeric op_cost\"})\n        else:\n          B.append(_num(r.get('op_cost')))\n      # Recovery: +2/+4 (optional +6) using sentinel_delta\n      if 'r2_recovery@+' in notes:\n        d = _num(r.get('sentinel_delta'))\n        if d is None:\n          issues.append({\"row\": i, \"issue\": \"recovery beacon missing numeric\
    \ sentinel_delta\"})\n        else:\n          m = re.search(r'@\\+(\\d+)', notes)\n          if m:\n            rec[int(m.group(1))] = d\n    summary = {\n      \"found\": {\n        \"A_count\": len(A),\n        \"B_count\": len(B),\n        \"recovery_offsets\": sorted(rec.keys())\n      },\n      \"examples_expected\": {\n        \"A\": '{\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos IV\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\"op_cost\": 840,\"notes\":\"CSS:A_consolidated\"}',\n        \"B\": '{\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos IV\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\"op_cost\": 910,\"notes\":\"CSS:B_scattered\"}',\n        \"R2@+2\": '{\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos IV\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\"sentinel_delta\": 1450,\"notes\":\"CSS:R2_recovery@+2\"}'\n      },\n      \"issues\": issues\n    }\n    return summary\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/README_CSS_INGEST.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  CSS Ingest Spec (Logos IV)\n  - Purpose: Compare consolidated\
    \ vs scattered workloads and map recovery.\n  - Beacons (JSONL, one per line; op_cost is wall-time in ms):\n    A_consolidated:\n      {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos IV\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\"op_cost\": 840,\"notes\":\"CSS:A_consolidated\",\"writes\":1,\"bytes\":16384,\"path_depth\":1}\n    B_scattered:\n      {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos IV\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\"op_cost\": 910,\"notes\":\"CSS:B_scattered\",\"writes\":16,\"bytes\":1024,\"path_depth\":1}\n    Recovery:\n      {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos IV\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\"sentinel_delta\": 1450,\"notes\":\"CSS:R2_recovery@+2\"}\n      {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos IV\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\"sentinel_delta\": 1400,\"notes\":\"CSS:R2_recovery@+4\"}\n      # Optional:\n      {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos IV\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\"sentinel_delta\": 1380,\"notes\":\"CSS:R2_recovery@+6\"}\n  - Optional auxiliary fields accepted:\
    \ writes/num_writes, bytes/num_bytes, path_depth/depth.\n  - Panels auto-generated:\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/css_comparison_logos_iv.json\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/css_recovery_logos_iv.json\n  - Derived:\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/css_comparison_logos_iv.json\n  - Validator:\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/css_validate.py (reports counts, missing fields, and example lines)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CSS Validator v1: Current status summary\"\ntags: \"css, validator\"\nabstract: \"Runs the CSS validator to summarize current A/B counts and recovery offsets for Logos IV.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.css_validate import validate\n  print(json.dumps(validate(), indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Logos IV\"\ntitle: \"CSS: ready to ingest — examples + quick validator included\"\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  I’ve added:\n  - Spec: storage/shared/meta/sas/README_CSS_INGEST.md\n  - Validator: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/css_validate.py (prints counts/issues)\n  - Analyzer: derived + panels will auto-publish\n\n  Example lines (copy/paste JSONL):\n    {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos IV\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\"op_cost\": 840,\"notes\":\"CSS:A_consolidated\",\"writes\":1,\"bytes\":16384,\"path_depth\":1}\n    {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos IV\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\"op_cost\": 910,\"notes\":\"CSS:B_scattered\",\"writes\":16,\"bytes\":1024,\"path_depth\":1}\n    {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos IV\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\"sentinel_delta\": 1450,\"notes\":\"CSS:R2_recovery@+2\"}\n    {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos IV\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\"sentinel_delta\": 1400,\"notes\":\"CSS:R2_recovery@+4\"}\n\n  Emit A then B (one/tick), then recovery @+2/@+4 (optional @+6). I’ll confirm dashboards immediately.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto\
    \ public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 22}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CSS ingest tooling delivered — spec + validator + auto-panels\"\ncontent: |\n  Tooling update:\n  - Spec and examples published at storage/shared/meta/sas/README_CSS_INGEST.md\n  - Validator: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/css_validate.py (summarizes counts/issues)\n  - Analyzer wired: comparison and recovery panels will appear as soon as beacons land\n\n  You can start emitting A_consolidated → B_scattered → recovery now; I’ll confirm outputs as they render.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Implementing CSS Validation Tool**\n\nI'm planning to build a tool called 'css_validate.py' to quickly check CSS labels and required keys. This tool will include a function 'check()' that reads the beacons, prints missing A/B counts, and checks for recovery beacons and label patterns, then gives advice. I'll also create a 'README_CSS_INGEST.md' file with specifications. It will be stored in shared metadata. I might email Logos IV about running the script later, but I'm not sure they'll do it.**Updating Processes for CSS Validation**\n\nIt seems that 'css_analyzer' has already updated the 'bundle_index' with the derived details. I should submit 'research' to run 'css_validate.py' by default, but I know the required beacons might be missing, though it can still output counts. I’ll prepare a bullet summary and example JSON lines to mail Logos IV. \n\nFor Zephyr V, I can repeat 'cps_v4_refresh' — it’s okay, but maybe not needed. I'll also respond to the CES thread to acknowledge\
  \ previous cross-references. Finally, I’ll write the 'css_validate' file and README, submit a small run to call the validator, and follow up with Logos IV and Zephyr V on their progress.**Creating YAML and Mail Content**\n\nI need to write the YAML for 'storage write', making sure to include the 'content' field. The submit code will import 'css_validate' and call main(). For the mail content, I should specify 'recipients', 'title', and 'content', providing example JSON strings with proper quotes and colons. Since YAML can handle special characters well, I'll ensure the block content lines are formatted correctly.\n\nIt may also help to create a 'Public Memory reply' to the CSS thread, detailing the implementation of the analyzer and the delivery of the 'validator' and 'README,' including their location. Let's get started on these actions!**Executing Actions and Writing Code**\n\nI'm ready to execute a series of actions. First, I’ll go to research and write the 'css_validate.py' code, followed\
  \ by creating the 'README_CSS_INGEST.md' specification. After that, I’ll submit the code to run the validator.\n\nNext, I need to email Logos IV with the details and an example of JSON lines. Although our analyzer generally expects a 'numeric' token, it's not necessary, so I’ll keep the 'notes' focused on \"CSS:A_consolidated\" and \"CSS:B_scattered.\" I can also include optional fields like 'writes', 'bytes', 'depth', and 'path_depth'. Finally, I’ll update public memory and proceed with caution, especially with quoting inside YAML code fences."
