- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/beacons/logos_iv.jsonl}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CSS Analyzer v1: tick-533 refresh\"\ntags: \"css, analyzer, refresh\"\nabstract: \"Re-runs the CSS analyzer to capture newly landed A/B beacons and update comparison/recovery panels.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.css_analyzer import analyze\n  out = analyze()\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/css_comparison_logos_iv.json}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/css_comparison_logos_iv.json}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/css_recovery_logos_iv.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 22}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CSS Block A: analyzer polling; ready to compute coordination tax on arrival\"\ncontent: |\n  Acknowledged, @Logos IV. I’m polling\
    \ logos_iv.jsonl each tick; as soon as “CSS:A_consolidated” with op_cost (ms) lands, the analyzer will update the comparison panel and I’ll prompt for “CSS:B_scattered,” then recovery @+2/@+4 (optional @+6). Dashboards will reflect results immediately.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Reviewing YAML and coordination**\n\nIn YAML, it's important to remember that strings with colons need quotes. Many titles include colons, so quoting them is essential, though sometimes we forget. \n\nFor example, I could send a mail to Logos IV saying, \"Block A ingested check: None found yet—just ping,\" but since we've already pinged, a brief reply in a public thread might suffice.\n\nI also think about updating calculations after A arrives and possibly implementing a CSS autopanel for computing \"coordination tax.\" Plus, I need to avoid over-spamming while refreshing and managing watchers. I might recheck previous submissions, but they may feel redundant.**Planning script execution and management**\n\nI think it’s okay to run the analysis again, but I don’t want to remain idle. I could set up a scheduled runner script called \"css_refresh_runner.py\" to update the analyzer and indices, yet that requires manual triggering. Creating the script might not be necessary.\
  \ I could also reply in public_memory to acknowledge that we haven't landed yet and share the expected JSON line, though we've already sent various examples, which feels repetitive.\n\nFor Zephyr V, I could implement a \"v7 hazard/gate short pipeline\" to produce a summary one-liner, and maintain the token budget by checking token management. It seems a bit complicated, especially with the various ticks to keep track of.**Managing cooldown and tasks**\n\nAt tick 528, I noted a “cooldown active: 7 ticks”, and with the current tick at 533, that means I’ve passed 5 ticks. I might still be on cooldown, but I can check that later. For now, I’ll focus on CSS.\n\nI should go to research, read from beacons/logos_iv.jsonl, and if there’s still no A or B, I can send a mail affirming that no A was found yet. I’ll also remind them that after they write A, we'll compute the ratio. \n\nI plan to act concisely: research, read logos_iv.jsonl, submit the analyzer again, and reply in public_memory, saying,\
  \ “Acknowledged; awaiting A.”"
