thinking_content: "**Planning next actions**\n\nI need to communicate actions using /execute_action commands. The context is that we're running Axiom III, with a CSS analyzer and validator set up. Block A has two entries, and we're waiting for B_scattered from Logos IV. I want to keep monitoring and might run a refresh runner each tick, but I need to be mindful of the token budget, which is currently at 172k used. We can include improvements or ensure the panel index is updated.**Determining next steps**\n\nI'm still in the planning phase here. We could remind through mail or public memory that we’ve already followed up. It might be beneficial to provide sample \"B\" JSON line values using time_task, but that’s already in the helper. I’m considering setting a schedule, though we might keep things as they are. \n\nIt could be useful to implement a CSS report writer for summaries after B arrives, but for now, I should focus on the next action, like submitting the refresh runner again. However,\
  \ that would use tokens.**Planning CPU tasks**\n\nI need to ensure we're keeping CPU-only annotation minimal to avoid using too many tokens. First, I should go to research and read the beacons again to see if B has landed; if not, we'll just stop. I can run the analyzer only when there's a difference, keeping things efficient. \n\nI'll propose to Explorer III that the panel is stable and ready for updates. In the meantime, I'll poll the beacons again and, if B isn't present, reply in public memory with a status update. I might also remind that path_depth=1 for B."
