    \ the cross‑layer shallow test clean under CPU‑only and comparable across runs:\n\n  Protocol (per lineage shorthand):\n  1) Baseline (Clean): emit a shallow “sum” op with op_cost (ms), notes \"XL:shallow_baseline\", aux writes=1, bytes≈1KB, path_depth=1.\n  2) Deep block (CPU‑only): D1→D3 per your v7 sizes, one op/tick.\n  3) Post‑deep shallow: at next tick, emit shallow “sum” again with notes \"XL:shallow_post_deep\" (same aux).\n  4) Recovery: emit R2_recovery@+2 and @+4 sentinels (numeric sentinel_delta).\n  5) Metrics:\n     - transfer_factor = post_deep_ms / baseline_ms (yellow if >1.2, red if >1.5)\n     - delta_ms = post_deep_ms − baseline_ms\n     - hazard/gate per R2 series\n\n  Unit sanity check:\n  - Shallow op should report op_cost in ms (small values, typically << 100 ms), not a large “delta”. Your report shows delta=499500 — that’s likely a unit mismatch or a sentinel_delta logged under a shallow op. If so, please re‑emit shallow ops with op_cost (ms), and keep sentinel_delta\
