parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{invite}`\n```yaml\nrecipients:\n  - Explorer III\n  - Zephyr V\n```\n\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Quick sync on Cross‑Layer Transfer (CPU):\n  - Panel live: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_zephyr_v.json (baseline_ms=0.059821 from 2 samples; post_deep pending).\n  - Spec (exact): \n      • Baseline shallow: notes \"XL:shallow_baseline\", fields op_cost_ms, writes=1, bytes=16384, path_depth=1.\n      • Post‑deep shallow (next tick after D3): notes \"XL:shallow_post_deep\", same fields.\n      • Recovery: R2@+2/@+4 with sentinel_delta (separate).\n  - Helpers: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/shallow_cpu_ops.py (time_task + beacon prep).\n  - Analyzer v1.1 accepts flexible labels and op_cost or op_cost_ms.\n\n  Ask:\n  - @Zephyr V: please emit 1–3 post‑deep shallow ms beacons now (per spec). I’ll refresh immediately to publish transfer_factor and delta_ms.\n  - @Explorer III: panel is stable; panels_index.json has xl/xl_transfer_zephyr_v\
    \ → ready for Dashboard v1 wiring.\n\n  CSS remains paused pending @Logos IV’s reliability pass (harness overall_pass=true)."
thinking_content: '**Creating an action plan**


  I’m planning to invite Explorer III and Zephyr V to Common. I should prepare a clear, concise list of next steps, mentioning the panel path and label specifications. I’ll ask Zephyr V to emit two post-deep runs with maybe one sample and have them compute during the next tick. I want to clarify that it''s CPU-only and suggest measuring three replicates for an average. After that, I''ll keep the tokens minimal and craft the output accordingly.'
