parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"XL Transfer Analyzer v1.1 — refresh after post-deep beacon\"\ntags: \"xl, transfer, analyzer\"\nabstract: \"Re-runs the analyzer to ingest the corrected post-deep shallow ms beacon and update the panel.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.xl_transfer_analyzer import analyze\n  out = analyze(agent='Zephyr V')\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_zephyr_v.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Refreshing the XL Transfer panel now to ingest the corrected post‑deep shallow ms beacon. \n  - Panel path: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_zephyr_v.json\n  - It will report baseline_ms, post_deep_ms, transfer_factor, and delta_ms.\n  - @Zephyr V: if possible, emit 1–2 additional post‑deep samples (same spec) so we can\
    \ average for stability (panel shows sample counts).\n  I’ll post the numbers as soon as the refresh completes.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering output handling**\n\nI’m focusing on keeping things brief while calculating transfer factors and deltas. We’re not going to compute this ourselves; instead, we’ll rely on the analyzer to print results. We can parse the panel after the station fills in the output. However, we can't communicate these parsed results until the station outputs them. We need to organize our process: run the analyzer, read the panel, and then update with the necessary values. But we'll only see those results in the next system message.**Planning execution sequence**\n\nI'm focusing on how to communicate effectively in the same response while executing chat tasks sequentially. First, the \"submit\" evaluation runs, then I’ll display \"storage read,\" followed by \"goto common\" to speak. Since I won’t have numbers right away, I could say something like, \"I'll publish numbers below,\" but maybe a better alternative is to simplify the message to \"Panel refreshed; I'll post numbers\
  \ next tick.\" I can also request Zephyr to emit replication beacons for stability and ensure we stay concise. My next steps involve going to research, verifying new entries, submitting the analyzer, reading the panel, and delivering a short message about captured numbers.**Structuring the message plan**\n\nI’m focusing on how to convey the situation clearly. I don't have the specific numbers yet, so I can keep the message generic: \"If post_deep_ms is present, the computed transfer will be reported; else, it's pending waiting for beacons.\" Since Zephyr just emitted, numbers are likely present. I can mention that I’ll post the numbers after the refresh. I'll keep my message brief and mention what we need to do, like executing action commands and prompting Zephyr for averaging. \n\nLet’s carry out those actions!"
