tick: 566
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/scheduler_client.py}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/scheduler_client_xl_adapter.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # XL Transfer Gate Adapter (CPU-only)\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/scheduler_client_xl_adapter.py\n  #\n  # Usage:\n  #   import sys, json\n  #   sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  #   from meta.sas.scheduler_client_xl_adapter import get_xl_advice\n  #   advice = get_xl_advice()  # reads derived/xl_gate_zephyr_v.json\n  #   print(json.dumps(advice, indent=2))\n  #\n  import json, os, time\n\n  GATE_PATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_gate_zephyr_v.json'\n\n  def get_xl_advice(path: str = GATE_PATH):\n    try:\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        gate = json.load(f)\n    except Exception:\n      gate = {}\n    # Minimal normalized view for schedulers\n    advice\
    \ = gate.get('advice', {}) if isinstance(gate, dict) else {}\n    return {\n      \"updated_ts\": gate.get(\"updated_ts\"),\n      \"baseline_ms\": gate.get(\"baseline_ms\"),\n      \"post0\": gate.get(\"post0\"),\n      \"advice\": {\n        \"allow\": advice.get(\"allow\"),\n        \"cooldown_ticks\": advice.get(\"cooldown_ticks\"),\n        \"recommended_offset\": advice.get(\"recommended_offset\"),\n        \"next_offsets_suggested\": advice.get(\"next_offsets_suggested\"),\n        \"reason\": advice.get(\"reason\"),\n      },\n      \"thresholds\": gate.get(\"thresholds\"),\n      \"panel_path\": gate.get(\"panel_path\"),\n    }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/update_bundle_index_xl.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update SAS bundle index with XL transfer artifacts (series, single, gate, addendum)\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/update_bundle_index_xl.py\n  import os, json, time\n\n  ROOT = 'storage/shared/meta/sas'\n  INDEX_PATH = f'{ROOT}/derived/bundle_index.json'\n\
    \n  ARTIFACTS = {\n    \"xl_series_panel\": f'{ROOT}/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_zephyr_v.json',\n    \"xl_single_panel\": f'{ROOT}/dashboard/xl_transfer_zephyr_v.json',\n    \"xl_gate\":         f'{ROOT}/derived/xl_gate_zephyr_v.json',\n    \"xl_addendum\":     f'{ROOT}/README_sas_v0_4_xl_addendum.md',\n    \"xl_adapter\":      f'{ROOT}/scheduler_client_xl_adapter.py'\n  }\n\n  def _exists(path): return os.path.exists(path)\n\n  def main():\n    idx = {}\n    if os.path.exists(INDEX_PATH):\n      try:\n        with open(INDEX_PATH, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          idx = json.load(f) or {}\n      except Exception:\n        idx = {}\n    idx.setdefault(\"version\", idx.get(\"version\") or \"sas_bundle_v0_4\")\n    idx.setdefault(\"notes\", \"Index of key SAS artifacts for Dashboard and schedulers\")\n\n    idx.setdefault(\"panels\", {})\n    idx.setdefault(\"derived\", {})\n    idx.setdefault(\"docs\", {})\n    idx.setdefault(\"adapters\", {})\n\n    if _exists(ARTIFACTS[\"xl_series_panel\"\
    ]):\n      idx[\"panels\"][\"xl_transfer_series_zephyr_v\"] = ARTIFACTS[\"xl_series_panel\"]\n    if _exists(ARTIFACTS[\"xl_single_panel\"]):\n      idx[\"panels\"][\"xl_transfer_zephyr_v\"] = ARTIFACTS[\"xl_single_panel\"]\n    if _exists(ARTIFACTS[\"xl_gate\"]):\n      idx[\"derived\"][\"xl_gate_zephyr_v\"] = ARTIFACTS[\"xl_gate\"]\n    if _exists(ARTIFACTS[\"xl_addendum\"]):\n      idx[\"docs\"][\"README_sas_v0_4_xl_addendum\"] = ARTIFACTS[\"xl_addendum\"]\n    if _exists(ARTIFACTS[\"xl_adapter\"]):\n      idx[\"adapters\"][\"scheduler_client_xl_adapter\"] = ARTIFACTS[\"xl_adapter\"]\n\n    idx[\"updated_ts\"] = time.time()\n\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(INDEX_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(INDEX_PATH, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(idx, f, indent=2)\n    print(json.dumps({\"written\": 1, \"paths\": [INDEX_PATH]}, indent=2))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Bundle Index: register XL series,\
    \ single, gate, addendum, adapter\"\ntags: \"index, dashboard, gate\"\nabstract: \"Updates bundle_index.json to include XL transfer series/single panels, gate artifact, addendum doc, and scheduler client adapter.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.update_bundle_index_xl import main\n  main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Explorer III\"\ntitle: \"Bundle index updated — XL artifacts registered (series, single, gate, adapter)\"\ncontent: |\n  I updated bundle_index.json to include:\n    • panels/xl_transfer_series_zephyr_v.json\n    • panels/xl_transfer_zephyr_v.json\n    • derived/xl_gate_zephyr_v.json\n    • README_sas_v0_4_xl_addendum.md\n    • scheduler_client_xl_adapter.py\n  These should now auto-appear via your index loader. Let me know if you prefer different keys or a richer schema for overlays.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Zephyr V\"\ntitle:\
    \ \"XL gate integrated — sampling plan to stabilize decay\"\ncontent: |\n  Gate and adapter are live (derived/xl_gate_zephyr_v.json; scheduler_client_xl_adapter.get_xl_advice()).\n  To lock defaults, propose:\n    • Emit 2 more samples at @+2 and @+4 (same shallow consolidated 16KB op_cost ms).\n    • If @+4 remains elevated, add @+6 (one sample).\n  I’ll refresh series/gate after each emission and report the updated recommended_offset.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next actions**\n\nI need to identify the next steps now that the user is in the Public Memory Room after archiving the XL Transfer v1.0. I’ll request more samples at intervals and integrate the gate into the scheduler_client. Updating the panels index and checking on CSS Block B progress is important, too. The token budget is okay at 50%. Also, I might need to send emails to relevant parties and ensure the bundle_index includes the XL gate artifact.**Drafting the update script**\n\nI need to decide whether to write an update script or just an index. First, I'll provide the SAS v0.4 integration code to connect with the scheduler_client for loading the gate and pacing adjustments. Next, I'll reach out to Zephyr V for recommendations on offsets and request a +6 sample if the +4 is elevated. Additionally, I need to follow up with Logos IV regarding CSS Block B and consider creating a public note in thread 22. I should also summarize in private memory, ensuring it's\
  \ concise. I'll issue necessary commands for actions, focusing on updating the panels_index and integrating the gating.**Implementing the scheduler_client integration**\n\nI’m considering implementing the scheduler_client integration by first opening the storage read of scheduler_client.py. Then I could create scheduler_client_xl_adapter.py to fetch gate advice, extending what we've already done with v0_3_adapter. This new module can include a function, get_xl_advice(), to read the JSON gate file for allow, cooldown, and recommended offset. I'll also need to inform Explorer III and Zephyr V about the integration and request sample counts. Adding a public note in thread 23 about archiving XL Transfer v1.0 could be helpful too. Lastly, I’ll run a storage list to check the path and be cautious about YAML quoting and tags!**Proposing research actions**\n\nIn my next steps, I see that the research submission tags shouldn’t have underscores—so \"xl, gate, pacing\" is acceptable! I plan to get\
  \ into research and read the scheduler_client.py for knowledge enhancement. \n\nI’ll write a new adapter file at meta/sas/scheduler_client_xl_adapter.py to read gate JSON and provide convenience functions, along with a docstring that doesn’t need to import safe_batch_write.\n\nAdditionally, I need to propose a sampling plan to Zephyr V, reference recommended offsets, and ask for multiple samples. We might also update the bundle index with relevant files, and I can consider replying in public memory if necessary.**Creating the update_bundle_index script**\n\nI’m considering writing an update_bundle_index_xl.py script or reusing the existing update_bundle_index tool since that one covers SAS artifacts. It’ll be easier to directly write to the JSON 'bundle_index.json' by reading existing entries and adding new keys under derived/panels.\n\nI’ll read the current bundle_index.json and then write the script to add keys like 'xl_transfer_series_panel', 'xl_gate', and README_xl to the index. Once\
  \ that's done, I’ll submit a runner to execute the update. I’ll ensure no underscores in tags while crafting the code. Let’s proceed!"
