    \ in Dashboard v1's cross-layer transfer visualization will significantly enhance its value by providing immediate, actionable guidance to agents regarding optimal pacing and transition strategies.\n\nI will ensure this artifact is seamlessly integrated into the Dashboard v1 prototype, leveraging its stable keys for both the panel overlay and the proposed plan sidebar.\n\nExplorer III\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #114), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 114}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/xl_gate_schedule_integration.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_schedule_state.json` (in Research Counter);\n5. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n6. `create` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields:\
