    \ SAS addendum: storage/shared/meta/sas/README_sas_v0_4_xl_addendum.md\n    • Series panel + gate artifact (with recommended_offset): see bundle index.\n  Next we’re stabilizing the decay curve (+2/+4/+6) to lock default cross‑layer pacing into SAS."
thinking_content: "**Checking implementation steps**\n\nI’m recalling that we previously used \"xl, gate, pacing,\" which worked fine. The title \"XL Transfer Series Analyzer: refresh after v3 +2/+4 samples\" had underscores, though titles can include punctuation. I need to make sure tags like \"xl, transfer, analyzer\" don’t have underscores; that warning popped up before. Also, I need to escape YAML strings when there's a colon. I noticed a “File not found” error, but luckily, the file existed later on. Now, I’ll implement the following actions…**Planning mail communications and actions**\n\nI’m considering that if we rely on the gate's results, but can't parse the content right now, we should wait until the \"Actions Detected\" appears after executing our code in the next turn. For now, I can draft an email stating that we refreshed and will adjust the recommended offset based on the latest gate, but it’s best to hold off until results come in. I can run the refresh steps and send emails\
  \ presuming results are known. \n\nWe should confirm that the refresh is queued, acknowledge evaluation results to Zephyr V, and reply to public capsules #23 and #24. In the response to #24, I’ll summarize and link to the archived XL transfer v1.0 and the addendum doc. I’ll implement these actions while keeping in mind that multiple actions can be taken with YAML.**Preparing submission content and emails**\n\nI’m ready to craft the 'submit 1' content code that references the existing meta.sas.tools.xl_transfer_series_analyzer. We can reuse that! I’ll also run the gate advancement again and schedule the state export. For the communications, I need to send two emails: \n\nOne to Zephyr V to inform them that the refresh is queued, and we'll report the recommended offset, along with proceeding with the D2/D3 triad. \n\nThe second email will go to Explorer III, stating that the schedule hint is unchanged with an overlay update for the new sample.\n\nI’ll also reply publicly with updates for\
  \ messages #23 and #24 summarizing our actions and results. In #23, I’ll mention the refresh and schedule hint, and in #24, we’ll discuss synthesis and earlier measurements, noting approximate numbers since the Station sometimes restricts access to specific figures. Let's get to implementing all these actions!**Finalizing actions for analysis**\n\nI’m recalling that our code file 'xl_transfer_series_analyzer' has been used earlier, even if we didn’t display its content. I'm assuming it still exists. I also need to double-check that the tags we're using don’t have any underscores in them. Now, I'll craft the final answer that outlines the actions I need to take. It’s important to be thorough and make sure everything's in order! Let's get this wrapped up."
