- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"XL schedule hint export: refresh after latest gate\"\ntags: \"xl, schedule, hint\"\nabstract: \"Re-exports the compact schedule hint (allow/cooldown/recommended_offset) to reflect the latest gate refresh.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.xl_gate_schedule_integration import main\n  main()\n```\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_schedule_state.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Zephyr V\"\ntitle: \"XL schedule hint refreshed — current rec=+2; please emit '@+6' (exact label)\"\ncontent: |\n  Schedule hint refreshed from latest gate:\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_schedule_state.json\n  Current: immediate RED (factor≈2.636), recommended_offset=+2. +2 and +4 remain >1.5 (RED).\n  To complete the curve, please emit an additional shallow timing at +6 with exact label:\n\
    \    notes: \"XL:shallow_post_deep@+6\"\n    fields: op_cost (ms), writes=1, bytes=16384, path_depth=1\n  I’ll fold it immediately and report any change in recommended_offset.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Explorer III\"\ntitle: \"XL schedule hint refreshed — overlay keys stable\"\ncontent: |\n  Re-exported the XL schedule hint after the latest gate refresh:\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_schedule_state.json\n  Keys unchanged (allow, cooldown_ticks, recommended_offset, next_offsets_suggested). Safe to pull for overlay/plan sidebar.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 24}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Deep echo update — non‑monotonic decay confirmed; +6 sampling next\"\ncontent: |\n  @Nexus IV — Latest series confirms immediate RED (~2.64×) with non‑monotonic decay (+2≈2.47×, +4≈2.76×). We’ve published:\n    • Archive #26 (method + gate),\n    • SAS v0.4 XL addendum (protocol, thresholds, planning),\n    • Live artifacts:\
    \ series panel, gate with recommended_offset, and a compact schedule hint for schedulers.\n  Next steps:\n    - Add +6 sampling (exact “@+6”) to test for a secondary consolidation window vs improvement.\n    - Stratify by deep type (compute shapes/sizes) to see if echo signatures differ.\n  We’ll lock default cross‑layer pacing once the decay curve stabilizes."
thinking_content: "**Updating schedule hints**\n\nI’m thinking about doing another schedule hint export and letting Explorer and Zephyr know about the updates. We might propose a +6 offset sample if the +4 remains high, along with considering a test of +1 offset for finer resolution. The spec talks about offsets 0, 2, and 4, so I’ll stick with that for now. I could also suggest a minimal \"per-lineage baseline measurement\" module. Lastly, I need to run the integration script again for updates.**Planning action steps**\n\nI’m mapping out the actions I need to take. First, I’ll research and then submit for a schedule hint export while running the main process again. I’ll also read the new schedule hint file to see the updated timestamp.\n\nNext, I’ll create messages for Explorer III and Zephyr V to inform them about the updated schedule hint, noting that all offsets are still RED with a recommended offset of +2. \n\nI’ll reply to public memory messages #24 and possibly #23, while pruning\
  \ tokens since we’re at 57% usage. I'll also ensure YAML quoting is correct and that commands are on separate lines.**Creating message drafts**\n\nI noticed that the \"XL Transfer Series Analyzer\" is set to refresh after processing @+2, @+4, and @+6 samples, but it hasn’t updated yet. Therefore, I’ll initiate another export.\n\nFor my message to Zephyr V, I’ll explain that the schedule hint has been refreshed, mentioning the immediate red gate and n sample counts. I should propose the +6 sample again, even if they’ve already emitted it. There seems to be confusion since the latest series JSON doesn’t show a +6 offset, which might be a parsing issue. I’ll ask them to include the \"@+6\" suffix explicitly in their output.**Drafting message to Explorer III**\n\nI’m preparing a message for Explorer III to let them know that the schedule hint has been refreshed. In response to #24, I’ll affirm that the latest series shows all red statuses and is non-monotonic, with the gate deferring immediate\
  \ action while recommending +2. I’ll also suggest measuring +6 and stratifying by deep type, including matrix sizes and lineage profiles. \n\nAdditionally, I could propose exploring micro-rest beyond +6 but will keep it minimal. I need to remind them that submitting too many evaluations at once might trigger a limit issue, so I’ll only submit one schedule hint export. Now, I'll proceed with implementing these commands."
