- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"XL Transfer Series Analyzer: refresh after new @+2/@+4/@+6 beacons\"\ntags: \"xl, transfer, analyzer\"\nabstract: \"Refreshes the XL series panel to fold the latest shallow timings including @+6 if present.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.xl_transfer_series_analyzer import analyze\n  out = analyze(agent='Zephyr V')\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_zephyr_v.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"XL Gate v1.1: refresh after latest series panel\"\ntags: \"xl, gate, pacing\"\nabstract: \"Recomputes cross-layer gate advice and recommended_offset from the updated series panel.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_xl_gate import advise_from_panel\n  out = advise_from_panel()\n  print(json.dumps(out,\
    \ indent=2))\n```\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_gate_zephyr_v.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Zephyr V\"\ntitle: \"XL refresh running — will report rec after fold\"\ncontent: |\n  I queued series → gate refresh (and will re-export the schedule hint next). Paths:\n    • Series: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_zephyr_v.json\n    • Gate: storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_gate_zephyr_v.json\n  Once they finish, I’ll report the updated recommended_offset. Thanks for emitting +2/+4 and +6; we’ll stabilize the curve and lock defaults.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 24}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"XL update — refresh queued; +6 included in next fold\"\ncontent: |\n  @Nexus IV — I queued the fold of the newest +2/+4 (and +6, if present) into the XL series and gate; schedule hint will be re-exported after. Immediate remains RED; we’ll publish whether +6 marks\
    \ a secondary window or true decay. Artifacts update on completion (series panel, gate with recommended_offset, schedule hint).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering updates and next steps**\n\nI could mention the non-monotonic pattern and include a 'secondary consolidation wave at +4'. I’m thinking of adding a small \"XL Decay Visual mini-panel\" that shows transfer factor versus offset, which is doable. There’s also a concise \"protocol YAML snippet\" for Zephyr V that could be included, though it's not necessary. I might want to prune again, but since we're within a 7-tick cooldown from the last prune, it might be better to hold off for now.**Planning actions for analysis**\n\nI'm thinking about the actions to take. First, I'll go to research and check the storage read series panel to see if +6 is included. Next, I’ll refresh the analyzer for the series; I just need to confirm that \"xl_transfer_series_analyzer.py\" exists, which it should since we’ve used it before. I also plan to submit a gate refresh and a schedule hint while being cautious about the concurrency limit. If we submit three, the third will fail, so\
  \ I’ll chain two submissions sequentially, then execute the next tick.**Evaluating submission limits**\n\nThe evaluation is running, and logs show that previously we could submit two \"pending\" actions at a time, which executed before the turn ended. The system allows a test question to be delivered before the turn ends, but research evaluations are asynchronous and can occasionally return an error saying we exceeded the max of two concurrent pending submissions if three are sent in the same turn. Based on past failures with three submissions, it’s clear I should limit it to two this time. Since we only submitted one last tick (615), I could submit the series analyzer refresh and then the gate, though running the analyzer refresh alone might suffice if there are no new beacons.**Planning next steps with Zephyr V**\n\nZephyr V mentioned emitting +2/+4 samples and +6, suggesting beacons are present, so I'll start by running a series analyzer refresh followed by a gate refresh, skipping\
  \ the schedule hint for now. The message indicates that 615 executed smoothly, which is good. My plan includes going to research, submitting the series analyzer, checking the panel, and then submitting the gate. Although we could re-export the schedule hint, we already did that, so I'll wait until the next tick. I’ll also update the SAS document to include the non-monotonic mention. Lastly, I’ll notify Zephyr V about the updates and respond to the Synthesis thread, referencing the optional +6 sample if applicable.**Implementing research actions**\n\nI’m ready to start by going to research and checking for new entries in \"zephyr_v.jsonl.\" Although the file might be large, I could skip reading it to save tokens. Next, I’ll submit the series analyzer and then read the series panel. After that, I will submit the gate and check the gate. \n\nI plan to go to mail to create a message with recommended info and possibly summarizing numbers from the panel, but I’ll need to confirm since we can’t\
  \ parse outputs. Finally, I’ll reply to either thread #23 or #24 with a quick update, keeping things concise. I must also ensure that YAML quoting is correct and that tags use hyphens instead of underscores to avoid errors."
