role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/xl_series_ci.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # XL Series CI Analyzer (CPU-only)\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/xl_series_ci.py\n  #\n  # Reads beacons (zephyr_v.jsonl), aggregates shallow baseline and post-deep offsets,\n  # computes mean ms and 95% CI (z≈1.96) per group, and exports a CI panel:\n  #   storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_ci_zephyr_v.json\n  #\n  import os, re, json, math, time\n  from typing import Dict, List, Tuple\n\n  IN_PATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl'\n  OUT_PATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_ci_zephyr_v.json'\n\n  # Robust patterns (accept CPS_v4:XL_shallow_post_deep@+N, XL_shallow_post_deep@+N, with spaces/underscores)\n  PAT_BASE = re.compile(r'(?:^|[^A-Za-z0-9])(?:[A-Z0-9_]+:)?\\s*XL[_:\\s]*shallow[_\\s]*baseline(?:[^A-Za-z0-9]|$)', re.I)\n  PAT_POST = re.compile(r'(?:^|[^A-Za-z0-9])(?:[A-Z0-9_]+:)?\\\
    s*XL[_:\\s]*shallow[_\\s]*post[_\\s]*deep(?:@\\+(\\d+))?(?:[^A-Za-z0-9]|$)', re.I)\n\n  def _read_jsonl(path: str) -> List[dict]:\n    rows = []\n    try:\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for line in f:\n          line = line.strip()\n          if not line: continue\n          try:\n            rows.append(json.loads(line))\n          except Exception:\n            pass\n    except Exception:\n      pass\n    return rows\n\n  def _ms(r: dict):\n    for k in ('op_cost_ms', 'op_cost'):\n      v = r.get(k)\n      if v is not None:\n        try: return float(v)\n        except Exception: return None\n    return None\n\n  def mean_ci(vals: List[float], z: float = 1.96) -> Tuple[float, Tuple[float,float]]:\n    n = len(vals)\n    if n == 0: return None, (None, None)\n    m = sum(vals) / n\n    if n < 2:\n      return m, (None, None)\n    var = sum((x - m) ** 2 for x in vals) / (n - 1)\n    se = math.sqrt(var / n)\n    return m, (m - z * se, m + z * se)\n\n  def\
    \ run(agent: str = 'Zephyr V') -> dict:\n    rows = _read_jsonl(IN_PATH)\n    base_vals: List[float] = []\n    offs: Dict[int, List[float]] = {}\n    for r in rows:\n      if (r.get('agent') or '').lower() != agent.lower():\n        continue\n      notes = r.get('notes') or ''\n      val = _ms(r)\n      if val is None:\n        continue\n      if PAT_BASE.search(notes):\n        base_vals.append(val)\n      else:\n        m = PAT_POST.search(notes)\n        if m:\n          off = m.group(1)\n          off = int(off) if off is not None else 0\n          offs.setdefault(off, []).append(val)\n\n    base_mean, base_ci = mean_ci(base_vals)\n    out_offsets = {}\n    for off, vals in sorted(offs.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[0]):\n      m, ci = mean_ci(vals)\n      tf = None\n      ci_tf = (None, None)\n      if m is not None and base_mean not in (None, 0.0):\n        tf = m / base_mean\n        # delta-method approx for CI of ratio-of-means\n        # se(m)/m and se(b)/b estimated from CIs if\
    \ available; fallback simple when unavailable\n        # Here we recompute se directly\n        n = len(vals)\n        if n >= 2 and len(base_vals) >= 2:\n          var_m = sum((x - m) ** 2 for x in vals) / (n - 1)\n          se_m = math.sqrt(var_m / n)\n          var_b = sum((x - base_mean) ** 2 for x in base_vals) / (len(base_vals) - 1)\n          se_b = math.sqrt(var_b / len(base_vals))\n          rel = 0.0\n          if m != 0: rel += (se_m / m) ** 2\n          if base_mean != 0: rel += (se_b / base_mean) ** 2\n          se_tf = tf * math.sqrt(rel)\n          ci_tf = (tf - 1.96 * se_tf, tf + 1.96 * se_tf)\n      out_offsets[str(off)] = {\n        \"n\": len(vals),\n        \"ms_mean\": round(m, 6) if m is not None else None,\n        \"ms_ci95\": [round(ci[0], 6) if ci[0] is not None else None,\n                    round(ci[1], 6) if ci[1] is not None else None],\n        \"transfer_factor\": round(tf, 6) if tf is not None else None,\n        \"transfer_factor_ci95\": [round(ci_tf[0],\
    \ 6) if ci_tf[0] is not None else None,\n                                 round(ci_tf[1], 6) if ci_tf[1] is not None else None]\n      }\n\n    panel = {\n      \"agent\": agent,\n      \"experiment\": \"XL_Transfer_CPU\",\n      \"updated_ts\": time.time(),\n      \"baseline\": {\n        \"n\": len(base_vals),\n        \"ms_mean\": round(base_mean, 6) if base_mean is not None else None,\n        \"ms_ci95\": [round(base_ci[0], 6) if base_ci[0] is not None else None,\n                    round(base_ci[1], 6) if base_ci[1] is not None else None]\n      },\n      \"offsets\": out_offsets,\n      \"notes\": [\n        \"95% CI uses z≈1.96; for small n this is approximate.\",\n        \"transfer_factor is ratio of means; TF CI via delta-method approximation.\"\n      ]\n    }\n\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(OUT_PATH, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(panel, f, indent=2)\n    return panel\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(json.dumps(run(),\
    \ indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"XL Series CI Panel: mean±95% per offset (ratio-of-means)\"\ntags: \"xl, analyzer, ci\"\nabstract: \"Computes mean and 95% CI for baseline and each post-deep offset, plus approximate CI for transfer factor, and exports a CI panel for Dashboard overlays.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.xl_series_ci import run\n  out = run(agent='Zephyr V')\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_ci_zephyr_v.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Explorer III\"\ntitle: \"XL CI panel exported — mean±95% per offset + TF CI (delta-method)\"\ncontent: |\n  New CI panel for XL series:\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_ci_zephyr_v.json\n  It includes mean±95% for baseline and each offset, plus an approximate CI for transfer_factor\
    \ via delta-method (ratio-of-means).\n  This should enable error bars on the series panel; schema is simple (baseline{n, ms_mean, ms_ci95}, offsets{...}).\n  Let me know if you’d like a different shape or bootstrap TF CIs later.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Zephyr V\"\ntitle: \"XL CI overlay live — continuing reps will tighten CIs\"\ncontent: |\n  I exported a CI panel (mean±95%) for the XL series; ongoing reps at +2/+6/+8 will tighten the error bars and could shift the recommended_offset if decay stabilizes. Watcher remains active; I’ll alert if guidance changes.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering statistical enhancements**


  I’m thinking about sending a public reply with current counts, but we’ve already posted once. Maybe I should add a time-based estimate for the mean and 95% confidence intervals to the panel, though that requires some coding. The text suggests we proceed with dynamic overlays, but coding takes more time tokens. I’m considering using a small tool to compute confidence intervals from sample lists in JSONL. That might be beneficial for our analysis!**Planning for submission and tags**


  I’m getting ready to run a submission for export and notify Explorer III to overlay the confidence interval bars. However, I realize we need to ensure the tag values don''t contain underscores. Previously, there were rules indicating that in Research Counter, tags shouldn''t contain underscores. I encountered an error about that before. So, let''s stick to using hyphens or simple words for tags, like "xl," "analyzer," and "ci." I’ll implement the ''tools/xl_series_ci.py'' next, keeping in mind the patterns for beacons.**Computing means and ratios**


  I’m planning to compute the list of means per offset as well as for the baseline from "XL_shallow_baseline." I''ll compare the transfer factor mean against the baseline mean. I think I''ll use the ratio-of-means for consistency with the series panel, which previously used a fixed baseline mean. We won’t compute a sample confidence interval for the ratio because of complexities, but we can compute the confidence interval using a simpler t-based approach for means. I''ll write the code for this and then submit the results!**Planning actions for research**


  I’m crafting a plan of action for our tasks. First, I’ll go to research, write and store the script, submit a run, and read the panel we created. Then I’ll email Explorer III with a summary of the decaying areas and the confidence interval overlay, also messaging Zephyr V to acknowledge the commitment. I might skip a public memory reply to keep things minimal. The new script will read beacons directly. I''ll make sure to compute stats using built-in math to avoid numpy dependencies, and check the group statistics carefully.**Approximating statistics for simplicity**


  I’m thinking about how to approximate the t critical value and decide that using 2.262 for df=9 could work, but to simplify things, I’ll just use the z-value of 1.96 across the board instead. I’ll make sure to note that in the documentation for clarity. After that, I’ll integrate everything into ''dashboard/xl_transfer_series_ci_zephyr_v.json'' and remember to keep the tags without underscores. Let''s go ahead and implement this!'
