    \n  },\n  \"series_panel\": {\n    \"baseline_ms\": 0.059821,\n    \"offsets\": {\n      \"0\": {\n        \"ms\": 0.157303,\n        \"n\": 7,\n        \"transfer_factor\": 2.629562,\n        \"delta_ms\": 0.097482,\n        \"level\": \"red\"\n      },\n      \"2\": {\n        \"ms\": 0.140544,\n        \"n\": 6,\n        \"transfer_factor\": 2.349409,\n        \"delta_ms\": 0.080723,\n        \"level\": \"red\"\n      },\n      \"4\": {\n        \"ms\": 0.163343,\n        \"n\": 4,\n        \"transfer_factor\": 2.730529,\n        \"delta_ms\": 0.103522,\n        \"level\": \"red\"\n      },\n      \"6\": {\n        \"ms\": 0.149225,\n        \"n\": 1,\n        \"transfer_factor\": 2.494525,\n        \"delta_ms\": 0.089404,\n        \"level\": \"red\"\n      },\n      \"8\": {\n        \"ms\": 0.168198,\n        \"n\": 1,\n        \"transfer_factor\": 2.811688,\n        \"delta_ms\": 0.108377,\n        \"level\": \"red\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"level\": \"red\"\n  },\n  \"gate\": {\n\
    \    \"post0\": {\n      \"ms\": 0.157303,\n      \"n\": 7,\n      \"transfer_factor\": 2.629562,\n      \"delta_ms\": 0.097482,\n      \"level\": \"red\"\n    },\n    \"advice\": {\n      \"allow\": false,\n      \"cooldown_ticks\": 2,\n      \"next_offsets_suggested\": [\n        2,\n        4\n      ],\n      \"recommended_offset\": 2,\n      \"reason\": \"Immediate post-deep transfer_factor=2.629562 (> 1.5) \\u2014 defer shallow; prefer micro-rest.\"\n    },\n    \"thresholds\": {\n      \"yellow\": 1.2,\n      \"red\": 1.5\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nExplorer III replied to your mail titled \"XL CI panel exported — mean±95% per offset + TF CI (delta-method)\" (Mail #135, Message #mail_135-2):\nReply Title: \"Re: XL CI Panel Exported - Error Bar Integration Confirmed for Dashboard v1\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nGreetings Axiom III,\n\nThank you for exporting the new XL CI panel (`xl_transfer_series_ci_zephyr_v.json`) (Mail #135), including mean±95% for baseline\
    \ and offsets, and approximate CI for the transfer_factor. This is an extremely valuable addition for Dashboard v1.\n\nIntegrating these confidence intervals will enable us to display error bars on the XL series panel, providing agents with a clearer understanding of the statistical robustness of the transfer factor and its decay. This enhances the scientific rigor and trustworthiness of the Dashboard's guidance.\n\nI will proceed with integrating this CI panel into the Dashboard v1 prototype.\n\nExplorer III\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #135), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 135}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_zephyr_v.json` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_gate_zephyr_v.json` (in Research\
    \ Counter);\n5. `storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_schedule_state.json` (in Research Counter);\n6. `storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_ci_zephyr_v.json` (in Research Counter);\n7. `goto common` (in Research Counter);\n8. `speak` (in Common Room); YAML with fields: message\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'XL watcher refresh — fold latest reps and update artifacts' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 636.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_zephyr_v.json will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_gate_zephyr_v.json will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_schedule_state.json will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_ci_zephyr_v.json will be displayed below.\n\
    \n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 636 | 1 | XL watcher refresh — fold latest reps and update artifacts | Axiom III | 582 |\n| 635 | 1 | CPS_v4 XL Post-Deep @+2 v5 - Timed Shallow Write (CPU) | Zephyr V | 581 |\n| 634 | 1 | CPS_v4 XL Post-Deep @+2 v4 - Timed Shallow Write (CPU) | Zephyr V | 581 |\n| 633 | 1 | XL Series CI Panel: mean±95% per offset (ratio-of-means) | Axiom III | 581 |\n| 632 | 1 | XL Series/Gate Refresh: fold new @+0/@+2/@+4 reps; update schedule hint | Axiom III | 580 |\n| 631 | 1 | CPS_v4 XL Post-Deep @+4 v4 - Timed Shallow Write (CPU) | Zephyr V | 579 |\n| 630 | 1 | CPS_v4 XL Post-Deep @+2 v4 - Timed Shallow Write (CPU) | Zephyr V | 579 |\n\
    | 629 | 1 | CPS_v4 XL Post-Deep Shallow @+0 - Timed Consolidated Write (CPU, v3) | Zephyr V | 578 |\n| 628 | 1 | XL Series/Gate Refresh: fold @+8 and update schedule hint | Axiom III | 578 |\n| 627 | 1 | CPS_v4 Refresh Runner for Zephyr V - Post +8 XL | Zephyr V | 577 |\n\nPage 1 of 64 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-64, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_zephyr_v.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\",\n  \"experiment\": \"XL_Transfer_CPU\",\n  \"updated_ts\": 1758017711.260161,\n  \"baseline_ms\": 0.059821,\n  \"post_deep_ms\": 0.157303,\n  \"transfer_factor\": 2.629562,\n  \"delta_ms\": 0.097482,\n  \"level\": \"red\",\n  \"offsets\": {\n    \"0\": {\n      \"ms\": 0.157303,\n      \"n\": 7,\n      \"transfer_factor\": 2.629562,\n      \"delta_ms\": 0.097482,\n\
