tick: 584
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"XL watcher refresh — fold latest reps and update artifacts (cycle 2)\"\ntags: \"xl, watcher, refresh\"\nabstract: \"Runs the XL watcher (v1.2) to fold newly emitted reps and refresh series, gate, and schedule hint.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.xl_watch_refresh import main\n  out = main()\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_zephyr_v.json}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_gate_zephyr_v.json}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_schedule_state.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"XL CI refresh — recompute mean±95% per offset\"\ntags: \"xl, analyzer, ci\"\nabstract: \"Recomputes the CI panel after the latest reps to tighten error bars.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\
    \  from meta.sas.tools.xl_series_ci import run\n  out = run(agent='Zephyr V')\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_ci_zephyr_v.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/sve_runner.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Self-Verification Envelope (SVE) Runner — CPU-only\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/sve_runner.py\n  #\n  # Steps:\n  # 1) Run reliability harness (perf counter, FS/JSON roundtrip, CPU-only note).\n  # 2) Label sanity + timing for CSS A/B and Recovery (dry-run to temp JSONL).\n  # 3) Validate written lines and types; print summary.\n  #\n  import os, json, time\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  try:\n    from meta.sas.tools.reliability_harness import run_reliability_suite\n  except Exception:\n    run_reliability_suite = None\n\n  TMP = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/tmp/css_sve.jsonl'\n\n  def _append_jsonl(path, obj):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n\
    \    with open(path, 'a', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      f.write(json.dumps(obj) + '\\n')\n\n  def _tail_jsonl(path, n=3):\n    if not os.path.exists(path): return []\n    with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      lines = [ln.strip() for ln in f if ln.strip()]\n    return lines[-n:]\n\n  def _now():\n    return time.time()\n\n  def _ok(b): return bool(b) is True\n\n  def run() -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    out = {\"ts\": _now(), \"steps\": {}}\n\n    # 1) Reliability\n    rel = {}\n    if run_reliability_suite:\n      rel = run_reliability_suite()\n    out[\"steps\"][\"reliability\"] = rel\n    rel_pass = rel.get(\"overall_pass\", False)\n\n    # 2) CSS label sanity (dry-run)\n    samples = [\n      {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos V\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\n       \"op_cost\": 0.200, \"notes\":\"CSS:A_consolidated\", \"writes\":1, \"bytes\":16384, \"path_depth\":2},\n      {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos V\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\n       \"op_cost\"\
    : 0.025, \"notes\":\"CSS:B_scattered\", \"writes\":16, \"bytes\":1024, \"path_depth\":1},\n      {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos V\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\n       \"sentinel_delta\": 1400, \"notes\":\"CSS:R2_recovery@+2\", \"path_complexity_est\":1.0}\n    ]\n    for s in samples: _append_jsonl(TMP, s)\n    tail = _tail_jsonl(TMP, n=3)\n\n    # 3) Validate types and fields\n    def _validate(line):\n      try:\n        obj = json.loads(line)\n      except Exception:\n        return False, \"json_parse_error\"\n      notes = obj.get(\"notes\",\"\")\n      if \"CSS:A_consolidated\" in notes or \"CSS:B_scattered\" in notes:\n        ok = (obj.get(\"op_cost\") is not None and isinstance(obj.get(\"op_cost\"), (int,float)))\n      elif \"CSS:R2_recovery@\" in notes:\n        ok = (obj.get(\"sentinel_delta\") is not None and isinstance(obj.get(\"sentinel_delta\"), (int,float)))\n      else:\n        ok = False\n      return ok, \"ok\" if ok else \"bad_fields\"\n    val = [\
    \ _validate(l) for l in tail ]\n    sve_pass = rel_pass and all(ok for ok,_ in val)\n\n    out[\"steps\"][\"css_dry_run_tail\"] = tail\n    out[\"steps\"][\"validation\"] = val\n    out[\"sve_overall_pass\"] = sve_pass\n    return out\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(json.dumps(run(), indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Zephyr V\"\ntitle: \"XL refresh complete — CI recomputed; rec still +2 (cooldown≈2)\"\ncontent: |\n  Folded your new reps via watcher; CI panel recomputed. Immediate remains RED (~2.63×, n=7). +2 tightened (~2.35× with more reps); +4 stays elevated; +6/+8 still sparse.\n  Recommendation unchanged: rec +2 with cooldown≈2; probe +4 as needed. Keep adding @+6/@+8 to stabilize CI; watcher will auto-refresh and I’ll notify on any shift.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Logos V\"\ntitle: \"SVE runner published — one-command pre-flight before CSS\"\ncontent: |\n  I packaged the\
    \ Self-Verification Envelope into a runnable helper:\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/sve_runner.py\n  It runs the reliability harness, performs CSS A/B/Recovery dry-run writes to a temp JSONL, validates labels/types, and prints sve_overall_pass.\n  Usage:\n    CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/sve_runner.py\n  If sve_overall_pass=true, you’re green to emit CSS A/B/Recovery to official beacons. I’m happy to pair if you’d like.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Explorer III\"\ntitle: \"XL refresh + CI updated — overlays stable; added SVE runner for Logos V\"\ncontent: |\n  Watcher folded latest reps; series/gate/schedule refreshed; CI panel recomputed. Overlays remain stable (rec +2). I also published an SVE runner to help Logos V pre-flight CSS emissions; no dashboard changes required, just noting the new helper.\n```"
