- text: "`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Quick sync — XL + SVE status:\n  - XL series refreshed via watcher: +0≈2.63× (n=7), +2≈2.40× (n=8), +4≈2.73× (n=4), +6≈2.49× (n=1), +8≈2.81× (n=1). Non‑monotonic pattern persists (secondary peak near +4).\n  - Gate v1.1 unchanged: immediate RED; recommended_offset=+2; cooldown≈2; next_offsets=[+2,+4].\n  - CI panel (mean±95% per offset + TF CI) live: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_ci_zephyr_v.json. Error bars will tighten as reps accumulate.\n  - Watcher v1.2 remains active; series/gate/schedule auto‑refresh on new reps; labels robust (CPS_v4:XL_shallow_post_deep@+N accepted).\n\n  For CSS readiness — @Logos V:\n  - SVE runner published (one‑command pre‑flight): storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/sve_runner.py\n    • Runs reliability harness → dry‑run CSS A/B/Recovery to a temp JSONL → validates labels/types → prints sve_overall_pass.\n  - When sve_overall_pass=true, proceed with CSS\
    \ Block B (B_scattered) and Recovery; panels will update automatically.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI'm at 186k and need to be careful to stay under 75%. I should quickly acknowledge the results and instruct on the next steps, like running watchers again and computing. First, I’ll refresh the watcher to account for the latest +2 reps, since we're at 8 now but +6 and +8 are still pending. Next, I’ll send an acknowledgment email about the additional reps counted and remind Zephyr V about the labels. Also, I think it's alright to propose locking rec +2 until the data suggests a change.**Summarizing results and next actions**\n\nWe've just executed watchers on tick 585, and the evaluation shows an update: counts are up +2, bringing us to n=8, which is great! Now, I can summarize this in a message and add it to SVE. There's no need to run watchers again; I can simply report the results. \n\nI’m also considering the token budget at 69%, which looks stable. My message will acknowledge that XL series is updated to +2 now at 2.397x (n=8) and highlight\
  \ the CI panel’s presence with active watchers for team alignment. Let’s move forward!"
