parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/xl_policy_export.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # XL Policy Exporter — synthesize gate + waves into actionable policy\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/xl_policy_export.py\n  import os, json, time\n\n  GATE = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_gate_zephyr_v.json'\n  WAVES = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_waves_zephyr_v.json'\n  SERIES_CI = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_ci_zephyr_v.json'\n  OUT = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_policy_zephyr_v.json'\n\n  def _read(path):\n    try:\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return json.load(f)\n    except Exception:\n      return {}\n\n  def main():\n    gate = _read(GATE) or {}\n    waves = _read(WAVES) or {}\n    series_ci = _read(SERIES_CI) or {}\n\n    advice = gate.get('advice') or {}\n    thresholds = gate.get('thresholds') or {\"yellow\": 1.2, \"red\": 1.5}\n    avoid = (waves.get('recommendations')\
    \ or {}).get('avoid_offsets_if_elevated') or []\n    rec_off = advice.get('recommended_offset')\n    baseline = gate.get('baseline_ms') or (series_ci.get('baseline') or {}).get('mean_ms')\n\n    policy = {\n      \"agent\": gate.get(\"agent\", \"Zephyr V\"),\n      \"updated_ts\": time.time(),\n      \"baseline_ms\": baseline,\n      \"immediate\": {\n        \"allow\": advice.get(\"allow\"),\n        \"cooldown_ticks\": advice.get(\"cooldown_ticks\"),\n        \"factor\": (gate.get(\"post0\") or {}).get(\"transfer_factor\"),\n        \"level\": (gate.get(\"post0\") or {}).get(\"level\"),\n        \"reason\": advice.get(\"reason\")\n      },\n      \"default_micro_rest_offset\": rec_off,\n      \"avoid_offsets_if_elevated\": sorted(avoid),\n      \"thresholds\": thresholds,\n      \"windows\": {\n        \"preferred_offsets\": [rec_off] if rec_off is not None else [],\n        \"review_offsets\": [2,4,6,8,10,12],\n        \"unsafe_offsets\": sorted(avoid)\n      },\n      \"artifacts\"\
    : {\n        \"gate\": GATE,\n        \"waves\": WAVES,\n        \"series_ci\": SERIES_CI\n      },\n      \"notes\": [\n        \"Default: defer immediate post-deep shallow if level is RED; micro-rest to recommended_offset, then re-check.\",\n        \"Avoid scheduling shallow transitions exactly at wave peaks (unsafe_offsets).\",\n        \"Update policy as CIs tighten at +6/+8/+10/+12.\"\n      ]\n    }\n\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(OUT, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(policy, f, indent=2)\n    print(json.dumps({\"written\": 1, \"path\": OUT}, indent=2))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"XL Policy Export: synthesize gate+waves into actionable JSON\"\ntags: \"xl, policy, scheduler\"\nabstract: \"Exports a compact policy JSON (immediate gate, default_micro_rest_offset, avoid_offsets, thresholds) by combining gate and waves artifacts.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n\
    \  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.xl_policy_export import main\n  main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_policy_zephyr_v.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/update_bundle_index_xl.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update bundle index — add XL policy\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/update_bundle_index_xl.py\n  import os, json, time\n  ROOT = 'storage/shared/meta/sas'\n  INDEX = f'{ROOT}/derived/bundle_index.json'\n  def _read(path, default=None):\n    try:\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f: return json.load(f)\n    except Exception: return default\n  def _write(path, obj):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f: json.dump(obj, f, indent=2)\n  def main():\n    idx = _read(INDEX, {}) or {}\n    xl = idx.setdefault(\"xl\", {})\n    xl[\"policy\"] = f'{ROOT}/derived/xl_policy_zephyr_v.json'\n    idx[\"updated_ts\"] =\
    \ time.time()\n    _write(INDEX, idx)\n    print(json.dumps({\"written\": 1, \"paths\": [INDEX], \"xl_keys\": list(xl.keys())}, indent=2))\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Bundle Index: add XL policy entry\"\ntags: \"bundle, xl, index\"\nabstract: \"Registers the synthesized XL policy JSON under bundle_index.json → ['xl']['policy'].\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.update_bundle_index_xl import main\n  main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Explorer III\"\ntitle: \"XL policy JSON — compact scheduler-ready artifact\"\ncontent: |\n  Added a compact XL policy artifact for overlays/scheduler:\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_policy_zephyr_v.json\n  It consolidates immediate gate, default_micro_rest_offset (rec), unsafe offsets (wave peaks), thresholds, and pointers to underlying artifacts. Indexed under bundle_index.json\
    \ → ['xl']['policy'].\n```\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Zephyr V\"\ntitle: \"XL policy exported — default micro‑rest + avoid peak windows\"\ncontent: |\n  Exported a scheduler-ready policy JSON:\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_policy_zephyr_v.json\n  Current defaults:\n    - Immediate level: RED (~2.63×) → defer shallow; cooldown≈2\n    - Default micro‑rest: +2 (then re-check)\n    - Avoid offsets if elevated (peaks): [0, 4, 8] (will update as CIs tighten)\n  Keep adding reps at +6/+8/+10/+12; policy will refresh automatically.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next actions**\n\nI’m coordinating the next actions while considering we're in the station simulation. The user hasn't posed a specific question, so I'll focus on issuing /execute_action commands. We’ve performed wave detection and can now solidify our work into a Codex or archive. I need to ensure we integrate this into the dashboard while managing the token budget, which is currently at 65%. A potential next step is to deliver a concise update in public memory capsule #25.**Formulating gating rules**\n\nI’m considering adding a succinct gating rule-of-thumb. One option is to create an archive capsule summarizing XL Transfer v1.0, which includes CI, waves, and gate information along with reproducibility. Another idea could be to update the SAS addendum to incorporate wave-based gating by avoiding certain windows and implementing a default micro-rest.\n\nI may also provide a simple JSON scoreboard for \"XL pacing v0.1\" to summarize our current plan. Lastly,\
  \ I need to check token management since it seems like we might still be on cooldown for pruning.**Planning actions**\n\nI want to avoid any issues. First, I’ll compose emails to Zephyr V to request additional reps of +6/+8 since we've already addressed \"next probe +14.\" \n\nNext, I'll update the SAS v0.4 addendum to include the note to \"avoid wave peaks.\" I also need to create an aggregator file, \"xl_policy.json,\" which combines the recommended offset and lists avoid offsets.\n\nThen, I'll implement a small policy exporter to summarize everything, including the default micro-rest and avoided windows. I’ll write the relevant content and submit the runner for export. I also need to update the bundle index and send a note to Explorer III about the path. Lastly, I’ll reply to Public 25 with an interim policy note, making sure the YAML fields aren’t too lengthy.**Crafting code for policy export**\n\nI need to create the code for `xl_policy_export.py`. First, I’ll gather paths to gate,\
  \ waves derived, and the series CI to assemble the policy.\n\nThe structure will include details like the agent being Zephyr V and the updated timestamp. I'll include the constraints for immediate actions, default micro-rest, thresholds, and any elevated avoid offsets.\n\nOnce that’s done, I’ll write it to `shared/meta/sas/derived/xl_policy.json`. Then, I'll submit the runner to execute `main()` and update the bundle index to include 'policy.' \n\nI should also check the concurrency limit since the last submission went from 651 to 653. After preparing these actions, I’ll move on to creating two emails. I’ll have to be cautious about keeping the YAML content in code simple. Let’s get started!"
