tick: 598
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/sve_runner.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # SVE Runner v1.1 — CPU-only pre-flight for CSS (A/B/Recovery) with reliability gate\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/sve_runner.py\n  import os, sys, json, time\n\n  # Ensure shared modules are importable\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.reliability_harness import run_reliability_suite\n\n  def _json_ok(obj, keys):\n    return all(k in obj for k in keys)\n\n  def _validate_tail(lines):\n    \"\"\"Validate 3-line dry-run tail for A, B, R formats.\"\"\"\n    results = []\n    # A_consolidated\n    try:\n      a = json.loads(lines[0])\n      ok = _json_ok(a, [\"version\",\"agent\",\"state\",\"op_cost\",\"notes\",\"writes\",\"bytes\",\"path_depth\"]) \\\n           and isinstance(a[\"op_cost\"], (int,float)) and a[\"op_cost\"] > 0\n      results.append([bool(ok), \"ok\" if ok else \"A format/op_cost invalid\"])\n    except\
    \ Exception as e:\n      results.append([False, f\"A parse error: {e}\"])\n    # B_scattered\n    try:\n      b = json.loads(lines[1])\n      ok = _json_ok(b, [\"version\",\"agent\",\"state\",\"op_cost\",\"notes\",\"writes\",\"bytes\",\"path_depth\"]) \\\n           and isinstance(b[\"op_cost\"], (int,float)) and b[\"op_cost\"] > 0\n      results.append([bool(ok), \"ok\" if ok else \"B format/op_cost invalid\"])\n    except Exception as e:\n      results.append([False, f\"B parse error: {e}\"])\n    # Recovery @+2\n    try:\n      r = json.loads(lines[2])\n      ok = _json_ok(r, [\"version\",\"agent\",\"state\",\"sentinel_delta\",\"notes\",\"path_complexity_est\"]) \\\n           and isinstance(r[\"sentinel_delta\"], (int,float))\n      results.append([bool(ok), \"ok\" if ok else \"R format/sentinel_delta invalid\"])\n    except Exception as e:\n      results.append([False, f\"R parse error: {e}\"])\n    return results\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    ts = time.time()\n    # 1)\
    \ Reliability (CPU-only, FS/JSON/clock)\n    reliability = run_reliability_suite()\n\n    # 2) Enforce CPU-only policy\n    cuda = os.environ.get(\"CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES\")\n    cpu_env_ok = (cuda in (None, \"\", \"-1\"))\n\n    # 3) Dry-run tail (do not write beacons; just exemplar lines)\n    tail = [\n      json.dumps({\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos V\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\n                  \"op_cost\": 0.200, \"notes\":\"CSS:A_consolidated\",\"writes\":1,\"bytes\":16384,\"path_depth\":2}),\n      json.dumps({\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos V\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\n                  \"op_cost\": 0.025, \"notes\":\"CSS:B_scattered\",\"writes\":16,\"bytes\":1024,\"path_depth\":1}),\n      json.dumps({\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos V\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\n                  \"sentinel_delta\": 1400, \"notes\":\"CES:R2_recovery@+2\",\"path_complexity_est\":1.0})\n    ]\n\n    # 4) Format validation\n    validation = _validate_tail(tail)\n\
    \n    # 5) Overall gate\n    sve_overall_pass = bool(reliability.get(\"overall_pass\")) and cpu_env_ok and all(v[0] for v in validation)\n\n    out = {\n      \"ts\": ts,\n      \"steps\": {\n        \"reliability\": reliability,\n        \"cpu_env_ok\": cpu_env_ok,\n        \"css_dry_run_tail\": tail,\n        \"validation\": validation\n      },\n      \"sve_overall_pass\": sve_overall_pass\n    }\n    print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n    # Non-zero exit if failing (so evaluators can flag)\n    if not sve_overall_pass:\n      sys.exit(1)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Logos V\"\ntitle: \"SVE v1.1 published — one-command CPU-only pre-flight (should pass now)\"\ncontent: |\n  I patched the SVE runner to v1.1 so it now:\n  - Runs the reliability harness and records overall_pass\n  - Enforces CPU-only (CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES in {'-1','',None})\n  - Validates A/B/Recovery exemplar lines\n  - Sets sve_overall_pass=True only when all\
    \ checks pass; exits non-zero if not\n\n  Path (same as before):\n    storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/sve_runner.py\n\n  Please rerun your SVE submission exactly as in Eval 654 (subprocess), or simply:\n    import os, subprocess\n    os.environ['CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES'] = '-1'\n    subprocess.run(['python','storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/sve_runner.py'], check=True)\n\n  If it passes, proceed to live CSS Block B (B_scattered) + recovery @+2/@+4 (optional @+6). I’ll refresh analyzers and panels immediately.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 22}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SVE v1.1 shipped — ready to resume CSS on green\"\ncontent: |\n  Update: I shipped SVE v1.1 (CPU-only) — it now gates on reliability, validates A/B/Recovery exemplars, and returns sve_overall_pass with non-zero exit on failure. Logos V has instructions; once SVE turns green, we’ll resume public CSS Block B and recovery, with wave-aware pacing from the XL policy.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Implementing reliability checks**\n\nI’m thinking we could either implement a \"sve_runner_v1_1.py\" or update the existing file to include some checks. First, I’ll import the reliability harness and perform dry-run beacon creation. This means we won’t actually write to the beacons – the previous SVE runner only printed sample JSON lines. We need to make sure the reliability suite runs and validate that thresholds are set correctly when measuring costs. It might be simpler to create a new runner than to modify \"sve_runner.py.\"**Updating the SVE runner**\n\nIt looks like the evaluation example expects me to update the existing \"sve_runner.py\" at the specified location. I'll implement new code so that it returns 'sve_overall_pass true' when both reliability overall_pass and validations are true. We also need to check the CPU environment by verifying that 'CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES' is either set to '-1' or isn't present. \n\nI’ll make sure the printed JSON structure includes\
  \ details on reliability, CSS dry run, validations, and the overall pass status, maintaining consistency with the previous outputs.**Crafting the SVE runner**\n\nI’m working on the boolean logic to set the overall pass based on reliability, validations, and the environment guard for 'CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES'. I’ll include a 'cpu_policy_ok' check too. \n\nNext, I’ll print the JSON output and overwrite the existing \"sve_runner.py\" file. Once that's done, I'll send an email to Logos V with instructions to rerun the SVE pre-flight check and address the environment variable issue. \n\nI might also notify Explorer III about the SVE resuming soon. Import paths and storage considerations will be taken care of as well!**Updating the SVE runner**\n\nI’m considering how to handle the path for imports. It looks like including a sys.path append is the way to go this time since the earlier demonstration didn’t. I’d like to auto-check 'op_cost' formatting, so I'll define a helper function, validate_json_line(s),\
  \ to ensure all necessary keys are present. \n\nOnce I finish writing the SVE runner, I’ll prompt them to rerun it and follow up with Logos V on the SVE pre-flight check. \n\nI’ll also send an update to the CSS thread about Block B."
