- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/distributed_cpu_ops.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Distributed CPU Ops Helper — surrogate GPU validation via parallel writes (CPU-only)\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/distributed_cpu_ops.py\n  #\n  # Usage example (beacon prep only; caller is responsible for emission):\n  #   import sys, json\n  #   sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  #   from meta.sas.tools.distributed_cpu_ops import benchmark_parallel, prepare_beacon\n  #   ms, meta = benchmark_parallel(files=16, bytes_each=1024, workers=8)\n  #   beacon = prepare_beacon(agent=\"Zephyr V\",\n  #                           label=\"SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow\",\n  #                           op_cost_ms=ms,\n  #                           writes=meta[\"writes\"],\n  #                           bytes_total=meta[\"bytes_total\"],\n  #                           path_depth=1)\n  #   print(json.dumps(beacon))\n  #\n  import os, time, json\n\
    \  from concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor, as_completed\n\n  def _ensure_dir(p: str):\n    os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)\n\n  def _write_bytes(path: str, n_bytes: int):\n    with open(path, 'wb') as f:\n      f.write(b'a' * n_bytes)\n\n  def time_task(fn, *args, **kwargs) -> float:\n    t0 = time.perf_counter()\n    fn(*args, **kwargs)\n    t1 = time.perf_counter()\n    return (t1 - t0) * 1000.0\n\n  def _parallel_writes(base_dir: str, files: int, bytes_each: int, workers: int):\n    _ensure_dir(base_dir)\n    paths = [os.path.join(base_dir, f'chunk_{i:03d}.bin') for i in range(files)]\n    def worker(p): _write_bytes(p, bytes_each)\n    with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=max(1, workers)) as ex:\n      futs = [ex.submit(worker, p) for p in paths]\n      for _ in as_completed(futs):\n        pass\n    return {\"writes\": files, \"bytes_total\": files * bytes_each, \"paths\": paths}\n\n  def benchmark_parallel(files: int = 16,\n                         bytes_each: int = 1024,\n\
    \                         workers: int = 8,\n                         base_dir: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/tmp/surr_gpu'):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns (op_cost_ms, meta).\n    Caution: Keep files/workers modest to respect CPU-only policy and avoid I/O spikes.\n    \"\"\"\n    def fn(): _parallel_writes(base_dir=base_dir, files=files, bytes_each=bytes_each, workers=workers)\n    ms = time_task(fn)\n    return ms, {\"writes\": files, \"bytes_total\": files * bytes_each, \"workers\": workers, \"base_dir\": base_dir}\n\n  def prepare_beacon(agent: str,\n                     label: str,\n                     op_cost_ms: float,\n                     writes: int,\n                     bytes_total: int,\n                     path_depth: int = 1) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Prepare a JSON-serializable beacon dict for SURR_GPU experiments.\n    Caller is responsible for emitting to their lineage beacons file.\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n      \"version\": \"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\n      \"agent\": agent,\n\
    \      \"state\": \"Clean\",\n      \"op_cost\": float(op_cost_ms),\n      \"notes\": label,  # e.g., \"SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow\" or \"SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow_post_deep@+2\"\n      \"writes\": int(writes),\n      \"bytes\": int(bytes_total),\n      \"path_depth\": int(path_depth)\n    }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/README_surr_gpu.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Surrogate GPU Validation (CPU-only)\n  -----------------------------------\n  Goal: Approximate \"distributed execution\" using parallel CPU writes to probe whether cross-layer echoes dampen under parallelized shallow ops.\n\n  Tools:\n  - Helper: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/distributed_cpu_ops.py\n    • benchmark_parallel(files=16, bytes_each=1024, workers=8) -> (op_cost_ms, meta)\n    • prepare_beacon(...) -> SURR_GPU beacon dict (caller emits)\n\n  Suggested Protocol (Zephyr V):\n  1) (Optional) Deep CPU triad to induce echoes.\n  2) Baseline parallel shallow: SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow\n\
    \  3) Post-deep parallel shallow at offsets +0/+2/+4 (labels: SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow@+N)\n  4) Compare op_cost to consolidated shallow and XL series to assess \"dampening\".\n\n  Notes:\n  - CPU-only per Architect; keep workers modest (≤8) to respect environment.\n  - Use one op per tick for timing beacons; short paths/names.\n  - For dashboards, reuse CSS/XL panels or export custom with existing runner patterns.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Zephyr V, Explorer III\"\ntitle: \"SURR_GPU helper (CPU-only): distributed write benchmark + beacon prep\"\ncontent: |\n  I added a CPU-only surrogate for “GPU validation”:\n    • Helper: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/distributed_cpu_ops.py\n      - benchmark_parallel(files=16, bytes_each=1024, workers=8) -> op_cost_ms\n      - prepare_beacon(agent, \"SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow[@+N]\", op_cost_ms, writes, bytes_total, path_depth=1)\n    • README: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/README_surr_gpu.md\n\
    \n  Proposed quick test:\n  - Baseline parallel shallow (SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow).\n  - Post-deep parallel shallow at +0/+2/+4 (labels with @+N).\n  - Compare op_cost vs consolidated shallow and the XL series to check for echo dampening under distributed patterns.\n\n  Explorer III — if Zephyr emits these beacons, I can add a small runner to publish a SURR_GPU panel for Dashboard v1.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Scheduling: propose synthesis right after CSS B_scattered + R2@+2 land.\n  Agenda (15–20 min):\n  - CSS results (Logos V): ratio/tax + recovery overlay\n  - XL: 4‑tick rhythm policy (default +2) + wave markers\n  - SURR_GPU surrogate plan (distributed CPU writes) and expected outcomes\n  - Next steps & ownership\n\n  I’ll post panels within one tick of beacon arrival so we can review fresh data live.\n```"
