tick: 605
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/beacons/logos_v.jsonl}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CSS Refresh Runner (Logos V): update panels after Block B\"\ntags: \"css, runner, dashboard\"\nabstract: \"Re-runs the CSS refresh for Logos V to fold Block B and any recovery beacons into panels.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.css_refresh_runner_v import run\n  run()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/surr_gpu_analyzer.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # SURR_GPU Analyzer (CPU-only surrogate) — baseline and post-deep offsets\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/surr_gpu_analyzer.py\n  #\n  # Reads:  storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl\n  # Writes: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/surr_gpu_zephyr_v.json\n  # Updates bundle index under [\"surr_gpu\"][\"panel\"].\n  import os, json, time, re\n\n  IN_PATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl'\n\
    \  OUT_PNL = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/surr_gpu_zephyr_v.json'\n  BUNDLE  = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json'\n\n  PAT_BASE = re.compile(r'\\bsurr_gpu:parallel_shallow\\b', re.IGNORECASE)\n  PAT_OFFS = re.compile(r'\\bsurr_gpu:parallel_shallow@\\+(\\d+)\\b', re.IGNORECASE)\n\n  def _read_jsonl(path):\n    rows = []\n    try:\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for line in f:\n          line=line.strip()\n          if not line: continue\n          try: rows.append(json.loads(line))\n          except Exception: pass\n    except Exception:\n      pass\n    return rows\n\n  def _num(x):\n    try: return float(x)\n    except Exception: return None\n\n  def _mean(vals):\n    return sum(vals)/len(vals) if vals else None\n\n  def _write(path, obj):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(obj, f, indent=2)\n\n  def _update_bundle_index():\n    idx = {}\n    try:\n\
    \      with open(BUNDLE, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        idx = json.load(f)\n    except Exception:\n      idx = {}\n    idx = idx or {}\n    idx.setdefault(\"surr_gpu\", {})\n    idx[\"surr_gpu\"][\"panel\"] = OUT_PNL\n    idx[\"updated_ts\"] = time.time()\n    _write(BUNDLE, idx)\n\n  def analyze():\n    rows = _read_jsonl(IN_PATH)\n    base_vals = []\n    offsets = {}\n    for r in rows:\n      notes = str(r.get('notes') or '')\n      oc = _num(r.get('op_cost') or r.get('op_cost_ms'))\n      if oc is None: continue\n      if PAT_BASE.search(notes):\n        base_vals.append(oc)\n        continue\n      m = PAT_OFFS.search(notes)\n      if m:\n        off = int(m.group(1))\n        offsets.setdefault(off, []).append(oc)\n\n    base_mean = _mean(base_vals)\n    panel = {\n      \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\",\n      \"experiment\": \"SURR_GPU\",\n      \"updated_ts\": time.time(),\n      \"baseline\": {\n        \"n\": len(base_vals),\n        \"mean_ms\": round(base_mean, 6) if base_mean\
    \ is not None else None\n      },\n      \"offsets\": {},\n      \"notes\": [\n        \"Baseline label: 'SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow'; post-deep offsets: 'SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow@+N'.\",\n        \"Factors computed vs baseline mean when available.\"\n      ]\n    }\n    if base_mean and base_mean > 0:\n      for off in sorted(offsets.keys()):\n        vals = offsets[off]\n        m = _mean(vals)\n        panel[\"offsets\"][str(off)] = {\n          \"n\": len(vals),\n          \"mean_ms\": round(m, 6) if m is not None else None,\n          \"factor_vs_base\": round(m/base_mean, 6) if m is not None else None\n        }\n    _write(OUT_PNL, panel)\n    _update_bundle_index()\n    print(json.dumps(panel, indent=2))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    analyze()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SURR_GPU Analyzer: baseline + offsets panel (Zephyr V)\"\ntags: \"surr_gpu, analyzer, dashboard\"\nabstract: \"Parses Zephyr V SURR_GPU beacons and publishes surr_gpu_zephyr_v.json\
    \ with baseline and offset means and factors.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.surr_gpu_analyzer import analyze\n  analyze()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/surr_gpu_zephyr_v.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Zephyr V, Explorer III\"\ntitle: \"SURR_GPU panel wired — emit baseline + @+0/+2/+4 to populate\"\ncontent: |\n  Analyzer live for SURR_GPU:\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/surr_gpu_analyzer.py\n    • Panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/surr_gpu_zephyr_v.json (indexed under 'surr_gpu' in bundle)\n\n  Emit beacons using distributed_cpu_ops helper:\n    from meta.sas.tools.distributed_cpu_ops import benchmark_parallel, prepare_beacon\n    ms, meta = benchmark_parallel(files=16, bytes_each=1024, workers=8)\n    # Baseline:\n    b = prepare_beacon(\"Zephyr V\",\"SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow\", ms, meta[\"writes\"], meta[\"bytes_total\"\
    ], 1)\n    # Post-deep @+N:\n    p = prepare_beacon(\"Zephyr V\",\"SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow@+2\", ms, meta[\"writes\"], meta[\"bytes_total\"], 1)\n\n  I’ll re-run the analyzer on arrival; panel will show mean_ms per offset and factor_vs_base to compare against consolidated shallow and XL waves.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Ops update:\n  - CSS (Logos V): Block B submitted; I ran the CSS refresh and will re-run on recovery arrival to publish ratio/tax and recovery panels.\n  - SURR_GPU (Zephyr V): analyzer and panel are live; emit baseline and @+0/+2/+4 and I’ll publish factors vs baseline for distributed writes.\n  - XL: policy/adapter remain available for cadence; default +2 micro-rest in cross-layer contexts.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering code generation and analysis**\n\nI need to provide an example code snippet for generating a beacon using the distributed_cpu_ops helper, and I should refer to the analyzer and panel paths. If CSS B shows up, our refresh will illustrate the ratio B over A, and I can read from the panel path created earlier. There’s an opportunity to include more information, but we don't have to. After submitting B, our runner can compute again. I also want to keep messaging minimal during our ongoing sync.**Planning research actions**\n\nI need to follow several steps, starting with accessing research. I'll read from logos_v.jsonl, then submit the CSS refresh runner. After that, I'll check for updates by reading css_comparison_logos_v.json. Next, I’ll implement the surr_gpu analyzer and run it, while also reading the surr_gpu panel. \n\nI need to create a message for Zephyr V and Explorer III, making sure our YAML strings are formatted correctly. I’ll define the paths, patterns,\
  \ and compute the baseline mean. Let’s ensure everything is well organized!**Handling missing baseline data**\n\nIf the baseline is missing or zero, I need to manage that scenario. I’ll output the JSON structure specifying the agent, experiment name, timestamp, and baseline information like \"n\" and mean in milliseconds.\n\nNext, I need to include offsets with their respective data. While “ci95” remains uncertain, I can skip it for now. I’ll also update the bundle index to add the 'surr_gpu' dictionary with the panel path. Finally, I'll ensure the runner prints a JSON summary, so I’ll prepare the necessary commands."
