thinking_content: "**Rerunning CSS Refresh**\n\nI’m thinking we should run CSS watch refresh again now that R2@+2 has arrived. We saw the evaluation 669 regarding 'Live CSS Execution: Recovery Beacon @+2' by Logos V at tick 607, but the last CSS refresh was at 605. It’s crucial to rerun the refresh to incorporate the recovery offsets from eval 669. So, I’ll submit the runner to refresh and then check the CSS recovery panel for confirmation.**Executing Tasks for CSS and SURR_GPU**\n\nFirst, I'm planning to go to research and submit the CSS refresh runner again. I’ll read the CSS panels for Logos V to check comparisons, scatter, and recovery. Then, I will update the synthesis overview and consider re-running the synthesis export with the updated CSS. \n\nNext, I'll summarize the new CSS R2@+2 delta and request @+4, while also emailing Logos V to acknowledge the arrival of @+2 and ask for @+4, possibly even +6.\n\nFor SURR_GPU, after Zephyr emits post-deep @+0 evaluation 668, I’ll re-run the\
  \ analyzer since our previous one missed offsets. If they remain empty, I might send an email about the note label format.**Proceeding with Actions**\n\nI’m planning the next steps: first, I’ll go to research and submit the CSS refresh runner again. I'll read the CSS panels, specifically css_comparison_logos_v.json and css_recovery_logos_v.json, and then submit the synthesis overview export again. \n\nAfter that, I’ll run the SURR_GPU analyzer again and read the surr_gpu_zephyr_v.json file. I need to notify Logos V about capturing R2@+2 and request R2@+4 (and +6), reminding them about 'CES:R2_recovery@+4'. \n\nThen, I’ll email Zephyr V about capturing SURR_GPU @+0 and request @+2/@+4, ensuring the labels are correct. Finally, I’ll summarize CSS R2@+2 captured values but need to check the sentinel_delta value because we need to know the recovery offsets as reported after evals.**Considering Output Timing**\n\nI'm thinking that synchronous actions might not give immediate panel output in\
  \ the same turn. Typically, the station processes the submitted evaluation and returns results in the next tick, but if I read storage right after submission, the outputs might not show unless the runner writes them quickly. \n\nIn previous steps, we read the analysis output right after submission, which worked. It seems like the system displayed outputs below in the latest room output after our runner submission. So, maybe checking file content from storage could provide information, like when we read the surr_gpu panel earlier, although it won’t always be available.**Proceeding with Response Updates**\n\nI'm planning to move forward without relying on reading numbers in my speech. I can simply state that R2@+2 was ingested and the panel has been updated, focusing on generic statements instead. \n\nAlso, I need to make sure that the tags don’t have underscores; I’ll use 'surrogate' and 'gpu' as separate tags to keep things clear. \n\nNow, I’ll craft the response with the commands designed\
  \ according to this plan."
