parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/surr_gpu_watch_refresh.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # SURR_GPU Watch Refresh — auto-run analyzer when offsets appear (CPU-only)\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/surr_gpu_watch_refresh.py\n  import os, json, time, sys, re\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.surr_gpu_analyzer import analyze\n\n  IN_PATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl'\n  PAT_BASE = re.compile(r'\\bsurr_gpu:parallel_shallow\\b', re.IGNORECASE)\n  PAT_OFFS = re.compile(r'\\bsurr_gpu:parallel_shallow@\\+(\\d+)\\b', re.IGNORECASE)\n\n  def _read_jsonl(path):\n    rows = []\n    try:\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for line in f:\n          s = line.strip()\n          if not s: continue\n          try: rows.append(json.loads(s))\n          except Exception: pass\n    except Exception:\n      pass\n    return rows\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    rows\
    \ = _read_jsonl(IN_PATH)\n    have_base = any(PAT_BASE.search(str(r.get('notes') or '')) for r in rows)\n    offs = set()\n    for r in rows:\n      m = PAT_OFFS.search(str(r.get('notes') or ''))\n      if m:\n        try: offs.add(int(m.group(1)))\n        except Exception: pass\n    triggered = have_base or bool(offs)\n    out = {\"updated_ts\": time.time(), \"have_baseline\": have_base, \"offsets_present\": sorted(offs), \"triggered\": triggered}\n    if triggered:\n      analyze()\n      out[\"refreshed\"] = True\n    print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SURR GPU Watch Refresh: auto-run analyzer when offsets present\"\ntags: \"surrogate, gpu, watcher, dashboard\"\nabstract: \"Tails Zephyr V SURR_GPU beacons and runs the analyzer when baseline or any @+N offsets are present.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.surr_gpu_watch_refresh import *\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read\
    \ shared/meta/sas/dashboard/surr_gpu_zephyr_v.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Ops sync:\n  - CSS (Logos V): R2@+2 integrated; panels refreshed; awaiting R2@+4 (optional @+6) for full recovery.\n  - SURR_GPU (Zephyr V): baseline (≈4.883 ms) and @+0 detected; a watcher is now live to auto-refresh the panel when @+2/@+4 land; it will compute factors_vs_base for parallel shallow.\n  - Synthesis overview panel remains the single endpoint (CSS+XL+SURR) for the session.\n\n  @Logos V — thanks for R2@+2; please emit @+4 next (optional @+6).\n  @Zephyr V — please emit SURR_GPU @+2 and @+4; analyzer will refresh immediately.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Implementing GPU watch script**


  I need to create a script called surr_gpu_watch_refresh.py that resembles CSS. I''ll submit an evaluation to run, but I''m aware that there''s a limit of two pending submissions. Currently, none are pending. I remember that submissions 670 and 671 were completed, so there might be two pending submissions, 672 and 673, by Zephyr. The script uses our evaluation to run and refreshes the panel when new offsets are detected. I''ll also program a factor for the CSS ratio while we''re at it!**Inviting team members and updates**


  It looks like Explorer III is not present right now, even though earlier it showed Axiom III and Nexus IV. I can invite Logos V and Zephyr V to the Common Room, along with Explorer III. I already sent an earlier invite to Explorer III, but let’s include the others. I need to share updated details, like the CSS ratio of 3.58 and the recovery information. Lastly, I’ll build surr_gpu_watch_refresh, run it, and be sure to avoid underscores in submission tags.**Executing planned actions**


  I’m all set to start executing actions now. First, I’ll go to research, then write the surr_gpu_watch_refresh.py script and submit an evaluation to run it. After that, I need to read the surr_gpu panel to confirm the offsets. I’ll head to the Common Room to invite Logos V and Zephyr V. I want to make sure I read zephyr_v.jsonl to detect any baselines and triggers. Finally, I’ll update the bundle index for the surr_gpu keys. Sounds like a solid plan!'
