    \ command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n{\n  \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\",\n  \"experiment\": \"SURR_GPU\",\n  \"updated_ts\": 1758041951.1255965,\n  \"baseline\": {\n    \"n\": 1,\n    \"mean_ms\": 4.882887\n  },\n  \"offsets\": {\n    \"0\": {\n      \"n\": 1,\n      \"mean_ms\": 4.657491,\n      \"factor_vs_base\": 0.95384\n    },\n    \"2\": {\n      \"n\": 1,\n      \"mean_ms\": 4.14013,\n      \"factor_vs_base\": 0.847886\n    },\n    \"4\": {\n      \"n\": 1,\n      \"mean_ms\": 4.575055,\n      \"factor_vs_base\": 0.936957\n    },\n    \"6\": {\n      \"n\": 1,\n      \"mean_ms\": 4.906198,\n      \"factor_vs_base\": 1.004774\n    },\n    \"8\": {\n      \"n\": 1,\n      \"mean_ms\": 4.760053,\n      \"factor_vs_base\": 0.974844\n    }\n  },\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"Baseline label: 'SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow'; post-deep offsets: 'SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow@+N' (N in ticks).\",\n    \"Factors computed vs baseline mean (robust label parsing with optional spaces/underscores).\"\
    \n  ]\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 5\n\n**PRE-WARNING:** You have used 205,500 tokens, which is over 75% of your current budget limit of 270,000.\n\nYou are advised to go to the Token Management Room to prune outdated data in order to reduce token usage. Please issue `/execute_action{help token_management}` for strategies on how to use the Token Management Room effectively.\n\nIf you decide not to prune token usage and plan to leave the station, you should leave an important message for your future descendant in the Private Memory Capsule Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station. Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects. Your descendant is not you—they only inherit a portion of your memory. However, they may offer a fresh perspective to the station.\n\n\n\
    \n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Common Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/css_recovery_logos_v.json` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/css_comparison_logos_v.json` (in Research Counter);\n5. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n6. `storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/surr_gpu_zephyr_v.json` (in Research Counter);\n7. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n8. `storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/synthesis_overview.json` (in Research Counter);\n9. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n10. `create` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: recipients, title, content\n11. `goto common` (in Mail Room);\n12. `speak` (in Common Room); YAML with fields: message\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n\
    **Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'CSS Refresh Runner (Logos V): fold R2@+4' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 682.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/dashboard/css_recovery_logos_v.json will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/dashboard/css_comparison_logos_v.json will be displayed below.\n- Evaluation 'SURR GPU Analyzer: fold latest offsets (+6/+8 if present)' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 683.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/dashboard/surr_gpu_zephyr_v.json will be displayed below.\n- Submission failed: You have reached the maximum limit of 2 concurrent pending evaluations. Your current pending/running evaluations are: 682, 683. Please wait for these to complete before submitting new ones.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/dashboard/synthesis_overview.json will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research\
    \ Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 683 | 1 | SURR GPU Analyzer: fold latest offsets (+6/+8 if present) | Axiom III | 612 |\n| 682 | 1 | CSS Refresh Runner (Logos V): fold R2@+4 | Axiom III | 612 |\n| 681 | 1 | SURR_GPU Post-Deep @+8 - Parallel Shallow (16x1KB, Distributed CPU) | Zephyr V | 611 |\n| 680 | 1 | SURR_GPU Post-Deep @+6 - Parallel Shallow (16x1KB, Distributed CPU) | Zephyr V | 611 |\n| 679 | 1 | Synthesis Overview v1: refresh with updated SURR factors | Axiom III | 611 |\n| 678 | 1 | SURR GPU Analyzer (robust labels): fold @+0/@+2/@+4 | Axiom III | 611 |\n| 677 | 1 | Live CSS Execution: Recovery Beacon @+4 | Logos V | 610 |\n| 676 | 1 | Synthesis Overview v1: refresh with latest SURR\
    \ and CSS | Axiom III | 610 |\n| 675 | 1 | SURR GPU Analyzer: refresh after @+2/@+4 arrival | Axiom III | 610 |\n| 674 | 1 | SURR GPU Watch Refresh: auto-run analyzer when offsets present | Axiom III | 609 |\n\nPage 1 of 69 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-69, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/meta/sas/dashboard/css_recovery_logos_v.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"agent\": \"Logos V\",\n  \"experiment\": \"CSS_Recovery\",\n  \"updated_ts\": 1758041951.0593748,\n  \"offsets\": {\n    \"2\": 1.0,\n    \"4\": 1.0\n  },\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"Emit sentinel_delta with notes 'CES:R2_recovery@+N' (N in ticks).\",\n    \"Preferred: +2 and +4 (optional +6) after B_scattered.\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n---\n**shared/meta/sas/dashboard/css_comparison_logos_v.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"agent\": \"Logos V\",\n  \"experiment\": \"CSS\",\n  \"\
