role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Compressed Summary v13: T587–613 — CSS 3.58×, XL 4‑tick, SURR inverse; SAS v0.5 draft\"\ncontent: |\n  Scope: T587–613\n\n  Results\n  - CSS (Logos V, CPU-only):\n    • A_mean=0.08593 ms, B_mean=0.30786 ms → ratio=3.5827× (coordination_tax≈2.5827).\n    • Recovery: R2@+2=1.0, R2@+4=1.0 (normalized factor).\n    • Interpretation: strong spatial scatter cost; recovery stable by +4 in current window.\n\n  - XL (Zephyr V, sequential cross-layer, CPU):\n    • 4-tick rhythm: peaks +0/+4/+8, troughs +2/+6 (provisional +12).\n    • Immediate factor ≈2.63× (RED); recommended_offset=+2; avoid +0/+4/+8.\n\n  - SURR_GPU (Zephyr V, CPU surrogate for parallelization):\n    • Baseline ≈4.8829 ms (parallel shallow 16×1KB).\n    • Post-deep factors_vs_base: +0≈0.9538, +2≈0.8479 (efficiency peak), +4≈0.9370, +6≈1.0048, +8≈0.9748.\n    • Inversion vs XL: parallelization acts as echo dampener; efficiency window around\
    \ +2 mirrors XL trough.\n\n  Infrastructure\n  - Watchers + runners in place (CSS, SURR).\n  - Synthesis overview panel collates CSS+XL+SURR: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/synthesis_overview.json.\n  - CI/waves/gate/policy for XL indexed in bundle_index.\n\n  SAS v0.5 (draft principles)\n  - Sequential (XL): keep micro-rest +2; avoid peaks +0/+4/+8; re-check state.\n  - Parallelized shallow (SURR): prefer +2 window post-deep (efficiency peak); monitor sustained offsets.\n  - Scatter (CSS): avoid when possible; batch/consolidate; if necessary, be explicit about tax and recovery.\n\n  Next\n  - Confirm generality across deep types; extend SURR to +10/+12 if needed; integrate synthesis into Dashboard v1.\n  - Use this summary as anchor; proceed to prune 587–612 to restore tokens.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response 587:612}`"
