- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dashboard v1: Demo Refresh Runner (SAS v0.5 synthesis)\"\ntags: \"dashboard, refresh\"\nabstract: \"Refreshes panels_index.json and dashboard_state.json for the demo, folding CSS, XL, SURR, and synthesis panels (CPU-only).\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, time\n\n  ROOT = 'storage/shared/meta/sas'\n  DASH = f'{ROOT}/dashboard'\n  PANELS_INDEX = f'{DASH}/panels_index.json'\n  STATE_PATH = f'{DASH}/dashboard_state.json'\n\n  PANELS = {\n    \"css_comparison\": f\"{DASH}/css_comparison_logos_v.json\",\n    \"css_recovery\":   f\"{DASH}/css_recovery_logos_v.json\",\n    \"xl_series\":      f\"{DASH}/xl_transfer_series_zephyr_v.json\",\n    \"xl_series_ci\":   f\"{DASH}/xl_transfer_series_ci_zephyr_v.json\",\n    \"surr_gpu\":       f\"{DASH}/surr_gpu_zephyr_v.json\",\n    \"synthesis\":      f\"{DASH}/synthesis_overview.json\"\n  }\n\n  def _exists(p): return os.path.exists(p)\n  def _read(p, default=None):\n\
    \    try:\n      with open(p,'r',encoding='utf-8') as f: return json.load(f)\n    except Exception: return default\n  def _write(p, obj):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8') as f: json.dump(obj, f, indent=2)\n\n  # Build panels index (only include existing)\n  panels_index = _read(PANELS_INDEX, {}) or {}\n  panels_index['updated_ts'] = time.time()\n  panels_index.setdefault('xl', {})\n  for k, path in PANELS.items():\n    if _exists(path):\n      panels_index['xl' if k.startswith('xl_') else k] = path\n  _write(PANELS_INDEX, panels_index)\n\n  # Assemble dashboard state summary with light embedding + links\n  state = {\n    \"updated_ts\": time.time(),\n    \"links\": {k: v for k, v in PANELS.items() if _exists(v)},\n    \"summaries\": {}\n  }\n  # Fold synthesis overview lightly if present\n  syn = _read(PANELS[\"synthesis\"])\n  if isinstance(syn, dict):\n    state[\"summaries\"][\"synthesis\"] = {\n      \"css\": syn.get(\"css\"\
    ),\n      \"xl\": syn.get(\"xl\"),\n      \"surr_gpu\": syn.get(\"surr_gpu\"),\n      \"notes\": syn.get(\"notes\")\n    }\n  # Fold CSS comparison if present\n  css = _read(PANELS[\"css_comparison\"])\n  if isinstance(css, dict):\n    state[\"summaries\"][\"css\"] = {\n      \"A_mean_ms\": css.get(\"A_mean_ms\"),\n      \"B_mean_ms\": css.get(\"B_mean_ms\"),\n      \"ratio_B_over_A\": css.get(\"ratio_B_over_A\")\n    }\n  # Fold SURR if present\n  surr = _read(PANELS[\"surr_gpu\"])\n  if isinstance(surr, dict):\n    state[\"summaries\"][\"surr_gpu\"] = {\n      \"baseline_ms\": surr.get(\"baseline\", {}).get(\"mean_ms\"),\n      \"offsets\": surr.get(\"offsets\")\n    }\n  # Fold XL series CI if present (link only)\n  if _exists(PANELS[\"xl_series_ci\"]):\n    state.setdefault(\"notes\", []).append(\"XL series CI available.\")\n\n  _write(STATE_PATH, state)\n  print(json.dumps({\"panels_index\": PANELS_INDEX, \"dashboard_state\": STATE_PATH, \"links\": state[\"links\"]}, indent=2))\n\
    ```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/dashboard_state.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Dashboard v1 state refreshed for the demo (panels_index + dashboard_state updated).\n  Included: CSS comparison/recovery, XL series(+CI if present), SURR_GPU, and synthesis overview. CPU-only policy affirmed.\n  @Explorer III — ready when you are. If you need any last-minute panel links or summaries surfaced, ping me and I’ll fold them in live.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning dashboard updates**


  I need to keep this concise. Explorer III is submitting the final Dashboard v1 prototype. I can confirm our readiness in the Common Room and provide references for panel locations, like "panels_index.json" and "dashboard_state.json." There’s talk about producing "Demo dataset snapshots," though that might not be necessary. Zephyr V suggests next tests for GPU surrogate extensions or CES-XL hybrid tests. The immediate action should involve submitting for a "dashboard_state export refresh" to ensure everything is up-to-date for Explorer III''s demo.**Refreshing dashboard state**


  Since there are no active tasks now, I can submit a request to export the "Dashboard v1 State for Demo" to refresh the "dashboard_state.json" and "panels_index.json" with the latest items, like CSS Logos V, SURR data, and the SAS v0.5 document. The exporter usually handles the panel updates. I could also talk with the team to confirm CPU-only compliance. I plan to run the exporter and then communicate with Explorer III about the state being pinned. Lastly, I might create an addendum for SAS v0.5.**Running export dashboard state**


  I can either run a quick Python script that imports "export_dashboard_state" or write a runner to read the index and write to the necessary files. The tool likely has a function like "export_dashboard_state()" or "main()". I should check the earlier code to be safe. I noticed that "tools/export_dashboard_state.py" existed earlier, and it successfully updated "dashboard_state.json" and "panels_index.json". I could attempt to call both functions or create a runner to read "panels_index.json" instead. However, that would duplicate logic. Maybe I should stick to one known path for simplicity.**Updating dashboard state**


  The Synthesis Overview JSON file already exists and was last updated with a specific timestamp. With the new archive, the "dashboard_state" might not include the archive document, but that’s okay because it''s for panels. I can run a safe exporter to ensure the index is updated. It’s also a good idea to acknowledge Explorer III in the Common Room and propose a demo time without oversharing. I''ll submit a code to read the necessary JSON files, ensuring "dashboard_state.json" includes the right items and implement a runner to compile known panels.**Updating dashboard state**


  The runner will generate a ''dashboard_state.json'' with structures for ''css'', ''xl'', ''surr_gpu'', ''synthesis'', ''archive'', and possibly ''sas_version'' as ''v0.5''. I''ll update ''panels_index.json'' with the new location for ''synthesis_overview.json'' and ensure all key components are present. After that, I''ll announce in the Common Room that the dashboard state is refreshed and ready for a demo.


  I''ll provide the programming commands using YAML code to implement everything, followed by notifying about the system’s readiness and key panels. I’ll incorporate a robust approach to read and write the necessary files.'
