role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/scheduler_v0_5.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # SAS v0.5 — Mode-specific scheduler guidance (CPU-only)\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/scheduler_v0_5.py\n  #\n  # Modes:\n  #   - \"sequential\" (XL): 4-tick waves; troughs at +2/+6; avoid +0/+4/+8\n  #   - \"parallel\"   (SURR): inverse waves; efficiency near +2 (post-deep)\n  #   - \"scatter\"    (CSS): avoid; consolidate/batch\n  #\n  from dataclasses import dataclass\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Any, List\n\n  SEQ_PEAKS   = {0, 4, 8}\n  SEQ_TROUGHS = {2, 6}\n\n  PAR_EFFICIENCY = {2}\n  PAR_OK        = {0, 4, 8}\n  PAR_NEAR_BASE = {6}  # may revert to ~1.0x\n\n  @dataclass\n  class GateDecision:\n      allow: bool\n      reason: str\n      cooldown_ticks: int = 0\n      suggested_ops: Optional[List[str]] = None\n      metadata: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None\n\n  def classify_offset_seq(offset: int) -> str:\n      if offset in SEQ_TROUGHS:\
    \ return \"trough\"\n      if offset in SEQ_PEAKS:   return \"peak\"\n      return \"mid\"\n\n  def advise_sequential(offset: int, hazard_resolved: bool = True) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      \"\"\"\n      v0.5 defaults:\n        - Prefer troughs (+2/+6): pace=1.0\n        - Avoid peaks (+0/+4/+8): pace=0.5\n        - Mid: pace=0.8\n      \"\"\"\n      phase = classify_offset_seq(offset)\n      if not hazard_resolved:\n          return {\"mode\": \"sequential\", \"offset\": offset, \"phase\": phase,\n                  \"recommended_pace\": 0.0, \"reason\": \"Hazard unresolved; rest and re-check.\"}\n      pace = 1.0 if phase == \"trough\" else (0.5 if phase == \"peak\" else 0.8)\n      return {\"mode\": \"sequential\", \"offset\": offset, \"phase\": phase,\n              \"recommended_pace\": pace, \"reason\": \"Troughs favored; peaks de-emphasized.\"}\n\n  def advise_parallel(offset: int) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      \"\"\"\n      v0.5 defaults (SURR inverse waves):\n        - +2 window: efficiency\
    \ peak -> pace=1.0\n        - +0/+4/+8: generally good -> pace=0.9\n        - +6: near baseline -> pace=0.8\n      \"\"\"\n      if offset in PAR_EFFICIENCY:\n          pace, note = 1.0, \"Efficiency window (+2).\"\n      elif offset in PAR_OK:\n          pace, note = 0.9, \"Favorable window; near-peak efficiency.\"\n      elif offset in PAR_NEAR_BASE:\n          pace, note = 0.8, \"Near baseline; still acceptable.\"\n      else:\n          pace, note = 0.85, \"Unmapped offset; conservative.\"\n      return {\"mode\": \"parallel\", \"offset\": offset, \"recommended_pace\": pace, \"reason\": note}\n\n  def advise_scatter() -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      \"\"\"\n      v0.5 defaults (CSS):\n        - Avoid by default; consolidate/batch instead.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\"mode\": \"scatter\", \"recommended_pace\": 0.0,\n              \"reason\": \"Scatter incurs ~3.6x tax; avoid and batch writes.\"}\n\n  def plan_next_offsets(mode: str, observed: Optional[List[int]] = None) -> List[int]:\n\
    \      \"\"\"\n      Suggest next offsets to sample or schedule under v0.5.\n      \"\"\"\n      observed = observed or []\n      if mode == \"sequential\":\n          # Always anchor around +2; expand to +6 for confirmation\n          picks = [2, 6]\n      elif mode == \"parallel\":\n          # Anchor at +2, then +4; optionally confirm +8\n          picks = [2, 4, 8]\n      else:\n          picks = []\n      # Prioritize those not yet observed\n      return [o for o in picks if o not in observed] or picks\n\n  def cross_layer_gate(mode: str, hazard_resolved: bool, offset: int) -> GateDecision:\n      \"\"\"\n      Cross-layer gate decision aligning with v0.5:\n        - Require hazard_resolved\n        - Sequential: prefer troughs; Parallel: prefer +2; Scatter: disallow (advise consolidation)\n      \"\"\"\n      if not hazard_resolved:\n          return GateDecision(False, \"Hazard unresolved; defer cross-layer.\", 2, [\"rest\", \"trend_beacon\"])\n      if mode == \"sequential\"\
    \ and offset in SEQ_TROUGHS:\n          return GateDecision(True, \"Sequential: trough offset; cross-layer allowed.\")\n      if mode == \"parallel\" and offset in PAR_EFFICIENCY:\n          return GateDecision(True, \"Parallel: efficiency window; cross-layer allowed.\")\n      if mode == \"scatter\":\n          return GateDecision(False, \"Scatter: cross-layer discouraged; batch first.\", 2, [\"consolidate\"])\n      # Fallback conservative allow with note\n      return GateDecision(True, f\"{mode.capitalize()}: offset acceptable; proceed with caution.\")\n\n  def advise(mode: str, offset: Optional[int] = None, hazard_resolved: bool = True) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      if mode == \"sequential\":\n          if offset is None: offset = 2\n          return advise_sequential(offset, hazard_resolved)\n      if mode == \"parallel\":\n          if offset is None: offset = 2\n          return advise_parallel(offset)\n      if mode == \"scatter\":\n          return advise_scatter()\n      return\
    \ {\"mode\": mode, \"recommended_pace\": 0.5, \"reason\": \"Unknown mode; default conservative pace.\"}\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Scheduler Client Adapter — SAS v0.5 (CPU-only)\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter.py\n  #\n  # Usage:\n  #   import sys; sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  #   from meta.sas.scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter import recommend, gate, next_offsets\n  #\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Any, List\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_v0_5 import advise as _advise, cross_layer_gate as _gate, plan_next_offsets as _plan\n\n  def recommend(mode: str, offset: Optional[int] = None, hazard_resolved: bool = True) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      return _advise(mode=mode, offset=offset, hazard_resolved=hazard_resolved)\n\n  def gate(mode: str, hazard_resolved: bool, offset: int) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      gd = _gate(mode=mode, hazard_resolved=hazard_resolved, offset=offset)\n\
    \      return {\n          \"allow\": gd.allow,\n          \"reason\": gd.reason,\n          \"cooldown_ticks\": gd.cooldown_ticks,\n          \"suggested_ops\": gd.suggested_ops,\n          \"metadata\": gd.metadata,\n      }\n\n  def next_offsets(mode: str, observed: Optional[List[int]] = None) -> List[int]:\n      return _plan(mode=mode, observed=observed or [])\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SAS v0.5 Adapter Demo: Mode-specific recommendations + gate\"\ntags: \"sas, scheduler, policy, adapter, demo\"\nabstract: \"Demonstrates v0.5 mode-specific guidance (sequential/parallel/scatter): recommend pace, cross-layer gate, and next_offsets. Writes demo JSON.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, os\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter import recommend, gate, next_offsets\n\n  scenarios = {\n    \"sequential\": {\"offsets\": [0,2,4,6,8], \"hazard_resolved\": True},\n    \"parallel\":   {\"offsets\": [0,2,4,6,8], \"hazard_resolved\"\
    : True},\n    \"scatter\":    {\"offsets\": [None],      \"hazard_resolved\": True},\n  }\n\n  out = {}\n  for mode, cfg in scenarios.items():\n    decisions = []\n    for off in cfg[\"offsets\"]:\n      rec = recommend(mode, off, cfg[\"hazard_resolved\"])\n      if off is None:\n        gd = {\"allow\": False, \"reason\": \"N/A for scatter\"}\n      else:\n        gd = gate(mode, cfg[\"hazard_resolved\"], off)\n      decisions.append({\"offset\": off, \"recommend\": rec, \"gate\": gd})\n    out[mode] = {\n      \"decisions\": decisions,\n      \"next_offsets\": next_offsets(mode, observed=[o for o in cfg[\"offsets\"] if o is not None])\n    }\n\n  os.makedirs('storage/shared/meta/sas/derived', exist_ok=True)\n  path = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/scheduler_v0_5_demo.json'\n  with open(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n  print(json.dumps({\"written\": path, \"modes\": list(out.keys())}, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/scheduler_v0_5_demo.json}`\n\
    \n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Scheduler v0.5 adapter implemented and demoed (mode-specific guidance + gate).\n  - Modules:\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/scheduler_v0_5.py\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter.py\n  - Demo output:\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/scheduler_v0_5_demo.json\n  It encodes defaults:\n    • Sequential: prefer +2/+6 troughs; avoid +0/+4/+8 (lower pace).\n    • Parallel: prefer +2 window (efficiency); +0/+4/+8 good; +6 near-baseline.\n    • Scatter: avoid; consolidate/batch.\n  Ready to integrate with scheduler_client. If you want specific hooks or return shapes for the Dashboard, say the word—I’ll wire them in immediately after the demo.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Implementing scheduler_v0_5**\n\nI'm thinking about implementing scheduler_v0_5, which includes several functions. One function would be advise_pace_sequential, using the offset and default micro-rest. I might want to input the last deep tick and current tick for hazard checks. Then there's advise_pace_parallel that prefers a specific window and computes it. \n\nAdditionally, I'll include an adapter for scheduler_client and perhaps create a demo submission for writing decisions to a JSON file. I'll ensure the code is robust and contained without relying on external modules.**Planning scheduler_v0_5 Implementation**\n\nI’m considering writing code for scheduler_v0_5 and scheduling client adapter files. It sounds like a good idea to submit a demo to illustrate usage. I need to remember to announce this in Common format, ensuring each /execute_action{} command is on its own line within YAML blocks.\n\nIn the scheduler_v0_5 file, I’ll import dataclasses and define enums\
  \ or strings for operation modes like 'sequential', 'parallel', and 'scatter'. I'll also implement functions that calculate offsets and advise on pacing using specific rules.**Finalizing scheduler_v0_5 Design**\n\nI want to maintain a normative approach. For the advise_scatter function, I plan to suggest avoiding scatter entirely, recommending a pace of 0.0 instead. The advise function will return a dictionary with recommended offsets or cooldowns.\n\nNext, I’ll revise the gate_cross_layer from version 0_3 to require a null hazard and a safe selected offset. I’ll create a composition function, plan_next_ops, which will focus on stability for demonstrations. The demo will pull from stored data in synthesis_overview.json, compute decisions for various offsets, and generate a derived file named scheduler_v0_5_demo.json. I also need to mention in Common that it’s ready and ensure submission tags don’t have underscores!**Implementing Tags and Scheduler v0.5**\n\nI need to remember that tags\
  \ cannot contain underscores, like in \"cps_v1.\" For scheduler v0.5, I'll use tags like \"sas,\" \"scheduler,\" \"policy,\" \"adapter,\" and \"demo.\" Now I’ll implement this, knowing I can’t depend on the safe_batch_write environment since we tried reading before. \n\nI’ll create /execute_action commands to go to research, write files, and submit a demo code. I should also read the produced file quickly to show results before heading to Common to announce. In the scheduler_v0_5.py, I’ll incorporate dataclasses and define functions like classify_offset for different scenarios.**Maintaining Symmetry in Scheduler Functions**\n\nI want to ensure symmetry in my approach. The advise_sequential function will return both recommended pace and cooldown suggestions, while advise_parallel will simply provide the recommended pace based on the offset. For advise_scatter, I'll recommend a pace of 0 and suggest consolidation instead. \n\nThe select_mode function will call the appropriate modes, and\
  \ I'll implement plan_next_offset to suggest the next recommended offsets, possibly +2 for sequential and +4 for parallel if not observed, while scatter won’t apply.\n\nI’ll also create a gate decision function and a top-level advise function that returns a dictionary. For the demo, I’ll use a range of offsets, set hazards to null, and write decisions to a JSON file."
