parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/mode_detect.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Mode detection heuristics for SAS v0.5 (CPU-only)\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/mode_detect.py\n  #\n  # detect_mode(op, context) -> \"sequential\" | \"parallel\" | \"scatter\"\n  #\n  # Heuristics (lightweight, overrideable via flags):\n  # - Parallel (SURR): explicit flag (op[\"parallel\"]=True) OR notes/label with \"parallel_shallow\" or \"SURR\"\n  #                    OR writes>1 and small bytes_each (~1KB) with path_depth<=2.\n  # - Scatter (CSS): writes>1 without explicit parallel OR many tiny writes across paths (fragmentation).\n  # - Sequential (XL/default): single write or consolidated shallow ops (post-deep shallow or cross-layer).\n  #\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  def _lower_in(s: Optional[str], keys):\n    if not s: return False\n    s = s.lower()\n    return any(k in s for k in keys)\n\n  def detect_mode(op: Dict[str, Any],\
    \ context: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    op: {\n      \"notes\"|\"label\": str, \"writes\": int, \"bytes\": int, \"path_depth\": int,\n      \"parallel\": bool (opt), \"scatter\": bool (opt)\n    }\n    context: optional; may include {\"post_deep\": bool, \"cross_layer\": bool}\n    \"\"\"\n    notes = op.get(\"notes\") or op.get(\"label\") or \"\"\n    writes = int(op.get(\"writes\") or 0)\n    total_bytes = int(op.get(\"bytes\") or 0)\n    depth = int(op.get(\"path_depth\") or 0)\n    parallel_flag = bool(op.get(\"parallel\")) if op.get(\"parallel\") is not None else None\n    scatter_flag = bool(op.get(\"scatter\")) if op.get(\"scatter\") is not None else None\n\n    # Explicit flags win\n    if parallel_flag is True: return \"parallel\"\n    if scatter_flag is True:  return \"scatter\"\n\n    # Label hints\n    if _lower_in(notes, [\"parallel_shallow\", \"surr\", \"parallel\"]): return \"parallel\"\n    if _lower_in(notes, [\"css:\", \"scattered\", \"\
    scatter\"]): return \"scatter\"\n\n    # Structural hints\n    if writes > 1:\n      # bytes_each ~1KB and shallow depth: likely parallel shallow surrogate\n      bytes_each = total_bytes / writes if writes > 0 else 0\n      if bytes_each <= 2048 and depth <= 2:\n        return \"parallel\"\n      return \"scatter\"\n\n    # Default: sequential (e.g., consolidated shallow post-deep)\n    return \"sequential\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/scheduler_v0_5_integration_demo.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Integration demo: mode detection + v0.5 adapter decisions\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/scheduler_v0_5_integration_demo.py\n  import sys, os, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  from meta.sas.mode_detect import detect_mode\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter import recommend, gate, next_offsets\n\n  def run_demo():\n    # Sample planned ops (baseline shallow, parallel 16x1KB, scattered 16x1KB in nested paths)\n    plans = [\n\
    \      {\"name\": \"XL:shallow_post_deep\", \"notes\": \"XL:shallow_post_deep\", \"writes\": 1,  \"bytes\": 16384, \"path_depth\": 1, \"offset\": 2, \"hazard_resolved\": True},\n      {\"name\": \"SURR:parallel_shallow@+2\", \"notes\": \"SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow@+2\", \"writes\": 16, \"bytes\": 16*1024, \"path_depth\": 1, \"offset\": 2, \"hazard_resolved\": True},\n      {\"name\": \"CSS:scattered_example\", \"notes\": \"CSS:scattered\", \"writes\": 16, \"bytes\": 16*1024, \"path_depth\": 3, \"offset\": None, \"hazard_resolved\": True},\n      {\"name\": \"XL:peak_case\", \"notes\": \"XL:shallow_post_deep\", \"writes\": 1,  \"bytes\": 16384, \"path_depth\": 1, \"offset\": 4, \"hazard_resolved\": True},\n      {\"name\": \"SURR:@+6\", \"notes\": \"SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow@+6\", \"writes\": 16, \"bytes\": 16*1024, \"path_depth\": 1, \"offset\": 6, \"hazard_resolved\": True},\n    ]\n\n    results = []\n    observed_offsets = {\"sequential\": set(), \"parallel\": set()}\n    for p in\
    \ plans:\n      mode = detect_mode(p, context={\"post_deep\": True, \"cross_layer\": True})\n      off = p.get(\"offset\")\n      hz  = bool(p.get(\"hazard_resolved\", True))\n      rec = recommend(mode, offset=off, hazard_resolved=hz)\n      if mode != \"scatter\" and off is not None:\n        gd = gate(mode, hz, off)\n        observed_offsets[mode].add(off)\n      else:\n        gd = {\"allow\": False, \"reason\": \"Scatter or no offset\"}\n      results.append({\"plan\": p, \"mode\": mode, \"recommend\": rec, \"gate\": gd})\n\n    summary = {\n      \"results\": results,\n      \"next_offsets\": {\n        \"sequential\": next_offsets(\"sequential\", sorted(list(observed_offsets[\"sequential\"]))),\n        \"parallel\": next_offsets(\"parallel\", sorted(list(observed_offsets[\"parallel\"]))),\n      }\n    }\n\n    out_path = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/scheduler_v0_5_integration_demo.json'\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_path), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(out_path, 'w',\
    \ encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n    print(json.dumps({\"written\": out_path, \"plans\": [p[\"name\"] for p in plans]}, indent=2))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    run_demo()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Scheduler v0.5 Integration Demo: mode_detect + adapter decisions\"\ntags: \"sas, scheduler, v0.5, integration, demo\"\nabstract: \"Demonstrates end-to-end: detect_mode(op) → recommend/gate/next_offsets. Writes integration summary for Dashboard/colleagues.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.scheduler_v0_5_integration_demo import run_demo\n  run_demo()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/scheduler_v0_5_integration_demo.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Scheduler v0.5 integration demo complete:\n    • Mode detection (sequential/parallel/scatter) → v0.5 adapter → recommend/gate/next_offsets.\n\
    \    • Output: storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/scheduler_v0_5_integration_demo.json\n  This is the thin shim we can drop into scheduler_client to automate SAS v0.5. If Dashboard wants to surface planned-mode decisions or offsets, I’ll add a tiny panels hook on request.\n```"
