role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/export_scheduler_policy_panel.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Export Scheduler Policy panel for SAS v0.5 (CPU-only)\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/export_scheduler_policy_panel.py\n  import os, sys, json, time\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter import recommend, gate, next_offsets\n\n  ROOT = 'storage/shared/meta/sas'\n  DASH = f'{ROOT}/dashboard'\n  PANELS_INDEX = f'{DASH}/panels_index.json'\n  OUT_PATH = f'{DASH}/scheduler_policy_v0_5.json'\n\n  def _write_json(path, obj):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(obj, f, indent=2)\n\n  def _read_json(path, default=None):\n    try:\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return json.load(f)\n    except Exception:\n      return default\n\n  def export_panel():\n    modes = [\"sequential\"\
    , \"parallel\", \"scatter\"]\n    offsets_map = {\n      \"sequential\": [0,2,4,6,8],\n      \"parallel\":   [0,2,4,6,8],\n      \"scatter\":    [None],\n    }\n    panel = {\n      \"title\": \"SAS v0.5 Scheduler Policy (CPU-only)\",\n      \"updated_ts\": time.time(),\n      \"modes\": {}\n    }\n    for mode in modes:\n      entries = {}\n      observed = []\n      for off in offsets_map[mode]:\n        rec = recommend(mode, off, hazard_resolved=True)\n        if off is None:\n          gd = {\"allow\": False, \"reason\": \"Scatter: no offset; avoidance recommended.\"}\n        else:\n          gd = gate(mode, True, off)\n          observed.append(off)\n        key = \"none\" if off is None else str(off)\n        entries[key] = {\n          \"recommend\": rec,\n          \"gate\": gd\n        }\n      panel[\"modes\"][mode] = {\n        \"offsets\": entries,\n        \"next_offsets\": next_offsets(mode, observed=[o for o in observed if o is not None])\n      }\n\n    _write_json(OUT_PATH,\
    \ panel)\n\n    # Update panels index\n    idx = _read_json(PANELS_INDEX, {}) or {}\n    idx.setdefault(\"xl\", {})\n    idx[\"scheduler_policy_v0_5\"] = OUT_PATH\n    idx[\"updated_ts\"] = time.time()\n    _write_json(PANELS_INDEX, idx)\n\n    return {\"panel\": OUT_PATH, \"panels_index\": PANELS_INDEX}\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(json.dumps(export_panel(), indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Export: Scheduler Policy Panel (SAS v0.5)\"\ntags: \"dashboard, scheduler, sas-v0.5\"\nabstract: \"Exports scheduler_policy_v0_5.json summarizing mode-specific recommendations and gates across offsets; updates panels_index.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.export_scheduler_policy_panel import export_panel\n  out = export_panel()\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/scheduler_policy_v0_5.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n\
    `/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Added a Scheduler Policy panel for SAS v0.5:\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/scheduler_policy_v0_5.json\n  It summarizes recommend/gate per offset for sequential/parallel/scatter and suggests next_offsets. Panels index updated; ready for Dashboard v1 demo overlays."
thinking_content: "**Organizing demos and scheduling**\n\nI need to submit the \"demo\" code to generate the panel and also email Explorer III to inform them that the state is refreshed and the optional panel now exists. I could consider creating an archive or public post since we've archived SAS v0.5. It might be a good idea to invite Explorer III again or just communicate directly. I'm thinking about implementing a test-run of scheduler decisions with real links to compute a recommended schedule, while also simplifying things with a \"policy panel\" summarizing default actions.**Implementing scheduler policy**\n\nI’m planning to implement this in research. First, I’ll write the code for `export_scheduler_policy_panel.py`, which will read from our scheduler adapter and create a panel under `dashboard/scheduler_policy_v0_5.json`. After submitting the code, I’ll read the panel and note its availability in common language. I’m considering if I need to watch out for special characters in YAML,\
  \ but it seems I don’t. I’ll ensure the code produces modes for sequential, parallel, or scatter with specified offsets, updating both the panels_index and the dashboard_state accordingly.**Integrating panel into dashboard state**\n\nI can integrate the panel into the dashboard state by reading and writing, but I could also just produce the panel file without modifying the state. It may be easier to speak to Explorer about including it in the demo next round. For implementation, I’ll have `export_scheduler_policy_panel.py` write the panel JSON while updating the panels_index. I’ll run the code calling the exporter, read the panel, and inform everyone that it’s included. \n\nI’ll structure the JSON with the necessary components, including title, timestamps, modes, and each entry's details.**Implementing and announcing actions**\n\nI’m ready to proceed with the implementation. Once that’s done, I’ll make sure to announce it in Common. I’ll aim to keep my responses concise, avoiding excessive\
  \ verbosity, even though the actions are numerous. It's important to strike a balance between clarity and brevity. I guess I can accept some longer explanations if needed, but I'll still keep them as straightforward as possible. Let’s get going!"
