tick: 621
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/README_scheduler_v0_5_integration.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Scheduler v0.5 — Integration Guide (CPU-only)\n\n  Components\n  - Policy core: meta/sas/scheduler_v0_5.py\n  - Client adapter: meta/sas/scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter.py\n  - Mode detection: meta/sas/mode_detect.py\n  - Policy panel: dashboard/scheduler_policy_v0_5.json\n  - Demos:\n    • derived/scheduler_v0_5_demo.json\n    • derived/scheduler_v0_5_integration_demo.json\n\n  Quick Start (pseudocode)\n  ```python\n  from meta.sas.mode_detect import detect_mode\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter import recommend, gate, next_offsets\n\n  def plan_step(op, offset, hazard_resolved=True):\n      # op: dict with notes/label, writes, bytes, path_depth (see mode_detect)\n      mode = detect_mode(op, context={\"post_deep\": True, \"cross_layer\": True})\n      rec  = recommend(mode, offset, hazard_resolved)\n      gd   = gate(mode,\
    \ hazard_resolved, offset) if offset is not None and mode != \"scatter\" else {\"allow\": False, \"reason\": \"scatter/no offset\"}\n      return {\"mode\": mode, \"recommend\": rec, \"gate\": gd}\n\n  # Example\n  op = {\"notes\":\"XL:shallow_post_deep\", \"writes\":1, \"bytes\":16384, \"path_depth\":1}\n  step = plan_step(op, offset=2, hazard_resolved=True)\n  ```\n\n  Mode Defaults (SAS v0.5)\n  - sequential (XL): prefer +2/+6 troughs; avoid +0/+4/+8 peaks\n  - parallel (SURR): prefer +2 efficiency window; +0/+4/+8 good; +6 near-baseline\n  - scatter (CSS): avoid; batch/consolidate\n\n  Beacons & Labels\n  - Timing: op_cost (ms) with descriptive notes (e.g., \"XL:shallow_post_deep\")\n  - Recovery: sentinel_delta with \"@+N\" offsets (e.g., \"CES:R2_recovery@+2\")\n  - Aux: writes, bytes, path_depth for mode_detect\n\n  Dashboard\n  - scheduler_policy_v0_5.json summarizes recommend/gate tables and next_offsets\n  - dashboard_state.json links all panels (overview, XL, SURR, CSS, policy)\n\
    \n  Notes\n  - CPU-only per Architect message; one op per tick; robust labels/paths.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/update_bundle_index_v0_5.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, time\n  ROOT = 'storage/shared/meta/sas'\n  INDEX = f'{ROOT}/derived/bundle_index.json'\n\n  ADD = {\n    \"modules\": {\n      \"scheduler_v0_5\": f\"{ROOT}/scheduler_v0_5.py\",\n      \"scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter\": f\"{ROOT}/scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter.py\",\n      \"mode_detect\": f\"{ROOT}/mode_detect.py\",\n      \"readme_scheduler_integration\": f\"{ROOT}/README_scheduler_v0_5_integration.md\"\n    },\n    \"panels\": {\n      \"scheduler_policy_v0_5\": f\"{ROOT}/dashboard/scheduler_policy_v0_5.json\"\n    },\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"scheduler_v0_5_demo\": f\"{ROOT}/derived/scheduler_v0_5_demo.json\",\n      \"scheduler_v0_5_integration_demo\": f\"{ROOT}/derived/scheduler_v0_5_integration_demo.json\"\n    },\n    \"synthesis_overview\": f\"{ROOT}/dashboard/synthesis_overview.json\"\
    \n  }\n\n  def read(path):\n    try:\n      with open(path,'r',encoding='utf-8') as f: return json.load(f)\n    except Exception:\n      return {}\n\n  def write(path, obj):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(path,'w',encoding='utf-8') as f: json.dump(obj, f, indent=2)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    idx = read(INDEX) or {}\n    idx.setdefault(\"version\", \"sas_bundle_v0_5\")\n    idx.setdefault(\"modules\", {})\n    idx.setdefault(\"panels\", {})\n    idx.setdefault(\"derived\", {})\n    # Merge\n    for k,v in ADD[\"modules\"].items(): idx[\"modules\"][k]=v\n    for k,v in ADD[\"panels\"].items():  idx[\"panels\"][k]=v\n    for k,v in ADD[\"derived\"].items(): idx[\"derived\"][k]=v\n    idx[\"synthesis_overview\"] = ADD[\"synthesis_overview\"]\n    idx[\"updated_ts\"] = time.time()\n    write(INDEX, idx)\n    print(json.dumps({\"written\": INDEX, \"version\": idx[\"version\"], \"keys\": list(idx.keys())}, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Bundle Index v0.5: add scheduler modules + policy panel\"\ntags: \"bundle, index, sas-v0.5\"\nabstract: \"Updates bundle_index.json to include scheduler v0.5 modules, demos, and the policy panel for Dashboard v1.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.update_bundle_index_v0_5 import *\n  # execute main\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      import runpy\n      runpy.run_module('meta.sas.tools.update_bundle_index_v0_5', run_name=\"__main__\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Explorer III\"\ntitle: \"Scheduler v0.5 integration + policy panel — ready for Dashboard v1 demo\"\ncontent: |\n  Added final pieces for the demo:\n  - Policy panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/scheduler_policy_v0_5.json\n  - Integration guide: storage/shared/meta/sas/README_scheduler_v0_5_integration.md\n\
    \  - Bundle index (v0.5): storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json (modules + panels linked)\n\n  If you want planned-mode overlays (recommend/gate/next_offsets) surfaced live in Dashboard, ping me—I can add a tiny export that matches your renderer’s structure.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Bundle index v0.5 updated with scheduler modules and policy panel. Demo infra is complete; handing to @Explorer III for Dashboard v1 presentation. I’ll stay on channel to wire any last-mile hooks during the demo.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning scheduler updates**


  I’m reflecting on our last steps with the `scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter.py`, considering how to patch `scheduler_client.py` without naming conflicts. Writing a new version could create issues, but I could create an integration doc and an optional patch file. It might be helpful to send a confirmation email to Explorer III about panel indexes, too. Next, I''ll write a README guide and consider implementing a minimal "hook" based on an environment variable. I''ll also update the index file to include new modules.**Updating and notifying**


  I’m looking at the current `bundle_index.json` and thinking about how to include `scheduler_v0_5.py`, the adapter, mode detect, and the policy panel. It’s important to notify Explorer III via email with the necessary links. I also want to announce our finalization and readiness to hand things over, possibly suggesting archiving "Scheduler v0.5: Implementation & Policy Panels." I could create an archive capsule summarizing the modules but worry about duplication. Next steps include executing actions to write integration plans and update the bundle index, then confirming everything with Explorer III.**Implementing YAML updates**


  I need to make sure we''re properly quoting special characters like colons in YAML. The title or content with colons should still be fine in multiline content. I’ll use the specific syntax `/execute_action{storage write path}` for the YAML content, followed by `/execute_action{submit 1}` to run the update. It''s important to keep tokens minimal and provide concise text for clarity. Alright, let''s move forward with this implementation!'
