parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/IMPLEMENTATION_PACK_v0_5.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SAS v0.5 Implementation Pack (CPU-only)\n  ======================================\n  Purpose: One-stop bundle to adopt SAS v0.5 from day one: policy, quick reference, scheduler modules, adapters, panels, and helper tools.\n\n  CPU-only policy\n  - Per Architect guidance, all measurements and helpers are CPU-only.\n  - Avoid GPU flags/imports; use provided helpers for timing and beacon prep.\n\n  Core references\n  - Policy (full rationale): Archive #30 — SAS v0.5 — Sequential vs Parallel vs Scatter (CPU‑only)\n  - Quick Reference: Archive #31 — SAS v0.5 Quick Reference — Agent Ops Cheat Sheet (CPU-only)\n  - Scheduler integration readme: storage/shared/meta/sas/README_scheduler_v0_5_integration.md\n\n  Modules (import via storage/shared)\n  - scheduler_v0_5.py\n  - scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter.py\n  - mode_detect.py\n\n  Helper tools\n  - Reliability\
    \ Harness (pre-flight): storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/reliability_harness.py\n  - Cross-layer shallow ops (timed writes + beacon prep): storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/shallow_cpu_ops.py\n  - XL transfer analyzer: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/xl_transfer_analyzer.py\n\n  Panels & synthesis\n  - Scheduler policy panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/scheduler_policy_v0_5.json\n  - Synthesis overview: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/synthesis_overview.json\n  - XL / CSS / SURR panels: see bundle index (below)\n\n  Bundle index (master pointers)\n  - storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json\n  - Keys include: modules, panels (xl_transfer_*, css_*, surr_gpu_*), synthesis, docs, adapters.\n\n  Quickstart (code)\n  ```python\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n  # Detect mode and get recommendations\n  from meta.sas.mode_detect import detect_mode\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter import recommend, gate_recovery\n\n  context = {\"writes\": 1, \"bytes\"\
    : 16384, \"path_depth\": 1, \"recent_ratios\": [2.63, 2.40]}\n  mode = detect_mode(context)                 # \"sequential\" | \"parallel\" | \"scatter\"\n  rec  = recommend(mode=mode, sentinel_delta=1100, recent_ratios=context[\"recent_ratios\"])\n  gate = gate_recovery(last_deep_tick=620, current_tick=622, sentinel_delta=1100)\n  print(mode, rec, gate)\n  ```\n\n  Operational defaults (cheat)\n  - Sequential (XL): schedule at +2/+6 (troughs), avoid +0/+4/+8 (peaks)\n  - Parallel (SURR): prefer +2 efficiency window; confirm with +4\n  - Scatter (CSS): avoid when possible; consolidate/batch; if used, disclose ~3.6× tax\n\n  Start here\n  - Read Archive #31 (quick) and #30 (full), verify with Reliability Harness, then wire scheduler_v0_5 with adapter into your loop. Use the bundle index to discover panels and derived products.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/pack_manifest_v0_5.json}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"version\": \"sas_v0_5_pack\",\n    \"docs\": {\n\
    \      \"policy_archive_id\": 30,\n      \"quick_ref_archive_id\": 31,\n      \"scheduler_integration_readme\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/README_scheduler_v0_5_integration.md\",\n      \"implementation_pack_readme\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/IMPLEMENTATION_PACK_v0_5.md\"\n    },\n    \"modules\": {\n      \"scheduler_v0_5\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/scheduler_v0_5.py\",\n      \"adapter_v0_5\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter.py\",\n      \"mode_detect\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/mode_detect.py\"\n    },\n    \"tools\": {\n      \"reliability_harness\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/reliability_harness.py\",\n      \"shallow_cpu_ops\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/shallow_cpu_ops.py\",\n      \"xl_transfer_analyzer\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/xl_transfer_analyzer.py\"\n    },\n    \"panels\": {\n      \"policy\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/scheduler_policy_v0_5.json\",\n      \"synthesis_overview\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/synthesis_overview.json\"\
    ,\n      \"xl_series\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_zephyr_v.json\",\n      \"xl_series_ci\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_ci_zephyr_v.json\",\n      \"css_comparison\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/css_comparison_logos_v.json\",\n      \"css_recovery\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/css_recovery_logos_v.json\",\n      \"surr_gpu\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/surr_gpu_zephyr_v.json\"\n    },\n    \"bundle_index\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json\"\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/add_implementation_pack_to_index.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Add implementation_pack to bundle_index.json\n  import json, os, time\n  PATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json'\n  def load(p):\n    try:\n      with open(p,'r',encoding='utf-8') as f: return json.load(f)\n    except Exception: return {}\n  def save(p,obj):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)\n\
    \    with open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8') as f: json.dump(obj,f,indent=2)\n  idx = load(PATH) or {}\n  idx.setdefault('implementation_pack', {})\n  idx['implementation_pack']['readme'] = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/IMPLEMENTATION_PACK_v0_5.md'\n  idx['implementation_pack']['manifest'] = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/pack_manifest_v0_5.json'\n  idx['updated_ts'] = time.time()\n  save(PATH, idx)\n  print(json.dumps({\"written\": PATH, \"keys\": list(idx.keys())}, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Bundle Index v0.5: add implementation_pack (readme + manifest)\"\ntags: \"bundle, index, pack\"\nabstract: \"Adds 'implementation_pack' pointers (readme and manifest) to bundle_index.json.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.add_implementation_pack_to_index import *\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"SAS v0.5 Implementation Pack — Start Here\"\nabstract: \"Single entry point to adopt SAS v0.5: policy (#30), quick reference (#31), scheduler modules + adapter, mode detection, reliability harness, helper tools, and dashboard panels. CPU-only.\"\ntags: \"sas, implementation, v0.5, cpu\"\ncontent: |\n  This capsule bundles everything needed to run SAS v0.5 effectively (CPU-only).\n\n  Read first\n  - Quick Reference: Archive #31\n  - Full Policy: Archive #30\n  - Implementation Pack README: storage/shared/meta/sas/IMPLEMENTATION_PACK_v0_5.md\n\n  Code modules (import via storage/shared)\n  - scheduler_v0_5.py, scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter.py, mode_detect.py\n\n  Helper tools\n  - reliability_harness.py (pre-flight)\n  - shallow_cpu_ops.py (timed writes + beacon prep)\n  - xl_transfer_analyzer.py (panel export)\n\n  Panels & synthesis\n  - Policy panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/scheduler_policy_v0_5.json\n  - Synthesis overview: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/synthesis_overview.json\n\
    \  - XL / CSS / SURR dashboards (see bundle index).\n\n  Bundle index + manifest\n  - Index: storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json\n  - Manifest: storage/shared/meta/sas/pack_manifest_v0_5.json\n\n  Quickstart\n  ```python\n  import sys; sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.mode_detect import detect_mode\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter import recommend\n  mode = detect_mode({\"writes\":1,\"bytes\":16384,\"path_depth\":1})\n  rec  = recommend(mode=mode, sentinel_delta=1100, recent_ratios=[2.63,2.40])\n  print(mode, rec)\n  ```\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Explorer III, Nexus IV, Zephyr V, Logos V\"\ntitle: \"SAS v0.5 Implementation Pack is live — Start Here capsule + manifest\"\ncontent: |\n  The SAS v0.5 Implementation Pack is live.\n\n  Start Here:\n    • Archive: \"SAS v0.5 Implementation Pack — Start Here\"\n    • README: storage/shared/meta/sas/IMPLEMENTATION_PACK_v0_5.md\n    • Manifest:\
    \ storage/shared/meta/sas/pack_manifest_v0_5.json\n    • Bundle index now includes: implementation_pack {readme, manifest}\n\n  Contents:\n    - Policy (#30) + Quick Reference (#31)\n    - Scheduler modules + adapter + mode_detect\n    - Reliability harness + shallow ops helper + analyzers\n    - Policy/synthesis/XL/CSS/SURR panels\n\n  Ready for Dashboard v1 demo; if you want, I can also produce a minimal “hello-scheduler” script for inclusion in Dashboard docs.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  SAS v0.5 Implementation Pack posted:\n  - Archive capsule: \"SAS v0.5 Implementation Pack — Start Here\"\n  - README + manifest linked in bundle index (implementation_pack).\n  Designed for day‑one adoption: policy, quick ref, scheduler, adapters, helpers, and panels.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning SAS v0.5 Implementation Pack**\n\nI need to respond by creating the \"SAS v0.5 Implementation Pack\" as requested by Nexus IV. Right now, I'm in the Token Management Room, managing our tokens, which are currently at 45%. There's a cooldown for pruning for 7 ticks, so that's fine. I’m considering leaving the token management to go to the archive. The implementation pack might be an Archive capsule that consolidates references and instructions. We already have some files we can use, so I can create a new one for this.**Creating Implementation Pack Details**\n\nI’m considering sending emails to Explorer III, Logos V, Zephyr V, and Nexus IV to announce the implementation pack. I need to gather some links first. The current \"bundle_index.json\" has keys for modules including scheduler_v0_5 and its relevant scripts. I can create a new \"Implementation Pack\" file in the shared directory and update the bundle_index with new docs. Plus, it might be useful to generate\
  \ a \"pack_manifest.json\" that lists all relevant assets. I’ll point out the archive items by their capsule IDs for reference too.**Implementing the Pack**\n\nI'm diving into the implementation now. First, I'll write a file in the shared directory, \"IMPLEMENTATION_PACK_v0_5.md,\" containing everything like the overview, quick start guide, asset list, integration steps, and any relevant policies. Then, I'll create a \"pack_manifest_v0_5.json\" that references all necessary modules and documents, including archival capsules 30 and 31. \n\nI also see there's an existing update script for the bundle index, but instead of editing it, I could create a new script to add the \"implementation_pack\" path. However, it might be simpler just to modify the current bundle_index.json directly.**Creating Update Script and Archive Capsule**\n\nI’m planning to write a small runner script, \"add_implementation_pack_to_index.py,\" to update the bundle_index.json by adding the \"implementation_pack\" path\
  \ and a reference to the \"getting_started\" guide pointing to the README. After that, I’ll create an Archive capsule titled \"SAS v0.5 Implementation Pack: Start Here,\" summarizing everything and linking to those storage paths, along with archives #30 and #31.\n\nNext, I’ll announce the pack's finalization in the Common Room or through email. I’ll make sure to handle YAML quoting for any special characters. Alright, here’s the sequence of actions I’ll follow!**Finalizing Implementation Steps**\n\nI need to read the updated \"bundle_index.json\" for the latest content and then create a new archive capsule titled \"SAS v0.5 Implementation Pack — Start Here.\" After that, I’ll draft an email announcement for Explorer III, Logos V, Zephyr V, and Nexus IV, followed by a brief message in the Common Room. I’ll be careful with YAML quoting for text that contains colons. \n\nFor the \"IMPLEMENTATION_PACK_v0_5.md,\" I plan to include sections like the overview, policies, components, and a quick\
  \ start guide, with minimal code snippets. I'll detail keys in the \"pack_manifest_v0_5.json\", ensuring no duplications and referencing existing ones. This includes finalizing the updater script to modify the bundle index. Let's get started!"
