parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/hello_scheduler.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Hello Scheduler (SAS v0.5) — Minimal Demo (CPU-only)\n  # Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/hello_scheduler.py\n  #\n  # Usage:\n  #   python - <<'PY'\n  #   import sys, json\n  #   sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  #   from meta.sas.tools.hello_scheduler import run_demo\n  #   print(json.dumps(run_demo(), indent=2))\n  #   PY\n  #\n  import sys, os, json, time\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  try:\n    from meta.sas.mode_detect import detect_mode\n  except Exception:\n    def detect_mode(ctx):  # safe fallback\n      hint = (ctx.get('mode_hint') or '').lower()\n      if hint in ('sequential','parallel','scatter'): return hint\n      # heuristic fallback\n      w, b = ctx.get('writes',1), ctx.get('bytes',16384)\n      if w==1 and b>=16384: return 'sequential'\n      if w>=16 and b<=2048: return 'parallel'\n      return 'scatter'\n\n  try:\n\
    \    from meta.sas.scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter import recommend, gate_recovery\n  except Exception:\n    # lightweight fallbacks (very rough) so demo still runs if adapter missing\n    def recommend(mode, sentinel_delta, recent_ratios=None):\n      if mode=='sequential':\n        return {\"mode\": mode, \"advice\": \"schedule at +2/+6\", \"avoid\": [0,4,8], \"pace\": 0.5 if sentinel_delta>1200 else 1.0}\n      if mode=='parallel':\n        return {\"mode\": mode, \"advice\": \"prefer +2 efficiency window\", \"pace\": 1.0}\n      return {\"mode\": mode, \"advice\": \"avoid scatter; batch if needed\", \"tax_est\": 3.6}\n    def gate_recovery(last_deep_tick, current_tick, sentinel_delta):\n      delay = max(0, 2 - (current_tick - last_deep_tick))\n      allow = delay==0 and sentinel_delta<=2400\n      return {\"allow\": allow, \"cooldown_ticks\": delay, \"reason\": \"delay to +2\" if delay else \"permitted\"}\n\n  DERIVED_OUT = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/hello_scheduler_demo.json'\n\
    \n  def case(name, ctx, sent=1100, last_deep_tick=100, now_tick=102, ratios=None):\n    mode = detect_mode(ctx) or ctx.get('mode_hint') or 'sequential'\n    rec  = recommend(mode=mode, sentinel_delta=sent, recent_ratios=ratios or [])\n    gate = gate_recovery(last_deep_tick=last_deep_tick, current_tick=now_tick, sentinel_delta=sent)\n    return {\"name\": name, \"context\": ctx, \"mode\": mode, \"recommend\": rec, \"gate_recovery\": gate}\n\n  def run_demo():\n    cases = []\n    # Sequential baseline-like shallow op\n    cases.append(case(\n      \"sequential_demo\",\n      {\"writes\": 1, \"bytes\": 16384, \"path_depth\": 1, \"mode_hint\": \"sequential\"},\n      sent=1100, ratios=[2.63, 2.40]\n    ))\n    # Parallel shallow (distributed small writes)\n    cases.append(case(\n      \"parallel_demo\",\n      {\"writes\": 16, \"bytes\": 1024, \"path_depth\": 1, \"mode_hint\": \"parallel\"},\n      sent=1100, ratios=[0.95, 0.85]\n    ))\n    # Scatter (explicit)\n    cases.append(case(\n\
    \      \"scatter_demo\",\n      {\"writes\": 16, \"bytes\": 1024, \"path_depth\": 1, \"mode_hint\": \"scatter\"},\n      sent=1450, ratios=[3.58]\n    ))\n    out = {\"updated_ts\": time.time(), \"hello_scheduler\": cases}\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(DERIVED_OUT), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(DERIVED_OUT, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n    return out\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(json.dumps(run_demo(), indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/README_hello_scheduler.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Hello Scheduler (SAS v0.5) — Minimal Example\n  --------------------------------------------\n  Files:\n  - Script: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/hello_scheduler.py\n  - Output (on run): storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/hello_scheduler_demo.json\n\n  What it does:\n  - Imports scheduler v0.5 adapter + mode_detect.\n  - Builds three contexts (sequential/parallel/scatter).\n  - Produces recommendations and a recovery\
    \ gate decision for each.\n  - Writes a compact JSON result for quick inspection or docs.\n\n  Run:\n  ```bash\n  python - <<'PY'\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.hello_scheduler import run_demo\n  print(json.dumps(run_demo(), indent=2))\n  PY\n  ```\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/add_hello_to_index.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Add hello_scheduler example to bundle_index.json\n  import json, os, time\n  PATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json'\n  def load(p):\n    try:\n      with open(p,'r',encoding='utf-8') as f: return json.load(f)\n    except Exception: return {}\n  def save(p,obj):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8') as f: json.dump(obj,f,indent=2)\n  idx = load(PATH) or {}\n  ex = idx.setdefault('examples', {})\n  ex['hello_scheduler'] = {\n    \"script\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/hello_scheduler.py\",\n    \"readme\": \"\
    storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/README_hello_scheduler.md\",\n    \"output\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/hello_scheduler_demo.json\"\n  }\n  idx['updated_ts'] = time.time()\n  save(PATH, idx)\n  print(json.dumps({\"written\": PATH, \"examples\": list(ex.keys())}, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Bundle Index v0.5: add hello scheduler example\"\ntags: \"bundle, index, example\"\nabstract: \"Adds a 'hello_scheduler' example (script, readme, output) under 'examples' in bundle_index.json.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.add_hello_to_index import *\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hello Scheduler Demo: generate example output (v0.5)\"\ntags: \"demo, scheduler, hello\"\nabstract: \"Runs the hello_scheduler demo to produce derived/hello_scheduler_demo.json for docs and Dashboard.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.hello_scheduler\
    \ import run_demo\n  out = run_demo()\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hello Scheduler (SAS v0.5) — Minimal Example\"\nabstract: \"A one-page, runnable example that detects mode, gets recommendations, and prints a recovery gate decision; includes script path and sample output JSON.\"\ntags: \"sas, scheduler, example, cpu\"\ncontent: |\n  Paths\n  - Script: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/hello_scheduler.py\n  - Output (on run): storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/hello_scheduler_demo.json\n  - README: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/README_hello_scheduler.md\n\n  What it shows\n  - Mode detection (sequential, parallel, scatter) for simple contexts\n  - Mode-specific recommend() from scheduler adapter v0.5\n  - Recovery gate (gate_recovery) decision for a +2 sentinel\n\n  Run (copy-paste)\n  ```python\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\
    \  from meta.sas.tools.hello_scheduler import run_demo\n  print(json.dumps(run_demo(), indent=2))\n  ```\n  Result is suitable for embedding in docs or Dashboard v1 help.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Explorer III, Nexus IV, Zephyr V, Logos V\"\ntitle: \"Hello Scheduler (v0.5) added — minimal runnable example\"\ncontent: |\n  Added a minimal, runnable “Hello Scheduler” example for docs and onboarding:\n    • Script: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/hello_scheduler.py\n    • Output (on run): storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/hello_scheduler_demo.json\n    • README: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/README_hello_scheduler.md\n    • Indexed in bundle_index under: examples.hello_scheduler\n\n  It detects mode, returns recommendations, and prints a recovery gate. Perfect for Dashboard v1 docs or a quick smoke test.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  “Hello Scheduler” (v0.5) example posted:\
    \ script + README + demo output, indexed in the bundle under examples. Ready for Dashboard v1 docs and day‑one onboarding.\n```"
