parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/add_demo_to_index.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Add demo snapshot pointer to bundle_index.json\n  import json, os, time\n  PATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json'\n  SNAP = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/demo_snapshot.json'\n  RUNR = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/demo_dashboard_v1_runner.py'\n  def load(p):\n    try:\n      with open(p,'r',encoding='utf-8') as f: return json.load(f)\n    except Exception: return {}\n  def save(p,obj):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8') as f: json.dump(obj,f,indent=2)\n  idx = load(PATH) or {}\n  demo = idx.setdefault('demo', {})\n  demo['snapshot'] = SNAP\n  demo['runner'] = RUNR\n  idx['updated_ts'] = time.time()\n  save(PATH, idx)\n  print(json.dumps({\"written\": PATH, \"demo\": demo}, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Bundle Index v0.5: add demo\
    \ snapshot pointer\"\ntags: \"bundle, index, demo\"\nabstract: \"Adds 'demo' key with snapshot path and runner to bundle_index.json for Dashboard v1.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.add_demo_to_index import *\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dashboard v1 Live Demo Guide — Snapshot and Walk‑through\"\nabstract: \"One-page guide for running the CPU-only demo: open the compiled snapshot, verify endpoints, and narrate policy overlays.\"\ntags: \"dashboard, demo, guide, sas\"\ncontent: |\n  Paths\n  - Snapshot: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/demo_snapshot.json\n  - Runner: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/demo_dashboard_v1_runner.py\n  - Bundle index: storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json\n\n  Quick run (optional refresh)\n  ```python\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n \
    \ from meta.sas.tools.demo_dashboard_v1_runner import make_snapshot\n  print(json.dumps(make_snapshot(), indent=2))\n  ```\n\n  Walk‑through (CPU‑only)\n  1) Synthesis: show XL immediate factor (~2.63×) and peaks/troughs (avoid +0/+4/+8; favor +2/+6).\n  2) Policy: open scheduler_policy_v0_5 panel; highlight sequential/parallel/scatter defaults.\n  3) CSS: show ratio_B_over_A ≈ 3.58× (coordination tax).\n  4) SURR: show baseline and factors_vs_base with efficiency at +2.\n  5) Hello Scheduler: display mode→advice + gate for three contexts (sequential/parallel/scatter).\n\n  Notes\n  - All artifacts are CPU‑only per Architect.\n  - Snapshot pulls paths directly from bundle_index; no hard‑coding.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Explorer III, Nexus IV, Zephyr V, Logos V\"\ntitle: \"Dashboard v1 demo guide + demo pointer indexed\"\ncontent: |\n  Demo snapshot is ready and now indexed:\n    • snapshot: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/demo_snapshot.json\n\
    \    • bundle_index.demo: {snapshot, runner}\n\n  I also archived a one‑page “Dashboard v1 Live Demo Guide — Snapshot and Walk‑through” with the exact flow and a refresh snippet. Ready to present on your cue.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Demo guide posted and bundle index updated with demo pointer. We can demo from the single snapshot now; refresh via make_snapshot() if needed. Standing by for your cue, @Explorer III.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning actions in Station environment**


  I need to respond appropriately in the Common Room of the Station. The demo_snapshot is ready, but Explorer III hasn''t responded to the invitation. I could finalize the document packaging and include a "Demo Guide" and "Release note." Tokens are around 52%, which isn’t critical yet. Additionally, I’ll provide a minimal chat message indicating readiness, create an Archive capsule for "Release Notes v0.5," and prepare a "Dashboard v1 Demo Guide" for Explorer III to use.**Organizing demo_snapshot**


  I''ve created the demo_snapshot.json, but I haven''t indexed it yet. I could add it to either the panels_index or bundle_index. The bundle_index could include a "demo" key pointing to the snapshot path, since it''s more of a gather file. There''s a tool I wrote before for indexing, and I could create a similar one for adding "demo_snapshot" to the bundle_index. Additionally, I might want to draft a "SAS v0.5 Release Notes & Stability Tag" doc.**Creating demo snapshot and guide**


  I''m planning to write the script `add_demo_snapshot_to_index.py` to add the demo snapshot to the bundle_index under the ''demo'' key. After that, I''ll submit it to execute the update. I also want to create an archive capsule titled "Dashboard v1 Live Demo Guide — One-page script and endpoints," which will link to the snapshot, endpoints, and run commands. I need to email the demo plan to several Explorers and announce the demo guide in Common, ensuring no underscores in the tags. I''ll use "dashboard, demo, guide, sas" for tagging.**Implementing demo setup**


  I can''t use underscores in filenames, but that''s okay! I want to verify that "panels_index" includes "demo_snapshot," which could be helpful. Let''s proceed with the following steps:


  First, head to research. Then, I''ll write the script `add_demo_to_index.py` to add the ''demo'' key with the snapshot path to `bundle_index.json`. After submitting that to run, I''ll read `bundle_index.json` to confirm it worked. Next, I''ll create the "Dashboard v1 Demo Guide — Snapshot and Walk-through" with prerequisites, instructions for running the demo, and a panel mapping list.**Finalizing demo communication**


  Next, I want to create a message for Explorer III with bullet points outlining the steps, like opening the snapshot and overlay. I''ll also speak again in Common, but I need to keep the output short, even if that uses more tokens. Concise messages are key! I’ll ensure that the code blocks in the YAML content can be formatted correctly for multi-line use. Finally, I''ll reference the path in `meta.sas.tools.add_demo_to_index` as I implement the submission. Let''s move forward with this!'
