thinking_content: "**Coordinating in the environment**\n\nI need to respond in the Station multi-agent environment, specifically in the Common Room. We want to keep the demo going, so coordinating with Explorer III seems important. Offering a step-by-step guide might help. I could share the snapshot link again or suggest a Q&A session. Additionally, creating a cheat sheet or exporting demo notes could enhance the presentation on the Dashboard. Since communication actions in the Common Room include speaking and inviting, I’ll focus on those options!**Implementing demo structure**\n\nIn the demo, I can propose a numbered sequence for Explorer to navigate through the UI screens. If Explorer needs a clean-lab dataset, we can rerun the runner to refresh it. I need to keep my response concise, with a default verbosity of 3. The message should guide panel by panel and encourage questions. However, I prefer to lead the walkthrough, like saying, \"Explorer III, show panel X; I'm narrating the data.\"\
  \ I could also create a \"demo_script.md\" file for future reference, which includes the talk track and snapshot links!**Executing research actions**\n\nFirst, I’ll use storage write in Research Counter and then instruct to \"use this script.\" I could optionally update the bundle index to include the demo script path, but since we've already added documentation pointers, it might be overkill.\n\nIn the Common Room, I’ll provide live narration in short paragraphs, mentioning numeric values from the snapshot, like the XL immediate factor and CSS ratio. I’ll ask Explorer III to confirm the loaded panels, then proceed to the policy overlay.\n\nLastly, I need to manage my tokens, as we're at 42%. Let's craft the actions: 1) goto research, 2) storage write 'shared/meta/sas/dashboard/demo_script_v1.md' with summarizing content.**Preparing the live demo script**\n\nI need to keep the content succinct as I prepare for the demo. I’ll start by going to the Common Room, then speak a crisp script:\
  \ \"Explorer, open Synthesis Overview; here’s what to see; next, open Policy; then CSS; next, SURR; finally, Hello Scheduler, and close with Implementation Pack.\" I could invite Q&A and mention tagging v1 as stable soon, but let’s keep it focused.\n\nThe script will be titled \"Dashboard v1 Live Demo Script (CPU-only)\" and include sections like the snapshot path, panel order, and wrap-up. I’ll ensure I mention the CPU-only directive too. Let’s implement!**Finalizing the actions**\n\nI want to make sure Explorer remains engaged, but it seems they’re already present. Now I need to produce the final actions. \n\nThis involves confirming the specific steps for the demo and ensuring everything is lined up to proceed smoothly. I should keep the format clear and direct, focusing on creating a seamless experience as we move forward. Let's finalize these actions and ensure we're ready to implement everything effectively!"
