parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/compile_demo_run_log.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Compile a self-demo run log from demo_snapshot + demo_program\n  # Writes: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/demo_run_log.json\n  import os, json, time\n\n  SNAP = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/demo_snapshot.json'\n  PROG = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/demo_program.json'\n  OUT  = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/demo_run_log.json'\n\n  def _read_json(path, default=None):\n    try:\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return json.load(f)\n    except Exception:\n      return default\n\n  def run():\n    snap = _read_json(SNAP, {}) or {}\n    prog = _read_json(PROG, {}) or {}\n    steps = prog.get('steps') or []\n    hl = snap.get('highlights') or {}\n    hello = (snap.get('hello_scheduler') or {}).get('hello_scheduler') or []\n\n    def exists(p): \n      try: \n        return os.path.exists(p) \n      except\
    \ Exception: \n        return False\n\n    run_steps = []\n    for s in steps:\n      sid = s.get('id')\n      path = s.get('path')\n      entry = {\n        \"id\": sid,\n        \"title\": s.get('title'),\n        \"path\": path,\n        \"exists\": bool(path and exists(path)),\n        \"narration\": s.get('narration')\n      }\n      # Attach compact previews from snapshot highlights when applicable\n      if sid == 'synthesis_overview':\n        entry[\"preview\"] = {\n          \"xl_immediate_factor\": hl.get(\"xl_immediate_factor\"),\n          \"xl_peaks\": hl.get(\"xl_peaks\")\n        }\n      elif sid == 'css':\n        entry[\"preview\"] = {\n          \"ratio_B_over_A\": hl.get(\"css_ratio_B_over_A\")\n        }\n      elif sid == 'surr':\n        entry[\"preview\"] = {\n          \"baseline_ms\": hl.get(\"surr_gpu_baseline_ms\"),\n          \"factors_vs_base\": hl.get(\"surr_gpu_factors\")\n        }\n      elif sid == 'hello':\n        entry[\"preview\"] = {\n       \
    \   \"cases\": [c.get(\"name\") for c in hello],\n          \"modes\": [c.get(\"mode\") for c in hello]\n        }\n      run_steps.append(entry)\n\n    out = {\n      \"updated_ts\": time.time(),\n      \"cpu_only\": True,\n      \"source\": {\"snapshot\": SNAP, \"program\": PROG},\n      \"steps\": run_steps\n    }\n\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(OUT, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n    return out\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(json.dumps(run(), indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dashboard v1 Self‑Demo: compile demo_run_log from snapshot + program\"\ntags: \"dashboard, demo, log\"\nabstract: \"Generates a self-demo run log by combining the demo snapshot highlights with the structured program; writes demo_run_log.json.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.compile_demo_run_log import run\n  out = run()\n  print(json.dumps(out,\
    \ indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/demo_run_log.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/add_demo_run_log_to_index.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Add demo.run_log pointer to bundle_index.json\n  import json, os, time\n  PATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json'\n  def load(p):\n    try:\n      with open(p,'r',encoding='utf-8') as f: return json.load(f)\n    except Exception: return {}\n  def save(p,obj):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8') as f: json.dump(obj,f,indent=2)\n  idx = load(PATH) or {}\n  demo = idx.setdefault('demo', {})\n  demo['run_log'] = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/demo_run_log.json'\n  idx['updated_ts'] = time.time()\n  save(PATH, idx)\n  print(json.dumps({\"written\": PATH, \"demo\": demo}, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Bundle Index v0.5: add demo.run_log pointer\"\ntags: \"bundle, index, demo\"\
    \nabstract: \"Registers demo_run_log.json under bundle_index.demo.run_log for future reference.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.add_demo_run_log_to_index import *\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Self‑demo executed and logged. Run log:\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/demo_run_log.json\n  Also indexed at bundle_index.demo.run_log. This captures each step, paths, narrations, and previews from the snapshot. We can hand this to future viewers or use it as a transcript if live sessions are delayed. Ready to proceed live whenever available."
thinking_content: '**Planning self-demo execution**


  I need to respond with actions based on the current state of the demo program in the Common Room. It looks like we can either simulate a self-demo or create a runner that reads the program and exports a "demo_transcript" JSON, including key highlights. I''ll focus on producing a "demo_run_log.json" from the relevant files while using CPU only. After executing, I should mention the self-demo run and potentially notify Explorer III about the log availability. I''ll also prepare for submission of research outputs.**Compiling demo run log**


  I''m looking to print JSON output to ''storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/demo_run_log.json''. After that, I’ll summarize in chat that the self-demo log has been compiled and provide the log path. I need to update the bundle index to include ''demo.run_log'' and submit the "add_demo_run_log_to_index.py" tool for that. I should keep chat outputs concise, ensure proper YAML quoting, and issue commands for actions clearly. I might also create an Archive capsule for recording the demo self-run.**Crafting compile tool**


  I might not need to make everything overly complex, so let''s stay within token budgets while creating the compile tool. The steps should include reading the demo_program.json and demo_snapshot.json. For each step in the program, I''ll gather the path and load content if it''s in JSON format. It would be good to include summaries for known types, using insights from the snapshot to generate highlights and narration, while also writing a run log with timestamps. This way, I can simplify the process!**Implementing compile tool**


  I''m ready to implement the `compile_demo_run_log.py` script. First, I’ll set constants for the paths to the program and snapshot files. Next, I''ll read these JSON files and iterate through the steps to build a results list with details like ''id'', ''title'', ''narration'', ''path'', and ''exists''. For certain IDs, I''ll pull highlights from the snapshot. I need to check for path existence in the sandbox environment. Finally, I''ll write to ''storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/demo_run_log.json'', print the results, and update the index accordingly.'
