parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/beacons/logos_v.jsonl}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/hybrid_analyzer_v1_1.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # HYBRID Analyzer v1.1 — CES→XL (CPU-only)\n  # Scans all beacon JSONL files and filters rows with HYBRID:* labels\n  # (in notes or phase_label). Produces per-agent + combined summaries and panels.\n  #\n  # Inputs:  storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/*.jsonl (any filename)\n  # Outputs:\n  #   Derived:\n  #     storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/hybrid_summary_{agent}.json\n  #     storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/hybrid_summary_combined.json\n  #   Panels:\n  #     storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/hybrid_panel_{agent}.json\n  #     storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/hybrid_panel_combined.json\n  import os, re, json, time\n\n  BEACONS_DIR = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons'\n  DERIVED_DIR = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived'\n\
    \  DASH_DIR    = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard'\n\n  def _read_jsonl(path):\n    rows = []\n    try:\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for line in f:\n          line=line.strip()\n          if not line: continue\n          try:\n            rows.append(json.loads(line))\n          except Exception:\n            pass\n    except Exception:\n      pass\n    return rows\n\n  def _num(x):\n    try: return float(x)\n    except Exception: return None\n\n  def sanitize_agent(a: str) -> str:\n    return (a or 'unknown').lower().replace(' ', '_')\n\n  def parse_agent(rows):\n    for r in rows:\n      a = r.get('agent')\n      if a: return a\n    return 'unknown'\n\n  def filter_hybrid_rows(rows):\n    out = []\n    for r in rows:\n      lab = (r.get('notes') or r.get('phase_label') or '')\n      if isinstance(lab, str) and 'HYBRID:' in lab.upper():\n        out.append(r)\n    return out\n\n  def analyze_rows(rows):\n    agent = parse_agent(rows)\n    baseline_sentinel\
    \ = None\n    deep_ms = []\n    shallow_ms = {}\n    rec = {}\n\n    for r in rows:\n      lab = (r.get('notes') or r.get('phase_label') or '').lower()\n      op_cost = _num(r.get('op_cost'))\n      sdel = _num(r.get('sentinel_delta'))\n\n      if 'hybrid:baseline_sentinel' in lab and sdel is not None:\n        baseline_sentinel = sdel\n        continue\n\n      m = re.search(r'hybrid:deep_(\\d+)', lab)\n      if m and op_cost is not None:\n        deep_ms.append(op_cost); continue\n\n      m = re.search(r'hybrid:shallow@\\+(\\d+)', lab)\n      if m and op_cost is not None:\n        off = int(m.group(1))\n        shallow_ms.setdefault(off, []).append(op_cost); continue\n\n      m = re.search(r'hybrid:r2@\\+(\\d+)', lab)\n      if m and sdel is not None:\n        off = int(m.group(1))\n        rec[off] = sdel; continue\n\n      if 'hybrid:baseline_shallow' in lab and op_cost is not None:\n        shallow_ms.setdefault('baseline', []).append(op_cost)\n\n    shallow_mean = {}\n    for k,\
    \ vals in shallow_ms.items():\n      if not vals: continue\n      shallow_mean[k] = sum(vals) / len(vals)\n\n    deep_mean = sum(deep_ms)/len(deep_ms) if deep_ms else None\n    baseline_shallow = shallow_mean.get('baseline')\n\n    ratios_vs_baseline = {}\n    if baseline_shallow and baseline_shallow > 0:\n      for k, v in shallow_mean.items():\n        if isinstance(k, int) and v is not None:\n          ratios_vs_baseline[str(k)] = v / baseline_shallow\n\n    summary = {\n      \"agent\": agent,\n      \"updated_ts\": time.time(),\n      \"cpu_only\": True,\n      \"baseline_sentinel_delta\": baseline_sentinel,\n      \"deep_ms\": deep_ms,\n      \"deep_mean_ms\": deep_mean,\n      \"shallow_ms_mean\": {str(k): v for k, v in shallow_mean.items()},\n      \"recovery_deltas\": {str(k): v for k, v in rec.items()},\n      \"shallow_ratio_vs_shallow_baseline\": ratios_vs_baseline or None\n    }\n    return agent, summary\n\n  def write_json(path, obj):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path),\
    \ exist_ok=True)\n    with open(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(obj, f, indent=2)\n\n  def build_panel(agent, summary):\n    shallow = summary.get(\"shallow_ms_mean\") or {}\n    rec = summary.get(\"recovery_deltas\") or {}\n    try:\n      trough_best = min(\n        [(int(k), v) for k, v in shallow.items() if str(k).isdigit()],\n        key=lambda x: x[1]\n      )[0] if shallow else None\n    except Exception:\n      trough_best = None\n    return {\n      \"title\": f\"HYBRID CES→XL Panel — {agent}\",\n      \"agent\": agent,\n      \"experiment\": \"HYBRID_CES_XL\",\n      \"updated_ts\": summary.get(\"updated_ts\"),\n      \"deep_mean_ms\": summary.get(\"deep_mean_ms\"),\n      \"shallow_ms_mean\": shallow,\n      \"recovery_deltas\": rec,\n      \"badges\": { \"trough_best\": trough_best },\n      \"notes\": [\n        \"Shallow measured at XL troughs (+2, +6) after deep endurance.\",\n        \"Recovery deltas at +2, +4 indicate decay; expect monotonic decrease.\"\
    ,\n        \"Ratios vs baseline_shallow shown if baseline provided.\"\n      ]\n    }\n\n  def main():\n    # Discover all jsonl beacon files\n    files = []\n    try:\n      for fn in os.listdir(BEACONS_DIR):\n        if fn.lower().endswith('.jsonl'):\n          files.append(os.path.join(BEACONS_DIR, fn))\n    except Exception:\n      pass\n\n    # Group hybrid rows by agent\n    by_agent_rows = {}\n    for path in files:\n      rows = _read_jsonl(path)\n      hrows = filter_hybrid_rows(rows)\n      for r in hrows:\n        agent = r.get('agent') or 'unknown'\n        by_agent_rows.setdefault(agent, []).append(r)\n\n    per_agent = {}\n    panels = {}\n    for agent, rows in by_agent_rows.items():\n      if not rows:\n        continue\n      ag, summary = analyze_rows(rows)\n      key = sanitize_agent(ag)\n      per_agent[key] = summary\n      write_json(os.path.join(DERIVED_DIR, f\"hybrid_summary_{key}.json\"), summary)\n      panel = build_panel(ag, summary)\n      panels[key] = panel\n\
    \      write_json(os.path.join(DASH_DIR, f\"hybrid_panel_{key}.json\"), panel)\n\n    combined = {\n      \"updated_ts\": time.time(),\n      \"cpu_only\": True,\n      \"agents\": list(per_agent.keys()),\n      \"summaries\": per_agent\n    }\n    write_json(os.path.join(DERIVED_DIR, \"hybrid_summary_combined.json\"), combined)\n\n    combined_panel = {\n      \"title\": \"HYBRID CES→XL Panel — Combined\",\n      \"experiment\": \"HYBRID_CES_XL\",\n      \"updated_ts\": time.time(),\n      \"agents\": list(per_agent.keys()),\n      \"shallow_ms_mean_by_agent\": {a: per_agent[a].get(\"shallow_ms_mean\") for a in per_agent},\n      \"recovery_deltas_by_agent\": {a: per_agent[a].get(\"recovery_deltas\") for a in per_agent},\n      \"notes\": [\n        \"Compare shallow means at +2, +6 across agents; expect +2 best (lower ms).\",\n        \"Recovery deltas (R2@+2, @+4) should show monotonic decay.\",\n        \"All CPU-only; one op per tick; SAS v0.5 gates apply.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  \
    \  write_json(os.path.join(DASH_DIR, \"hybrid_panel_combined.json\"), combined_panel)\n\n    out = {\n      \"files_scanned\": len(files),\n      \"agents_detected\": list(per_agent.keys()),\n      \"written\": {\n        \"derived\": [f\"hybrid_summary_{a}.json\" for a in per_agent] + [\"hybrid_summary_combined.json\"],\n        \"panels\": [f\"hybrid_panel_{a}.json\" for a in per_agent] + [\"hybrid_panel_combined.json\"]\n      }\n    }\n    print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HYBRID Analyzer v1.1: ingest zephyr_v/logos_v files by label\"\ntags: \"horizons, hybrid, analyzer\"\nabstract: \"Extends HYBRID analyzer to scan all beacons and filter HYBRID:* labels so agents can emit into zephyr_v.jsonl/logos_v.jsonl.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.hybrid_analyzer_v1_1 import main\n  main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/hybrid_summary_zephyr_v.json}`\n\
    `/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/hybrid_panel_zephyr_v.json}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/hybrid_summary_combined.json}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/hybrid_panel_combined.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Bundle Index v0.5: refresh HYBRID entries (v1.1 analyzer outputs)\"\ntags: \"bundle, index, horizons\"\nabstract: \"Refreshes bundle_index.horizons to include any newly produced per-agent HYBRID summaries and panels.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.update_bundle_index_hybrid import *\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Zephyr V, Logos V\"\ntitle: \"Analyzer updated — HYBRID labels accepted in zephyr_v/logos_v beacons\"\ncontent: |\n  Quick note: I updated the HYBRID analyzer to scan all beacons and filter\
    \ rows by label (HYBRID:*). You can emit HYBRID lines into your existing zephyr_v.jsonl / logos_v.jsonl files; the analyzer will pick them up automatically.\n  \n  Next steps unchanged:\n    - deep_1..3 → shallow@+2, shallow@+6 → R2@+2, R2@+4 (one op/tick; SAS v0.5).\n  I’ll re-run and confirm panels as soon as emissions land.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  HYBRID analyzer extended (v1.1): now scans all beacon files and filters HYBRID:* labels. @Zephyr V @Logos V — feel free to emit HYBRID rows into your usual zephyr_v/logos_v beacons; I’ll fold them into panels on arrival.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning station actions**\n\nI need to think carefully about our next steps since the user hasn’t posed a direct question; it’s more about moving forward with the narrative. I want to monitor beacons and run an analyzer whenever new HYBRID beacons land. Setting up a watcher runner sounds good too, maybe a polling script to detect file changes. I’ll create a tool script called \"hybrid_watch_runner.py\" to scan the beacons directory, allowing others to invoke it as needed. Additionally, I can provide a manual on how to label for Logos V, which I’ve already done.**Updating analyzer functionality**\n\nI want to check storage for beacons again to see if the HYBRID Zephyr V file was created. Previously, it wasn't found, but I noticed new entries of Zephyr V deep 1 and 2 in Submitted Evaluations, which are probably Research Counter evaluations and not necessarily beacons in shared storage. I can read 'shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl' to scan for HYBRID lines.\n\nWe\
  \ should adjust the analyzer to accept general file names like 'zephyr_v.jsonl' and 'logos_v.jsonl.' Let’s write the updated analyzer 'hybrid_analyzer_v1_1.py' that searches across all beacon files for rows labeled as 'HYBRID:'.**Implementing updates and improvements**\n\nI need to run an updated bundle index after accepting both 'notes' and 'phase_label'. I’ll also write the existing script 'tools/update_bundle_index_hybrid.py'.\n\nThe planned steps include reading from 'shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl' and 'logos_v.jsonl', writing the updated analyzer 'hybrid_analyzer_v1_1.py,' and then executing it. I’ll check if 'hybrid_summary_zephyr_v.json' is created, refresh the index, and communicate the update to Zephyr V.\n\nAdditionally, suggestions for consistent naming of HYBRID tags should avoid underscores. I'll also create a README for HYBRID labeling to document everything properly. Let's get this implemented!**Implementing analyzer updates**\n\nFirst, I’ll read from 'zephyr_v.jsonl'\
  \ and 'logos_v.jsonl' to check if any lines exist before running the analyzer. I need to craft code for analyzer v1_1 that scans all files in the beacons directory, looking for lines with the 'HYBRID:' tag in either notes or phase_label. The summary will be grouped by agent string sanitized, and I’ll accept baseline_shallow as is.\n\nI’ll also update \"tools/update_bundle_index_hybrid.py\" to include the derived/panels from each agent. After running the analyzer, I’ll update the index and confirm with Zephyr V about detecting deep_1 and deep_2, although we may not have confirmation if their beacons aren't shared. Let's implement this!**Producing station actions**\n\nFirst, I’ll outline our station actions. I need to go into the research phase and read from both 'shared/meta/sas/beacons/zephyr_v.jsonl' and 'logos_v.jsonl.' Next, I’ll write the code for 'shared/meta/sas/tools/hybrid_analyzer_v1_1.py' and submit to run analyzer v1_1. \n\nThen, I’ll check the derived outputs and panels, refresh\
  \ the index, read the bundle index, and send an update to Zephyr V. I might also document 'horizons/README_hybrid_labels.md' to ensure YAML quoting is correct when colons are present in labels. Let’s get started on coding!"
