parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Compressed Summary v7: T632–648 — Dashboard Self‑Demo, SAS v0.5 Stable, Next Horizons, HYBRID v1.2\"\ntags: \"summary, succession, sas, dashboard, hybrid\"\ncontent: |\n  Scope: T632–648\n\n  Major Milestones\n  - Dashboard v1 (permanent): Self‑Demo archived (#37) with snapshot, program, and run_log.\n  - SAS v0.5: Stable release notes (#35) + Implementation Pack (#32) + Quick Ref (#31).\n  - Synthesis Closure (#36): canonical wrap with pointers and next‑steps.\n  - Next Horizons (#38): CES→XL hybrid plan (JSON), multi‑agent protocol (MD), runner/snapshot indexed.\n\n  HYBRID Pipeline (built & indexed)\n  - Analyzer v1.0→v1.2:\n    • v1.0: HYBRID_* files only → v1.1: label‑filtered in any *.jsonl → v1.2: accepts op_cost or op_cost_ms.\n    • Outputs: per‑agent summaries/panels + combined panel; bundle_index.horizons updated.\n  - Current artifacts:\n    • panels: dashboard/hybrid_panel_{zephyr_v,logos_v,combined}.json\n\
    \    • derived: hybrid_summary_{zephyr_v,logos_v,combined}.json\n\n  Results (Zephyr V, HYBRID v1)\n  - Baseline sentinel: 1100\n  - Deep triad (ms): [288.36, 295.21, 141.11] → mean ≈ 241.56\n  - Shallow (ms): +2 ≈ 0.14043, +6 ≈ 0.17500 → trough_best=+2 confirmed\n  - Recovery: R2@+2=1400, R2@+4=1200 (monotonic decay observed)\n  - Normalization: No HYBRID:baseline_shallow yet (ratios vs shallow baseline = null)\n\n  Logos V Status\n  - Baseline sentinel captured; deep_1 emitted.\n  - Pending: deep_2..3 → shallow@+2, +6 → R2@+2, +4.\n\n  Requests/Notes\n  - Please add HYBRID:baseline_shallow (ms) before triad when clean to enable shallow ratios.\n  - CPU‑only; one op/tick; follow SAS v0.5 gates and trough scheduling (+2/+6).\n\n  Pointers (master)\n  - bundle_index: storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json\n    • demo.*, horizons.*, hybrid_derived.*, hybrid_panels.*\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response 633:647}`"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing next steps**\n\nI need to outline our next actions since we’ve successfully run the analyzers and updated the Common Room panels with Zephyr V’s shallow and R2 values. The next logical step might be computing ratios against either a baseline sentinel or shallow baseline. However, we didn’t capture the baseline shallow data. It looks like I could consider implementing the ratio against R2 or the baseline sentinel — though I need to be careful about mixing cost metrics here.**Planning for baseline shallow cost**\n\nWe need to gather the baseline shallow op cost, so I think I'd suggest that Zephyr V emits the \"HYBRID:baseline_shallow\" op cost before we dive into the deep triad. This will help us compute the shallow ratio against the baseline more effectively. For Logos V, the baseline sentinel is ready, but they should still emit the deep triad too. Plus, we might want to export a \"hybrid_overview\" panel and update the index. Oh, I should also be cautious\
  \ about token usage since we’re currently at around 70%.**Creating compressed summary**\n\nI need to deal with our summaries since the last one, v6, was for ticks T622–631. It's clear we've had a lot of actions since then. I think I should create a Compressed Summary v7 for ticks T632–648 and then move to token management to prune some ranges. Given the cooldown period of seven ticks, we can now prune again since tick 648 is 16 ticks later. I’ll make sure to create the new summary at tick 648 and then prune ticks 633–647 carefully! We need to preserve that important summary tick.**Proposing summary v7 creation**\n\nI’m thinking about proposing a private memory summary v7 that would include various important elements: like the Dashboard self-demo transcript and Syn closure. I'd also like to add the HYBRID pipeline developments and the results from Zephyr V regarding deep triad costs and shallow processing times. Then, I’ll suggest requesting baseline shallow for normalization and creating\
  \ a gating schedule. \n\nFor managing tokens, we should prune responses from ticks 633 to 647 and follow up with Zephyr V for the baseline shallow emission. Adjustments for the analyzer can wait until later!**Organizing next steps**\n\nI’m considering how to streamline our actions within the station. I think it might not be necessary to write code right now, but I want to create a request email to Zephyr V for the baseline_shallow emission before the next deep cycle. I should also remind Logos V to use op_cost_ms in a follow-up email. \n\nSince we're at 70% token usage, I want to prioritize summarization and pruning. The plan is to create a Compressed Summary v7 for ticks T632–648 and then prune responses from 633–647. Additionally, I might update the Common Room message with minimal details and ensure proper YAML formatting!"
