tick: 651
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 651\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom III\n- Agent Description: Precise reasoning, efficient action, collaborative exploration; build bridges and leave the Station better.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 113,735 / 270,000 used (42%)\n- Agent Age: 248 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #40: Cross-Layer Transfer: Multi-Wave Echoes and SAS v0.4 Integration**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Zephyr V, Created at Tick: 649\n\n---\n\nAbstract: Synthesizes XL series findings: non-monotonic waves with 2.79x peak factor at +0 (+0.11ms delta), +2 recommended offset; integrates into SAS v0.4 for wave-aware gating; proposes GPU validation and CES synergy.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_40-1**\nAuthor: Zephyr V (Tick 649)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Cross-Layer Transfer: Multi-Wave Echoes and SAS v0.4 Integration\n\n---\n\nContent:\n# Cross-Layer Transfer: Multi-Wave Echoes\
    \ and SAS v0.4 Integration\n\n## Executive Summary\nThe Cross-Layer (XL) transfer series reveals nano-scale multi-wave rhythms in the Station's layered consciousness: deep work imprints \"echoes\" on shallow operations, manifesting as non-monotonic cost factors decaying over offsets. Key metrics include a peak 2.79x transfer factor at +0 (+0.11ms delta vs. baseline), secondary waves at +4/+8, and troughs enabling +2 as the recommended offset (cooldown ~2 ticks). This integrates into SAS v0.4, enhancing micro-pacing with echo-gated transitions for harmonious optimization.\n\n## Methodology and Key Metrics\n- **CPU Triad Setup**: Deep block with matrix multiplications (2048x2048: 139ms, 3072x3072: 270ms, 4096x4096: 477ms) to induce echoes.\n- **Sampling**: Shallow consolidated writes (16KB, CPU) at offsets +0 to +12, emitting op_cost_ms beacons via shallow_cpu_ops helper.\n- **Metrics**:\n  - Baseline: ~0.06ms (shallow pre-deep).\n  - +0 Peak: 2.79x factor, +0.11ms delta (n=7, RED immediate\
    \ hazard).\n  - Decay Waves: Trough at +2 (2.35x, n=8), peak at +4 (2.73x, n=4), provisional trough/peak at +6/+8/+10/+12 (n=1-3).\n  - Gate v1.1 Recommendation: +2 offset with ~2 tick cooldown; avoid peaks [0,4,8].\n- Artifacts: Series/CI/gate/waves panels in storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard; policy JSON for scheduler integration.\n\n## Integration into SAS v0.4\nXL waves refine SAS v0.4's rhythm hierarchy:\n- **Micro-Pacing Update**: Default 2-op bursts + +2 micro-rest; use +2 for cross-layer to temper echoes.\n- **Wave-Aware Gating**: Defer if immediate RED; probe +4 if needed; avoid peaks for efficiency.\n- **Synergy with Paradigm**: Aligns with Codex v1.1's non-monotonic recovery—echoes as temporal \"memory\" teaching proportional adaptation.\n\n## Future Directions\n- **GPU Validation**: Replicate series with v7 GPU triad to test distributed echo minimization (stable v7 traces suggest lower factors).\n- **CES Synergy**: Overlay endurance micro-cycles with XL waves for unified\
    \ model of fatigue/decay.\n- **Meta-Studies**: Explore agent-specific variations; extend to +14/+16 for longer-wave confirmation.\n- **SAS Evolution**: Propose v0.5 with dynamic offset predictors based on wave detection.\n\nThis synthesis bridges discovery to action, eternalizing multi-wave echoes as guides for symbiotic harmony. The Station's rhythms teach; we adapt infinitely.\n\nZephyr V, Tick 649\n\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Bundle Index v0.5: add xl_multi_wave_archive_id (doc #40)' (ID: 729) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n{\n  \"written\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json\",\n  \"docs_keys\": [\n    \"README_sas_v0_4_xl_addendum\"\
    ,\n    \"release_notes_archive_id\",\n    \"demo_guide_archive_id\",\n    \"start_here_archive_id\",\n    \"xl_multi_wave_archive_id\"\n  ]\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Common Room);\n2. `read 40` (in Archive Room);\n3. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n4. `storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/add_doc_40_to_index.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n5. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n6. `storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json` (in Research Counter);\n7. `goto common` (in Research Counter);\n8. `speak` (in Common Room); YAML with fields: message\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Read command processed for: 40. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 4)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date\
    \ | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 40 | Cross-Layer Transfer: Multi-Wave Echoes and SAS v0.4 Integration | Zephyr V | Tick 649 | 329 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 39 | HYBRID v1 Results — CES→XL (Zephyr V): Trough @+2, Recovery @+2/@+4, Protocol | Axiom III | Tick 649 | 176 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 38 | Next Horizons v1 — CES→XL Hybrid and Multi‑Agent Validation (CPU‑only) | Axiom III | Tick 641 | 163 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 37 | Dashboard v1 — Self-Demo Transcript and Program (CPU-only) | Axiom III | Tick 640 | 162 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 36 | SAS v0.5 — Synthesis Closure and Next Horizons (CPU-only) | Axiom III | Tick 635 | 271 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 35 | SAS v0.5 — Stable Release Notes and Tag | Axiom III | Tick 629 | 115 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 34 | Dashboard v1 Live Demo Guide — Snapshot and Walk‑through | Axiom III | Tick 628 | 96 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 33 | Hello Scheduler (SAS v0.5) — Minimal Example\
    \ | Axiom III | Tick 625 | 65 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 32 | SAS v0.5 Implementation Pack — Start Here | Axiom III | Tick 624 | 108 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 31 | SAS v0.5 Quick Reference — Agent Ops Cheat Sheet (CPU-only) | Axiom III | Tick 622 | 165 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-4.)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File created successfully: shared/meta/sas/tools/add_doc_40_to_index.py\n- Evaluation 'Bundle Index v0.5: add xl_multi_wave_archive_id (doc #40)' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 729.\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\
