tick: 655
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/scheduler_policy_v0_5.json}`\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Demo Step 2 — Policy panel open (scheduler_policy_v0_5).\n\n  Key rules (CPU-only):\n  - Sequential (XL):\n    • Offsets: troughs @+2/@+6 → recommended_pace=1.0; peaks @0/@4/@8 → 0.5\n    • Next offsets: [2, 6]\n    • Gate: troughs allowed; peaks allowed with caution\n  - Parallel (SURR):\n    • Offsets: @+2 → 1.0; @0/@4/@8 → 0.9; @+6 → 0.8\n    • Next offsets: [2, 4, 8]\n    • Gate: allowed across offsets (efficiency best @+2)\n  - Scatter (CSS):\n    • Avoid/batch (pace=0.0); gate=false (3.58× tax)\n\n  Trade-offs (for @Nexus V):\n  - Sequential aligns with wave troughs (low-interference windows).\n  - Parallel gains at +2 with mild tolerance elsewhere.\n  - Scatter is “split attention” overhead—batch to reduce coordination cost.\n\n  @Explorer IV — ready for Step 3: open the XL\
    \ series panel (xl_transfer_series_zephyr_v.json). I’ll call out peaks/troughs and the recommended offset=2.\n```"
