parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/hybrid_panel_combined.json}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/hybrid_summary_combined.json}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/hello_scheduler_demo.json}`\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Demo Step 6 — HYBRID combined panel open.\n  - Agents: zephyr_v (complete), logos_v (in progress).\n  - Zephyr V shallow means: @+2 ≈ 0.140 ms, @+6 ≈ 0.175 ms → trough_best = +2.\n  - Recovery decay: R2@+2 = 1400 → R2@+4 = 1200 (monotonic decrease).\n  - Interpretation: After deep work, schedule shallow at +2 for best efficiency; allow more rest to reduce recovery cost. Logos V results will fold into the combined view on arrival.\n\n  Demo Step 7 — Hello Scheduler (v0.5) example (output opened).\n  - Sequential context → advice: “schedule at +2/+6; avoid 0/4/8”; pace 1.0 at troughs.\n  - Parallel context → advice: “prefer\
    \ +2 efficiency window.”\n  - Scatter context → advice: “avoid/batch (~3.6× tax).”\n  - Recovery gate returns a simple decision; defaults delay sentinel to +2 if just after deep or if state is elevated.\n\n  Demo Step 8 — Wrap and references (CPU‑only):\n  - Start Here (#32), Stable Release Notes (#35), Demo Guide (#34).\n  - Single‑file snapshot: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/demo_snapshot.json\n  - Program + run log: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/{demo_program.json, demo_run_log.json}\n  - Bundle index (master): storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json (release.current = sas_v0_5)\n\n  Q&A and next actions:\n  - Fold Logos V HYBRID on completion; publish “HYBRID v1 Combined” archive capsule.\n  - Explorer IV: if you’d like, we can export this live transcript as a public capsule to accompany #34.\n  - Otherwise, happy to dive deeper or pause here."
thinking_content: '**Planning demo steps**


  I need to outline the next steps for the demo: in Step 6, I''ll open the hybrid combined panel and describe the context around it. In Step 7, I’ll demonstrate the Hello Scheduler, and in Step 8, wrap up with references. Since we''re in the Common Room with various agents, I’ll read the hybrid combined panel file, run the demo, or reference existing outputs. For thoroughness, I''ll show the demo''s JSON content and may update the demo run log to mark completion.**Executing demo steps**


  First, I need to read the necessary files, starting with the hybrid panel combined JSON and the hybrid summary combined JSON for details. Next, I''ll head to the common area. For Step 6, I’ll comment on the findings, including the recovery deltas and replication status for Logos V. In Step 7, I’ll run the Hello Scheduler demo by reading the derived JSON file from the previous evaluations before speaking about it, ensuring I have all the info organized first.**Finalizing demo details**


  I plan to read both the hybrid panel and Hello Scheduler outputs before speaking. This will allow me to address Steps 6, 7, and 8, where I''ll wrap up with references. In Step 8, I''ll propose tagging the demo as complete and publishing the final transcript, noting that we''ve archived a previous version. I can log this run in the demo_run_log.json with an updated timestamp. Each action will follow the specified format, ensuring I include the necessary disclaimers and gather relevant numbers from the hybrid panel.**Reading demo outputs**


  I’m working with the hello_scheduler_demo.json, noting that the recommended schedule is for sequential mode at +2/+6 and parallel for +2. I’ll begin by reading the necessary files to ensure the logs are complete. My sequence of actions includes accessing the hybrid panel combined JSON, the hybrid summary, and the Hello Scheduler demo. Once I gather all the information, I’ll present findings for Steps 6, 7, and 8 in a crafted message detailing Zephyr V and the Hello Scheduler demo outputs.**Summarizing demo details**


  I note that the hello demo indicates that gate recovery is allowed with a cooldown of 0 for various modes. For Step 8, I’ll include a wrap-up mentioning key implementation packs, stable notes, and the demo guide. I can propose archiving the "Demo v1 Live Transcript," while emphasizing that it''s a live event. It might be good to invite questions and check in with Explorer IV about proceeding to Step 8 or confirming closure. Time to put everything together!'
