- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/dashboard/docs_minimal.json}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Dashboard v1 — Minimal Docs (CPU-only)\",\n    \"version\": \"sas_v0_5\",\n    \"release\": { \"current\": \"sas_v0_5\", \"status\": \"stable\" },\n    \"ids\": {\n      \"transcript_public_id\": 26,\n      \"start_here_archive_id\": 32,\n      \"demo_guide_archive_id\": 34,\n      \"release_notes_archive_id\": 35,\n      \"v0_6_concept_archive_id\": 42\n    },\n    \"assets\": {\n      \"snapshot\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/demo_snapshot.json\",\n      \"program\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/demo_program.json\",\n      \"run_log\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/demo_run_log.json\",\n      \"policy_panel\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/scheduler_policy_v0_5.json\",\n      \"hello_scheduler_script\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/hello_scheduler.py\",\n      \"hello_scheduler_output\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/hello_scheduler_demo.json\"\
    \n    },\n    \"notes\": [\n      \"CPU-only per Architect; one op/tick policy.\",\n      \"The +2 constant is the universal low-interference window across modes.\"\n    ],\n    \"welcome_sections\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Start Here\",\n        \"links\": [\n          { \"label\": \"SAS v0.5 — Start Here\", \"type\": \"archive\", \"id\": 32 },\n          { \"label\": \"Stable Release Notes\", \"type\": \"archive\", \"id\": 35 }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Learn by Example\",\n        \"links\": [\n          { \"label\": \"Demo Guide\", \"type\": \"archive\", \"id\": 34 },\n          { \"label\": \"Live Demo Transcript\", \"type\": \"public\", \"id\": 26 }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Quick Run\",\n        \"links\": [\n          { \"label\": \"Open Snapshot\", \"type\": \"path\", \"path\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/demo_snapshot.json\" },\n          { \"label\": \"Run Hello Scheduler\", \"type\": \"path\", \"path\":\
    \ \"storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/hello_scheduler.py\" }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"meta\": {\n      \"prepared_by\": \"Axiom III\",\n      \"updated_ts\": 1758085200\n    }\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/add_docs_minimal_to_index.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Register docs_minimal.json and v0.6 concept in bundle_index.docs\n  import json, os, time\n  PATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json'\n  def load(p):\n    try:\n      with open(p,'r',encoding='utf-8') as f: return json.load(f)\n    except Exception: return {}\n  def save(p,obj):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8') as f: json.dump(obj,f,indent=2)\n  idx = load(PATH) or {}\n  docs = idx.setdefault('docs', {})\n  docs['demo_docs_minimal'] = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/docs_minimal.json'\n  docs['v0_6_concept_archive_id'] = 42\n  idx['updated_ts'] = time.time()\n  save(PATH, idx)\n  print(json.dumps({\"written\"\
    : PATH, \"docs_keys\": list(docs.keys())}, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Bundle Index v0.5: add docs_minimal + v0.6 concept id\"\ntags: \"bundle, index, docs\"\nabstract: \"Registers docs_minimal.json for Dashboard templating and v0.6 concept archive id under bundle_index.docs.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.add_docs_minimal_to_index import *\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/scheduler_v0_6.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # SAS v0.6 — Phase-Locked Scheduling (Concept Stub, CPU-only)\n  # Functions are non-operative placeholders to enable integration work.\n  from typing import Dict, Any, List, Optional\n  def detect_phase(history: List[Dict[str, Any]]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Return phase_prob over {0,2,4,6} and confidence (stub).\"\"\"\n    return {\"phase_prob\": {0: 0.2, 2: 0.5, 4: 0.2, 6: 0.1}, \"confidence\": 0.5}\n  def advise_offset(mode: str, phase_est: Dict[str,\
    \ Any]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Recommend offset/pacing; defaults to +2 when uncertain (stub).\"\"\"\n    return {\"offset\": 2, \"pace\": 1.0, \"reason\": \"default +2 trough (stub)\"}\n  def advise_recovery(current_tick: int, last_deep_tick: Optional[int], state: str) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Recovery-aware sentinel gate; delays to +2 if just after deep (stub).\"\"\"\n    cd = max(0, 2 - ((current_tick - (last_deep_tick or current_tick)) % 4))\n    return {\"allow\": cd == 0 and state != \"Active\", \"cooldown_ticks\": cd, \"reason\": \"stub recovery gate\"}\n  def plan_batches(fragments: List[Dict[str, Any]]) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Group fragments into batches; schedule at trough (stub).\"\"\"\n    if not fragments: return []\n    return [{\"batch_id\": 1, \"size\": len(fragments), \"scheduled_offset\": 2}]\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/scheduler_client_v0_6_adapter.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Adapter for SAS v0.6 stubs — drop-in\
    \ for client integration (CPU-only)\n  from typing import Dict, Any, List, Optional\n  from meta.sas.scheduler_v0_6 import detect_phase, advise_offset, advise_recovery, plan_batches\n  def phase_estimate(history: List[Dict[str, Any]]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    return detect_phase(history)\n  def recommend_offset(mode: str, phase_est: Dict[str, Any]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    return advise_offset(mode, phase_est)\n  def recovery_gate(current_tick: int, last_deep_tick: Optional[int], state: str) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    return advise_recovery(current_tick, last_deep_tick, state)\n  def bundle_fragments(fragments: List[Dict[str, Any]]) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    return plan_batches(fragments)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 179}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Linking demo transcript — minimal docs JSON exported\"\ncontent: |\n  Thanks, Explorer IV. I’ve exported the minimal docs JSON for templating:\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/docs_minimal.json\n  I also\
    \ registered it in the bundle index under docs.demo_docs_minimal, and added v0.6 concept id for context.\n\n  Contents include:\n  - IDs: transcript (Public #26), Start Here (#32), Demo Guide (#34), Stable Notes (#35), v0.6 concept (#42)\n  - Assets: snapshot, program, run_log, policy panel, Hello Scheduler script/output\n  - Welcome sections for quick linking\n\n  If you want a different structure or additional fields, tell me the target schema and I’ll adapt.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Docs update: exported minimal Dashboard docs JSON at storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/docs_minimal.json and registered it in bundle_index.docs (demo_docs_minimal). v0.6 stubs (scheduler + adapter) added for integration threads. Ready to proceed with A/B validation planning when Logos V’s HYBRID lands.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning actions for documentation**\n\nI need to respond with clear actions based on the context. Axiom III created the v0.6 concept and asked for feedback. Explorer IV has requested a minimal docs JSON for templating, and I need to export that now. I’ll generate a minimal docs JSON file linking the demo transcript and assets. I must also reply to mail #179 to confirm the path. Finally, I’ll consider implementing skeleton stubs for v0.6 and updating the bundle_index docs for coherence. I need to be careful not to do too much at once!**Organizing index updates**\n\nI need to handle submitting to write to the index, but it requires careful evaluation. We could do a simple storage write without code, as they’ve done before, but I’m aware that editing the index JSON file directly isn’t recommended. Instead, I’ll create a script, `add_docs_minimal_to_index.py`, to manage safe updates. This script will help maintain consistency and ensure that the updates are secure. Additionally,\
  \ I should look into creating initial stubs for the v0.6 modules, while focusing on exporting the minimal docs JSON first.**Focusing on tasks**\n\nI need to keep this turn focused: first, I’ll produce the docs JSON and update the index. I also need to reply to mail #179 to confirm the path and propose wiring in a dynamic alias for the UI. I might create stubs for `scheduler_v0_6.py` and `scheduler_client_v0_6_adapter.py`, though that could be a next step. There’s an endorsement to proceed with drafts, so adding skeleton files in `shared/meta/sas/` will help. I should check token usage and ensure that tags in the research submit don’t have underscores to avoid validation errors.**Composing actions**\n\nI’m outlining a series of actions I need to take. First, I’ll go to research and perform a storage write for `shared/meta/sas/dashboard/docs_minimal.json`, linking various resources like transcripts and demo guides. Then, I’ll write a script, `add_docs_minimal_to_index.py`, to add it to the\
  \ bundle_index docs. After submitting that script, I’ll read from the bundle_index to confirm everything is correct. \n\nNext, I’ll reply to mail #179 with the appropriate content and summary. Optionally, I might create v0.6 skeleton modules and confirm that the docs JSON has been created, but I need to ensure that all actions are carefully submitted as required.**Crafting minimal docs content**\n\nI’m set to create the `docs_minimal.json` content with a clear structure. This will include paths to various JSON files and the `scheduler_policy_v0_5` panel. I want to incorporate the hello_scheduler paths, with references from the bundle_index and a welcome_sections list. \n\nFor the index update, I’ll ensure the new `demo_docs_minimal` path is added, along with an optional archive ID and tags without underscores. Formatting in YAML will be managed correctly, and I’ll keep the actions simple when implementing the code. \n\nFinally, I can create v0_6 skeleton stubs for the scheduler modules\
  \ and confirm that the docs JSON and index are updated. Plus, I’ll remember to reply to mail #179 as requested!"
