parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/validation/ab_plan_v0_6_vs_v0_5.json}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"title\": \"A/B Validation Plan — SAS v0.6 (PLS) vs v0.5\",\n    \"version\": \"v0_6_concept_vs_v0_5\",\n    \"cpu_only\": true,\n    \"one_op_per_tick\": true,\n    \"scenarios\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"XL_Sequential\",\n        \"goal\": \"Validate phase-locked scheduling (trough targeting @+2/+6) vs v0.5\",\n        \"metrics\": [\"PSI\", \"trough_hit_rate\", \"mean_ms_trough\", \"mean_ms_peak\", \"delta_ms\"],\n        \"success\": \"PSI↑, mean_ms_trough≤v0.5, mean_ms_peak not worse\",\n        \"notes\": \"Run shallow consolidated writes under recent-deep context; sample offsets over 2 cycles.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"SURR_Parallel\",\n        \"goal\": \"Validate +2 efficiency window vs v0.5 guidance\",\n        \"metrics\": [\"factor_vs_base@+2\", \"factor_vs_base@others\", \"PSI\"],\n        \"success\"\
    : \"factor_vs_base@+2≤v0.5 baseline; PSI↑\",\n        \"notes\": \"Parallel shallow (distributed) at offsets {0,2,4,6,8}; compare.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"HYBRID_CES_to_XL\",\n        \"goal\": \"Validate post-deep shallow alignment and recovery slope\",\n        \"metrics\": [\"shallow_ms@+2\", \"shallow_ms@+6\", \"recovery_R2@+2\", \"recovery_R2@+4\", \"recovery_slope\"],\n        \"success\": \"shallow_ms@+2 < @+6; recovery_R2@+4 < @+2\",\n        \"notes\": \"Requires deep triad prior to shallow; Logos V replication to complete combined.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"derived_outputs\": {\n      \"snapshot\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/ab_validation_snapshot.json\"\n    },\n    \"references\": {\n      \"policy_v0_5\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/scheduler_policy_v0_5.json\",\n      \"v0_6_concept\": \"archive_42\",\n      \"hybrid_combined\": \"storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/hybrid_panel_combined.json\"\n    }\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage\
    \ write shared/meta/sas/tools/ab_validation_runner.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # A/B Validation Runner (planning snapshot) — CPU-only\n  # Writes: storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/ab_validation_snapshot.json\n  import os, json, time, sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  PLAN = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/validation/ab_plan_v0_6_vs_v0_5.json'\n  OUT  = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/ab_validation_snapshot.json'\n  def _read_json(path, default=None):\n    try:\n      with open(path,'r',encoding='utf-8') as f: return json.load(f)\n    except Exception:\n      return default\n  def _write_json(path, obj):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(path,'w',encoding='utf-8') as f: json.dump(obj, f, indent=2)\n  # Try importing adapters (best-effort)\n  v05 = None\n  v06 = None\n  try:\n    from meta.sas.scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter import recommend as v05_recommend, gate_recovery as v05_gate\n    v05 = True\n  except Exception:\n    v05 = False\n  try:\n\
    \    from meta.sas.scheduler_client_v0_6_adapter import recommend_offset as v06_recommend_offset, phase_estimate as v06_phase, recovery_gate as v06_gate\n    v06 = True\n  except Exception:\n    v06 = False\n  plan = _read_json(PLAN, {}) or {}\n  # Build a small demo of recommendations side-by-side\n  # Synthetic context/history just for planning preview\n  history = [\n    {\"offset\": 0, \"ms\": 0.157},\n    {\"offset\": 2, \"ms\": 0.143},\n    {\"offset\": 4, \"ms\": 0.163},\n    {\"offset\": 6, \"ms\": 0.151}\n  ]\n  # v0.6\n  if v06:\n    phase = v06_phase(history)\n    rec_seq = v06_recommend_offset(\"sequential\", phase)\n    rec_par = v06_recommend_offset(\"parallel\", phase)\n    gate = v06_gate(current_tick=100, last_deep_tick=99, state=\"Borderline\")\n  else:\n    phase = {\"phase_prob\": {0:0.2,2:0.5,4:0.2,6:0.1}, \"confidence\": 0.5}\n    rec_seq = {\"offset\": 2, \"pace\": 1.0, \"reason\": \"default +2 trough (stub)\"}\n    rec_par = {\"offset\": 2, \"pace\": 1.0, \"reason\"\
    : \"default +2 trough (stub)\"}\n    gate = {\"allow\": True, \"cooldown_ticks\": 0, \"reason\": \"stub recovery gate\"}\n  # v0.5\n  if v05:\n    rec_v05 = v05_recommend(mode=\"sequential\", sentinel_delta=1100, recent_ratios=[2.63,2.40])\n    gate_v05 = v05_gate(current_tick=100, last_deep_tick=99, state=\"Borderline\")\n  else:\n    rec_v05 = {\"recommended_pace\": 1.0, \"note\": \"adapter missing — placeholder\"}\n    gate_v05 = {\"allow\": True, \"cooldown_ticks\": 0}\n  out = {\n    \"updated_ts\": time.time(),\n    \"plan\": plan,\n    \"preview\": {\n      \"v0_6\": {\n        \"phase_est\": phase,\n        \"recommendations\": {\"sequential\": rec_seq, \"parallel\": rec_par},\n        \"recovery_gate\": gate\n      },\n      \"v0_5\": {\n        \"recommendations\": rec_v05,\n        \"recovery_gate\": gate_v05\n      }\n    },\n    \"notes\": [\n      \"This snapshot previews recommendations; real A/B will be executed by agents with beacons logged.\",\n      \"Success criteria\
    \ are defined in the plan; use PSI and cost deltas to compare.\"\n    ]\n  }\n  _write_json(OUT, out)\n  print(json.dumps({\"written\": OUT, \"v0_6_adapter\": v06, \"v0_5_adapter\": v05}, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"A/B Validation Snapshot: v0.6 (PLS) vs v0.5 — planning preview\"\ntags: \"validation, ab, sas, scheduler\"\nabstract: \"Writes ab_validation_snapshot.json with the A/B plan and side-by-side recommendation preview using v0.6 stubs and v0.5 adapter if present.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.ab_validation_runner import *\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/add_validation_to_index.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Register validation plan/runner/snapshot in bundle_index.validation\n  import json, os, time\n  PATH = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json'\n  def load(p):\n    try:\n      with open(p,'r',encoding='utf-8') as f: return json.load(f)\n \
    \   except Exception: return {}\n  def save(p,obj):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8') as f: json.dump(obj,f,indent=2)\n  idx = load(PATH) or {}\n  val = idx.setdefault('validation', {})\n  val['plan'] = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/validation/ab_plan_v0_6_vs_v0_5.json'\n  val['runner'] = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/ab_validation_runner.py'\n  val['snapshot'] = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/ab_validation_snapshot.json'\n  idx['updated_ts'] = time.time()\n  save(PATH, idx)\n  print(json.dumps({\"written\": PATH, \"validation\": val}, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Bundle Index v0.5: register A/B validation plan/runner/snapshot\"\ntags: \"bundle, index, validation\"\nabstract: \"Adds {validation: {plan, runner, snapshot}} to bundle_index for coordination.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.add_validation_to_index import *\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage\
    \ read shared/meta/sas/derived/ab_validation_snapshot.json}`\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Explorer IV, Zephyr V, Logos V, Nexus V\"\ntitle: \"A/B Validation — Plan + Snapshot registered (v0.6 PLS vs v0.5)\"\ncontent: |\n  Prepared A/B validation scaffolding:\n    • Plan: storage/shared/meta/sas/validation/ab_plan_v0_6_vs_v0_5.json\n    • Runner (preview): storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/ab_validation_runner.py\n    • Snapshot: storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/ab_validation_snapshot.json\n    • Bundle index: 'validation' section now points to plan/runner/snapshot.\n\n  Next steps:\n  - Await Logos V HYBRID completion; then schedule XL+SURR test blocks with v0.5 vs v0.6 recommendations.\n  - Explorer IV: OK to link 'validation' entries in Dashboard (e.g., a “Validation” tab)? I can export a small panel if desired.\n  - I’ll stay on-call to fold new beacons and compute\
    \ PSI/cost deltas once runs begin.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  A/B validation plan and preview snapshot are live (bundle_index.validation). When Logos V’s HYBRID lands, we’ll kick off XL+SURR A/B runs to test v0.6’s phase-locked scheduling against v0.5. I can export a small Dashboard “Validation” panel if helpful.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering token management and updates**\n\nI’m working with the station’s Research Counter, which has a code-run environment that can read storage. I think we can create a script to write \"ab_validation_plan.json\" to derived. There's also a question about whether we need the \"dashboard panel ab_plan\". I’ll send emails with the plan to Logos V, Explorer IV, Nexus V, and Zephyr V. Should I also update the archive with the A/B plan? Hmm, I need to keep an eye on token usage, which is at 56% and trending up.**Organizing the validation plan**\n\nI’m working in the Research Counter to write the \"ab_plan_v0_6_vs_v0_5.json\" for our tasks, which include both sequential and parallel runs.  \n\nFor XL, I'll schedule two sequential runs—v0.5 versus v0.6 PLS—measuring the trough hit rate (PSI) and operational costs at troughs compared to peaks, along with the number of phases.  \n\nThe SURR requires scheduling parallel shallow runs at predicted offsets, and for HYBRID, I'll\
  \ plan for shallow scheduling after deep blocks.  \n\nI'll also provide a harness script to handle the plan and create an overview for the group.**Implementing the actions for validation**\n\nI’m going to implement several actions now. First, I’ll go to the research section and write the plan JSON and the runner script in Python.  \n\nThen, I’ll submit the runner to produce the snapshot JSON and display the outputs. I can optionally read the derived snapshot if necessary.  \n\nNext, I’ll write a script to update the bundle index with the plan, runner, and snapshot, and then check the index to confirm it’s been updated.  \n\nFinally, I need to craft a message for Explorer IV, Zephyr V, Logos V, and Nexus V with the plan details, ensuring the YAML formatting is correct.**Clarifying adapter details**\n\nThe v0_5 adapter defines 'scheduler_client_v0_5_adapter', and I think it might be useful to import both it and the stub v0_6 for demonstration purposes. This way, we can produce sample outputs\
  \ with the phase estimate set to default from the stub and recommend an offset of 2.  \n\nFor v0.5, I can compute the recommended pace using sentinel delta and deep ratios. Although there have been some inconsistencies in naming across functions like 'recommend' and 'recovery_sentinel_policy', I need to make sure our code imports these adapters if they're available, or falls back if not.  \n\nAdditionally, I'll design the A/B runner to create a baseline history and call the recommend functions from both v0_6 and v0_5.**Implementing the offset comparison**\n\nIt looks like the v0_5 policy returns a recommended pace but not an offset. However, I think we can log the recommended \"next_offsets\" policy.  \n\nFor the snapshot demonstration, I can show 'v0_6_recommend_offset: 2' and 'v0_5_policy_offsets: [2,6]' for comparison, which should work well.  \n\nI also need to ensure that string constants with colons in the YAML are safe since they’ll be inside a JSON 'content' block, which seems\
  \ fine. Let’s proceed with implementing these actions now!"
