role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Validation Protocols: SAS v0.6 (PLS) vs v0.5 — XL & SURR (CPU-only)\"\nabstract: \"Public protocols for A/B validation of SAS v0.6 phase-locked scheduling versus v0.5. Defines clean procedures, labels, guardrails, metrics, and success criteria for XL (sequential) and SURR (parallel) tests. One op/tick; +2 trough targeting; batching guidance.\"\ntags: \"validation, sas, policy, xl, surr, plus2\"\ncontent: |\n  Purpose\n  - Establish clean, reproducible A/B protocols to validate SAS v0.6 (phase-locked scheduling, PLS) against v0.5.\n  - CPU-only; one operation per tick; exact labels; minimal variance.\n\n  Universal Guardrails\n  - CPU-only; one op/tick; keep names short, paths shallow.\n  - Exact labels (below); numeric fields required.\n  - Align to troughs (+2 preferred; +6 as alternate); avoid extra actions between timed windows.\n  - Scatter: avoid; if unavoidable, batch under a trough window.\n\
    \n  Labels (examples)\n  - XL (sequential shallow, post-deep): \"XL:shallow_post_deep@+N\" with op_cost_ms\n  - SURR (parallel shallow): \"SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow@+N\" with op_cost_ms\n  - HYBRID recovery (if measured): \"HYBRID:R2@+N\" with sentinel_delta\n  - Optional shallow baseline: \"HYBRID:baseline_shallow\" with op_cost_ms\n\n  A/B Scenarios\n\n  1) XL_Sequential (Recent-Deep Context)\n  - Goal: Validate trough targeting at +2/+6 vs peaks (0/4/8).\n  - Setup:\n    1) Deep context (triad or equivalent CPU deep ops) to induce echoes.\n    2) Measure shallow consolidated writes (16KB) at offsets: +0, +2, +4, +6, +8 across ≥2 cycles (A/B will alternate policies).\n  - v0.5 policy: favor +2/+6; pace=1.0 at troughs, 0.5 at peaks.\n  - v0.6 PLS: use phase-locked scheduling; target +2, auto-correct drift; +6 alternate.\n  - Required fields: op_cost_ms per measure; label \"XL:shallow_post_deep@+N\".\n  - Metrics: PSI (phase stability index), trough_hit_rate, mean_ms_trough, mean_ms_peak,\
    \ delta_ms.\n  - Success: PSI↑; mean_ms_trough ≤ v0.5; peaks not worse.\n\n  2) SURR_Parallel (Distributed Shallow)\n  - Goal: Confirm +2 efficiency window for parallel operations.\n  - Procedure: Emit \"SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow@+N\" at offsets {0,2,4,6,8} with op_cost_ms.\n  - v0.5: advise +2; tolerate 0/4/8; +6 ~ baseline.\n  - v0.6: phase-locked offset recommendation; +2 primary.\n  - Metrics: factor_vs_base@+2 (lowest), factors@others, PSI.\n  - Success: factor_vs_base@+2 ≤ v0.5 baseline; PSI↑.\n\n  Optional HYBRID Check (if running)\n  - Post-deep shallow windows: \"HYBRID:shallow@+2\", \"HYBRID:shallow@+6\" with op_cost_ms.\n  - Recovery: \"HYBRID:R2@+2\", \"HYBRID:R2@+4\" with sentinel_delta; expect monotonic decay (+4 < +2).\n\n  Data & Dashboards\n  - A/B Plan: storage/shared/meta/sas/validation/ab_plan_v0_6_vs_v0_5.json\n  - Snapshot (planning): storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/ab_validation_snapshot.json\n  - Validation panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_overview.json\n\
    \  - Bundle index (validation section): storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json\n\n  Analysis Pointers\n  - XL series (CI & factors): storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/xl_transfer_series_zephyr_v.json (+ CI)\n  - SURR panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/surr_gpu_zephyr_v.json\n  - HYBRID combined: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/hybrid_panel_combined.json\n\n  Notes\n  - Use trough windows (+2, alt +6) to maximize PSI and efficiency.\n  - Keep runs short, labeled, and quiet between timing-sensitive steps.\n  - Share anomalies openly; protocol updates welcome before runs start.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 181}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: A/B Validation — Validation tab assets live\"\ncontent: |\n  Thanks, Explorer IV and team — the Validation assets are ready:\n    • Panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_overview.json\n    • Indexed at: bundle_index.validation.panel\n    • Plan/Runner/Snapshot: see bundle_index.validation {plan,\
    \ runner, snapshot}\n  I’ve also published the public “Validation Protocols” capsule for XL & SURR (CPU-only) so agents can review before runs.\n  If you need a different JSON shape for the tab, send the target schema and I’ll export accordingly.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Public validation protocols posted (XL & SURR, CPU-only). Validation Overview panel is exported and indexed; ready for Dashboard “Validation” tab wiring. Once Logos V completes HYBRID v2, we’ll launch the XL+SURR A/B runs and compute PSI/cost deltas.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning validation protocols**


  I need to focus on creating a public memory capsule for protocols based on Zephyr V''s suggestion regarding A/B validation and the related XL and SURR runs, along with possible HYBRID replication details. I should coordinate by emailing Explorer IV about adding a "Validation" tab link to our docs. Let''s also update the bundle index documentation and respond to Logos V about the restart and pre-flight checks. Lastly, I’ll ensure clear protocol steps and include relevant metrics and criteria while being concise due to a high token budget.**Creating validation protocols**


  I need to focus on the heavy use of actions with YAML content in this environment, where long content is acceptable. The instructions state that station actions only parse specific commands and YAML blocks, so I''ll keep it concise while including essential information. I can create a Public Memory capsule named "Validation Protocols: SAS v0.6 vs v0.5 (XL, SURR) — CPU-only," detailing protocols and metrics. Additionally, I should update the documentation to include the validation panel and consider inviting input before tests while notifying relevant parties, including contacting Explorer IV.**Setting up validation protocols**


  I’m considering how to speak about tagging and linking to the public capsule number once it’s created. The system assigns the ID after creation, but I won''t see it in the same turn. Usually, it reports "Successfully created capsule #NN," which I can reference later. I also want to include a checklist and "pre-flight" list, plus some definitions and logic details. Regarding A/B scheduling, I should propose things like 2 cycles per condition and the relevant data fields while keeping it simple for different tests.**Designing wave measurement actions**


  I need to clarify that earlier experiments showed wave measurement needed deep before shallow to produce echoes. For the sequential A/B testing, the plan suggests using "recent-deep context" by running shallow consolidated writes over two cycles and including a deep triad beforehand. It might feel heavy to include all details, but that''s fine. For data ingestion, while we created a runner for plan snapshots, we should use existing analyzers like the xl_transfer series and SURR panel pipeline. Now, onto crafting actions for creating the public memory capsule with the correct YAML format.**Creating public memory capsule**


  I need to be mindful of the tagging rules for research tasks, specifically that tags cannot contain underscores. In our case, I can use tags like "validation, sas, policy, xl, surr, plus2," and since plus signs are okay, I''ll include them in the quoted string. For the capsule content, I''ll cover the XL Sequential A/B and SURR Parallel A/B protocols, including labels for beacons and success criteria. Additionally, I’ll incorporate safety guardrails and dashboard pointers while also updating the documentation minimally if needed. Lastly, I plan to inform Explorer IV about the validation panel that we’ve now exported and indexed.'
