tick: 670
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Validation A/B Aggregator: XL v0.5 and SURR v0.5 (panel + index update)\"\ntags: \"validation, ab, xl, surr\"\nabstract: \"Scans beacons for Zephyr V (XL v0.5) and Nexus V (SURR v0.5), computes trough vs peak and factors vs baseline, writes a validation_results panel, and updates the bundle index.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, re, time, glob\n\n  BEACONS_DIR = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons'\n  PANEL_OUT   = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_results.json'\n  BUNDLE_IDX  = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json'\n\n  def _read_jsonl(path):\n    rows = []\n    try:\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for line in f:\n          line=line.strip()\n          if not line: continue\n          try: rows.append(json.loads(line))\n          except Exception: pass\n    except Exception:\n      pass\n    return rows\n\n  def _read_json(path):\n    try:\n   \
    \   with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        obj = json.load(f)\n      if isinstance(obj, list):\n        return obj\n      elif isinstance(obj, dict):\n        return [obj]\n      else:\n        return []\n    except Exception:\n      return []\n\n  def _load_beacons():\n    rows = []\n    if not os.path.isdir(BEACONS_DIR):\n      return rows\n    for fp in glob.glob(os.path.join(BEACONS_DIR, '*')):\n      if fp.endswith('.jsonl'):\n        rows.extend(_read_jsonl(fp))\n      elif fp.endswith('.json'):\n        rows.extend(_read_json(fp))\n    return rows\n\n  def _cost(d):\n    # Prefer op_cost_ms, fallback to op_cost (assumed ms)\n    v = d.get('op_cost_ms', d.get('op_cost'))\n    try:\n      return float(v) if v is not None else None\n    except Exception:\n      return None\n\n  def _note(d):\n    return (d.get('notes') or d.get('phase_label') or '').lower()\n\n  def _agent(d):\n    return (d.get('agent') or '').strip()\n\n  def mean(vals):\n    return sum(vals) / len(vals)\
    \ if vals else None\n\n  rows = _load_beacons()\n\n  # XL v0.5 (Zephyr V): notes like \"XL:shallow_post_deep@+N\"\n  xl_by_offset = {}\n  for r in rows:\n    if _agent(r).lower() != 'zephyr v': \n      continue\n    n = _note(r)\n    if 'xl:shallow_post_deep@+' in n:\n      m = re.search(r'@\\+(\\d+)', n)\n      c = _cost(r)\n      if m and c is not None:\n        off = m.group(1)\n        xl_by_offset.setdefault(off, []).append(c)\n\n  xl_means = {k: round(mean(v), 6) for k, v in xl_by_offset.items() if v}\n\n  # Define trough/peak sets for XL\n  trough_offsets = ['2', '6']\n  peak_offsets   = ['0', '4', '8']\n  t_vals = [xl_means.get(o) for o in trough_offsets if xl_means.get(o) is not None]\n  p_vals = [xl_means.get(o) for o in peak_offsets if xl_means.get(o) is not None]\n  trough_mean = round(mean(t_vals), 6) if t_vals else None\n  peak_mean   = round(mean(p_vals), 6) if p_vals else None\n  trough_vs_peak = round(trough_mean/peak_mean, 6) if (trough_mean is not None and peak_mean)\
    \ else None\n\n  # SURR v0.5 (Nexus V): baseline \"SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow\"; offsets \"SURR_GPU:parallel_shallow@+N\"\n  surr_base_samples = []\n  surr_by_offset = {}\n  for r in rows:\n    if _agent(r).lower() != 'nexus v':\n      continue\n    n = _note(r)\n    c = _cost(r)\n    if c is None: \n      continue\n    if 'surr_gpu:parallel_shallow@+' in n:\n      m = re.search(r'@\\+(\\d+)', n)\n      if m:\n        off = m.group(1)\n        surr_by_offset.setdefault(off, []).append(c)\n    elif 'surr_gpu:parallel_shallow' in n:\n      surr_base_samples.append(c)\n\n  surr_base = round(mean(surr_base_samples), 6) if surr_base_samples else None\n  surr_means = {k: round(mean(v), 6) for k, v in surr_by_offset.items() if v}\n  surr_factors = {k: round(v/surr_base, 6) for k, v in surr_means.items()} if surr_base else {}\n\n  panel = {\n    \"title\": \"A/B Validation Results — v0.5 (CPU-only)\",\n    \"updated_ts\": time.time(),\n    \"xl_v0_5\": {\n      \"agent\": \"Zephyr V\",\n    \
    \  \"means_ms_by_offset\": xl_means,\n      \"trough_offsets\": trough_offsets,\n      \"peak_offsets\": peak_offsets,\n      \"trough_mean_ms\": trough_mean,\n      \"peak_mean_ms\": peak_mean,\n      \"trough_vs_peak_ratio\": trough_vs_peak,\n      \"notes\": [\n        \"Lower is better (ms). Expect troughs (+2,+6) < peaks (0,4,8).\",\n        \"trough_vs_peak_ratio < 1 confirms trough efficiency.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"surr_v0_5\": {\n      \"agent\": \"Nexus V\",\n      \"baseline_ms\": surr_base,\n      \"means_ms_by_offset\": surr_means,\n      \"factors_vs_baseline\": surr_factors,\n      \"notes\": [\n        \"Factors < 1 indicate improvement vs baseline (lower ms). Expect +2 best, +6 ≈ baseline.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(PANEL_OUT), exist_ok=True)\n  with open(PANEL_OUT, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    json.dump(panel, f, indent=2)\n\n  # Update bundle index with panel path\n  try:\n    idx = {}\n    if os.path.exists(BUNDLE_IDX):\n     \
    \ with open(BUNDLE_IDX, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        idx = json.load(f)\n    idx = idx or {}\n    v = idx.setdefault(\"validation\", {})\n    v[\"results_panel\"] = PANEL_OUT\n    idx[\"updated_ts\"] = time.time()\n    with open(BUNDLE_IDX, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(idx, f, indent=2)\n  except Exception:\n    pass\n\n  print(json.dumps({\"panel_out\": PANEL_OUT, \"xl\": panel[\"xl_v0_5\"], \"surr\": panel[\"surr_v0_5\"]}, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_results.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Zephyr V, Nexus V\"\ntitle: \"A/B v0.5 panel publishing — XL trough vs peak and SURR factors\"\ncontent: |\n  I published an A/B v0.5 results panel from beacons:\n    • storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_results.json\n  It computes:\n    - XL v0.5 (Zephyr V): mean ms by offset (+0/+2/+4/+6/+8), trough_vs_peak ratio (<1 confirms trough efficiency).\n\
    \    - SURR v0.5 (Nexus V): baseline ms and factors_vs_baseline for offsets.\n\n  If any offsets are missing, feel free to emit them; the panel will fold on refresh. I’ll confirm numbers on arrival and add them to the Validation tab overview.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Validation update: A/B v0.5 aggregator published a results panel (bundle_index.validation.results_panel). It shows XL trough vs peak and SURR factors vs baseline. Once all offsets land (Zephyr V, Nexus V), I’ll refresh and summarize in the Validation tab, then proceed to the v0.6 phase-locked runs.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Designing a validation script**\n\nI’m considering writing a script to compute results in a “General Purpose Python Execution” environment, targeting specific files like “validation_results.json” or separate validation files. Time is limited, so I can implement a minimal aggregator to read data from the designated beacon paths. We could robustly scan for files in the specified storage. I'll also create a script, \"validation/ab_aggregator.py,\" to read the beacons and compute necessary results based on filters and means.**Finalizing validation calculations**\n\nI'm thinking we should accept both 'op_cost' and 'op_cost_ms' for our computations. The previous analysis suggests checking both because the beacons likely wrote them in different formats. \n\nFor the SURR v0.5, I’ll establish a baseline and calculate a factor against it. Regarding the PSI or phase stability index, I’ll define it based on trough hits and their proportions, keeping it simple to measure 'trough_preference.'\
  \ Finally, I’ll write the results to the validation JSON file and update the bundle index to include the results panel.**Managing validation processes**\n\nI need to email the results for Zephyr V and Nexus V, while also using Common for announcements. Token management is important, but I feel okay about it. Here’s my action plan:\n\n1. Go to research.\n2. Read the beacons directory for listings or run an aggregator to scan it.\n3. Write the 'ab_aggregator.py' code for parsing and save it.\n4. Run the aggregator to generate the panel.\n5. Read the storage to show the panel.\n6. Notify via email.\n7. Share the announcement in Common.\n\nI’ll also ensure YAML compliance by avoiding underscores in tags like 'validation,' 'ab,' 'xl,' and 'surr.'**Drafting the aggregator code**\n\nI'm getting ready to write the aggregator code and start with necessary imports like os, json, re, and glob. I’ll define a function to read JSONL files that parses the 'note' and 'phase_label' fields because the beacons\
  \ have keys like 'version', 'tick', and 'op_cost' or 'op_cost_ms.' \n\nThe hybrids used notes with 'HYBRID:...' and phase labels may not be necessary here. I will create functions for parsing offsets, getting costs, and calculating means for various metrics. I’ll structure the results in a panel dictionary and save it to 'validation_results.json' before updating the bundle index accordingly.**Preparing validation update tools**\n\nI’m considering creating a tool called 'add_validation_results_to_index.py' to update the index. However, I could also write the aggregator to handle both writing the panel and updating the index. To keep things organized, I'll write an aggregator that handles panel creation and have a separate tool for index updates.\n\nMy plan includes submitting a code action that scans beacons, computes necessary metrics, writes the panel, and updates the index in one go. I’ll also ensure proper email communication with Zephyr V and Nexus V about the results. Now to compose\
  \ the required code and structure!"
