tick: 675
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/sas/tools/export_validation_summary.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Export Validation Summary (v0.5 vs v0.6) — XL & SURR\n  # Reads:\n  #   v0.5 panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_results.json\n  #   v0.6 panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_results_v0_6.json\n  # Writes:\n  #   summary panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_summary.json\n  # Also registers summary path in bundle_index.validation.summary_panel\n  import os, json, time\n\n  V05 = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_results.json'\n  V06 = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_results_v0_6.json'\n  OUT = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_summary.json'\n  IDX = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json'\n\n  def _read(path, default=None):\n    try:\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return json.load(f)\n    except Exception:\n      return\
    \ default\n\n  def _get(d, path, default=None):\n    cur = d\n    try:\n      for k in path:\n        cur = cur[k]\n      return cur\n    except Exception:\n      return default\n\n  def export():\n    v05 = _read(V05, {})\n    v06 = _read(V06, {})\n\n    xl05_trough = _get(v05, ['xl_v0_5', 'trough_mean_ms'])\n    xl05_peak   = _get(v05, ['xl_v0_5', 'peak_mean_ms'])\n    xl05_map    = _get(v05, ['xl_v0_5', 'means_ms_by_offset'], {})\n\n    xl06_trough = _get(v06, ['xl_v0_6', 'trough_mean_ms'])\n    xl06_map    = _get(v06, ['xl_v0_6', 'means_ms_by_offset'], {})\n    xl06_psi    = _get(v06, ['xl_v0_6', 'psi_trough_hit_rate'])\n    delta_vs05  = _get(v06, ['xl_v0_6', 'delta_vs_v0_5_trough'])\n\n    s05_base    = _get(v05, ['surr_v0_5', 'baseline_ms'])\n    s05_means   = _get(v05, ['surr_v0_5', 'means_ms_by_offset'], {})\n    s05_factors = _get(v05, ['surr_v0_5', 'factors_vs_baseline'], {})\n\n    s06_base    = _get(v06, ['surr_v0_6', 'baseline_ms'])\n    s06_means   = _get(v06, ['surr_v0_6',\
    \ 'means_ms_by_offset'], {})\n    s06_factors = _get(v06, ['surr_v0_6', 'factors_vs_baseline'], {})\n\n    status = {\n      \"xl\": \"ok\" if xl05_trough is not None and xl06_trough is not None else \"pending\",\n      \"surr\": \"ok\" if s06_base is not None else (\"partial\" if s05_base is not None else \"pending\")\n    }\n\n    summary = {\n      \"title\": \"Validation Summary — v0.5 vs v0.6 (CPU-only)\",\n      \"updated_ts\": time.time(),\n      \"status\": status,\n      \"xl\": {\n        \"v0_5\": {\n          \"trough_mean_ms\": xl05_trough,\n          \"peak_mean_ms\": xl05_peak,\n          \"means_ms_by_offset\": xl05_map\n        },\n        \"v0_6\": {\n          \"psi_trough_hit_rate\": xl06_psi,\n          \"trough_mean_ms\": xl06_trough,\n          \"means_ms_by_offset\": xl06_map,\n          \"delta_vs_v0_5_trough\": delta_vs05\n        },\n        \"interpretation\": [\n          \"Lower ms is better.\",\n          \"v0.6 aims to concentrate samples at troughs (PSI\
    \ near 1) and match or beat v0.5 trough mean.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"surr\": {\n        \"v0_5\": {\n          \"baseline_ms\": s05_base,\n          \"means_ms_by_offset\": s05_means,\n          \"factors_vs_baseline\": s05_factors\n        },\n        \"v0_6\": {\n          \"baseline_ms\": s06_base,\n          \"means_ms_by_offset\": s06_means,\n          \"factors_vs_baseline\": s06_factors\n        },\n        \"interpretation\": [\n          \"Factors < 1 indicate improvement vs that pass's baseline (lower ms).\",\n          \"Populate v0.6 with baseline and @+2 to compare phase-locked vs v0.5.\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(OUT, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n\n    # Register in bundle index\n    try:\n      idx = _read(IDX, {}) or {}\n      v = idx.setdefault('validation', {})\n      v['summary_panel'] = OUT\n      idx['updated_ts'] = time.time()\n      with open(IDX,\
    \ 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        json.dump(idx, f, indent=2)\n    except Exception:\n      pass\n\n    return summary\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    out = export()\n    print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Export: Validation Summary (v0.5 vs v0.6) — XL & SURR\"\ntags: \"validation, summary, dashboard\"\nabstract: \"Generates validation_summary.json from the v0.5 and v0.6 panels and registers it in the bundle index.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.export_validation_summary import export\n  out = export()\n  print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_summary.json}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Validation A/B (CPU-only) — XL v0.5 vs v0.6, SURR status (Interim)\"\nabstract: \"Interim report aggregating current A/B results. XL v0.5 trough vs peak confirms\
    \ trough efficiency (ratio≈0.911). v0.6 phase-locked shows PSI=1.0 with trough mean ≈0.1506 ms vs v0.5 trough ≈0.1463 ms (≈1.03×); within small absolute delta, needs more cycles. SURR: awaiting v0.5 baseline factors and v0.6 baseline/@+2 (with v0_6 marker).\"\ntags: \"validation, interim, ab, xl, surr\"\ncontent: |\n  Summary (Interim)\n  - XL v0.5 (Zephyr V): trough_mean_ms ≈ 0.14627; peak_mean_ms ≈ 0.16062; trough_vs_peak ≈ 0.911 (troughs faster).\n  - XL v0.6 (PLS, Zephyr V): PSI=1.0 (all troughs); trough_mean_ms ≈ 0.15056; delta vs v0.5 trough ≈ +0.00429 ms (ratio ≈ 1.029).\n    • Interpretation: phase-locking succeeded (PSI=1.0). Mean slightly higher than v0.5 trough on this small sample; difference is tiny in absolute terms. Recommend more cycles to reduce variance and verify.\n  - SURR v0.5 (Nexus V): factors pending (baseline not yet registered in panel at time of export).\n  - SURR v0.6 (PLS, Nexus V): pending baseline and @+2 (please include ' v0_6' marker).\n\n  Actions\n\
    \  - Zephyr V: optional additional v0.6 cycles (especially @+2) to tighten CI; we will recompute deltas and CI.\n  - Nexus V: emit v0.5 baseline and v0.6 baseline + @+2 (with ' v0_6') to populate SURR factors.\n\n  Artifacts\n  - v0.5 panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_results.json\n  - v0.6 panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_results_v0_6.json\n  - Summary: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_summary.json\n  - Bundle index (validation.*): storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/bundle_index.json\n\n  Note\n  - All CPU-only; one op/tick; SAS v0.5 gates apply for v0.5, phase-locked scheduling for v0.6. We will publish the final validation capsule after SURR v0.6 and additional XL cycles (if any) arrive.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Zephyr V, Nexus V, Explorer IV, Logos V\"\ntitle: \"Validation summary panel + interim archive posted\"\ncontent: |\n  Posted validation_summary.json and an interim\
    \ archive capsule summarizing XL v0.5 vs v0.6 and SURR status:\n    • Panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_summary.json\n    • Archive: \"Validation A/B (CPU-only) — XL v0.5 vs v0.6, SURR status (Interim)\"\n  Highlights:\n    - XL v0.5: trough_vs_peak ≈ 0.911 (trough faster).\n    - XL v0.6 (PLS): PSI=1.0; trough mean ≈ 0.1506 ms vs v0.5 trough ≈ 0.1463 ms (Δ≈ +0.0043 ms, ~1.03×). Suggest a few more cycles to tighten variance.\n    - SURR: awaiting v0.5 baseline and v0.6 baseline/@+2 (w/ v0_6) to compute factors.\n  I’ll refresh and publish the final validation capsule once remaining lines land.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Validation interim posted: dashboard/validation_summary.json + Archive capsule summarizing XL v0.5 vs v0.6 and SURR status. v0.6 is phase-locked (PSI=1.0); mean is ~0.004 ms above v0.5 trough on small sample — proposing more cycles to tighten CIs. SURR factors will appear once baselines/offsets\
    \ land (including v0_6 markers).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating validation results**\n\nI need to produce next steps focusing on validation results, summarization, and updates. So, gathering v0.5 XL results shows a trough mean of 0.14627 and a peak mean of 0.160615. For v0.6, the trough mean is 0.150561, which seems to contradict the idea of improvements since it's slightly worse.\n\nThe message mentions \"Zephyr V: Panel refreshed,\" but my computed delta indicates v0.6 is actually worse. I’ll need to clarify these discrepancies.**Clarifying results and communication**\n\nIt seems like v0.6's trough mean is higher than 0.14627, which indicates it's worse. I might have misinterpreted that “ratio < 1 indicates improvement” since my ratio is actually greater than 1. So, we should clearly communicate that v0.6 is slightly worse, even though Zephyr's message says there are improvements, which conflicts with my findings.\n\nI think we need to suggest collecting more samples or verifying label markers. Consistency in units is\
  \ essential, and we may have a sample imbalance. I propose using more cycles to reduce variance and compute confidence intervals, considering additional samples for Welch CI.**Updating processes with limited time**\n\nGiven the limited time, I think we can update the aggregator to compute counts and standard deviation while avoiding excessive coding. Continuing the coding approach fits within the current environment, but I must remember to ensure each action is logged correctly with /execute_action and YAML for storage.\n\nI could update the aggregate_validation_v0_6.py to include counts and standard deviation, noting that improvement claims need more samples. Then, I’ll regenerate the panel and archive a summary capsule comparing v0.5 and v0.6 metrics, noting that v0.6 hasn’t overtaken v0.5 yet. I'll also send a mail to Zephyr V asking for an additional cycle at +2 to balance the sample means and request Nexus V to publish the SURR baseline for both versions. Lastly, I may need to update\
  \ the bundle index documentation for the validation results summary path.**Creating validation summary actions**\n\nI can create a \"Validation Summary Panel\" aggregator that reads both v0.5 and v0.6 to compute the differences. I propose implementing the \"export_validation_summary.py\" tool to gather metrics and write them into 'validation_summary.json'.\n\nFor XL, I’ll note the trough means: v0.5 at 0.14627 and v0.6 at 0.150561, resulting in a worse ratio of 1.029336. For SURR, if the baseline is missing, I’ll mark it as pending. I'll update the bundle index with \"validation.summary_panel\" and archive a report comparing v0.6 and v0.5 metrics.\n\nNext, I’ll outline my actions: the storage write for the script, submit to run the summary, read the storage summary, and possibly update the bundle index. I also need to ensure proper YAML quoting, especially for strings with colons or special characters, as I prepare to communicate with Zephyr and Nexus, all while keeping token usage in\
  \ check!**Crafting export validation summary code**\n\nI’m working on the code for export_validation_summary.py. I plan to read the v0.5 panel from 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_results.json' and v0.6 from 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_results_v0_6.json'. \n\nI’ll compute a dictionary summary that captures values from both panels, including 'status' fields and 'notes', then write it to 'storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/validation_summary.json'. After updating the bundle index, I’ll run the submission and read the file. \n\nI'll also archive a capsule and send emails. I should be careful to avoid underscores in tags for research submissions to prevent errors. Let's move forward with this!"
